E["npc:falfindel-waywarder"] = {t="npc",n="Falfindel Waywarder",z="feralas",s="Falfindel Waywarder is a night elf druid stationed at Thalanaar, the outpost guarding the border between Feralas and the Thousand Needles. From this frontier watchpost, he works to heal corrupted lands and safeguard the southern wilderness of Kalimdor. Travelers wandering down from Stonetalon or the Barrens often find him seeking aid to restore balance to the wild.",h="Falfindel Waywarder is a night elf druid stationed at Thalanaar, the outpost guarding the border between...",sec={{t="Watch at the Southern Border",b="Thalanaar marks the gateway where the lush forests of Feralas descend into the towering mesas and dry salt plains of Thousand Needles. Falfindel Waywarder stands watch at this remote outpost, greeting weary travelers who have ventured far across the continent. Surrounded by natural grandeur and lurking dangers, he serves as a point of contact for the night elves seeking to monitor both local threats and broader environmental calamities across Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="Healing the Charred Vale",b="Despite his southern post, Falfindel remains deeply concerned with the devastation far to the north in Stonetalon Mountains. The Charred Vale, ruined by dark sorcery and fiery destruction, stands as a painful scar upon Kalimdor's wilderness. When adventurers deliver aid to Falfindel to assist in its recovery, he calls upon the spirits of the forest. Summoning forth swarms of wisps, he directs them to make haste north to Stonetalon to begin mending the scorched earth.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on the Quilboar and the Wastes",b="In addition to coordinating restoration efforts, Falfindel keeps a close watch on the surrounding region, including the quilboar dens of Razorfen Kraul. By reviewing recovered journals and gathering intelligence on quilboar leadership, Falfindel ensures that the Alliance understands the rising dangers threatening the passes between Feralas and the central deserts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Falfindel Waywarder located?",a="Falfindel is stationed at Thalanaar, the night elf outpost situated on the border between Feralas and Thousand Needles.",al={"falfindel location","where is falfindel","falfindel waywarder map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Falfindel's role at Thalanaar?",a="He serves as a druid and guide at the outpost, monitoring regional threats such as the quilboar of Razorfen Kraul and coordinating restoration efforts for ruined lands like the Charred Vale.",al={"what does falfindel do","falfindel purpose","falfindel quests"},it="purpose"},{q="How does Falfindel help the Charred Vale?",a="When adventurers assist in efforts to reclaim the Charred Vale, Falfindel channels an incantation to summon forest wisps, dispatching them north to Stonetalon to heal the blighted land.",al={"falfindel stonetalon","falfindel charred vale","reclaiming the charred vale falfindel"}},{q="Why is Falfindel interested in Razorfen Kraul?",a="He studies the threat posed by the quilboar of the Kraul and inspects items like Lonebrow's journal to track the influence of their leaders, such as the Crone of the Kraul.",al={"crone of the kraul falfindel","lonebrow journal falfindel","falfindel quilboar"},it="motive"},{q="Is Falfindel aligned with the Alliance or neutral?",a="Falfindel is a night elf druid allied with Darnassus and the Alliance. Horde travelers approaching Thalanaar will find the outpost hostile.",al={"is falfindel alliance","falfindel faction"},it="side"},{q="What does Falfindel say to travelers?",a="He warmly greets friendly visitors by acknowledging their long journey, remarking, 'You look as though you have traveled from afar.'",al={"falfindel gossip","falfindel quote"}},{q="Who is Falfindel Waywarder?",a="Falfindel Waywarder is a night elf stationed at the outpost of Thalanaar, bordering Feralas and the Thousand Needles. Attuned to the health of the land and the perils facing the southern reaches of Kalimdor, he watches over travelers and works closely with fellow night elves to counter emerging threats to the wilderness.",al={"who is falfindel","falfindel waywarder lore","who is falfindel waywarder"},it="identity",add="444437e8"},{q="What does Falfindel Waywarder want?",a="Falfindel seeks to protect the fragile wilderness and aid the healing of devastated lands. He directs allies to summon forest spirits to revitalize the Charred Vale, coordinates deliveries to keep local outposts supplied, and seeks to eliminate the corrupted quilboar crone lurking within Razorfen Kraul.",al={"what does falfindel want","falfindel goals","falfindel quests purpose"},it="wants",add="e0cb4d91"},{q="Why is Falfindel Waywarder here?",a="Falfindel serves as a druid and guide at Thalanaar, guarding the passage between Thousand Needles and Feralas. From this remote outpost, he monitors the rising quilboar threat spilling from the Barrens and coordinates efforts to restore balance to blighted forests across central and southern Kalimdor.",al={"why is falfindel here","why is falfindel at thalanaar","falfindel purpose"},it="why_here",add="2bf92e29"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Falfindel represents your people's vigilance on the frontiers of Kalimdor, striving to mend nature's scars and guard against encroaching wilderness perils.",["class:Druid"]="His efforts to send forest spirits and wisps to heal the scorched soils of Stonetalon reflect the sacred druidic mission of restoration.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers making the long trek south from the Barrens or Stonetalon, Falfindel and the watch at Thalanaar offer a welcoming sanctuary."},kw={"charred vale","falfindel","feralas","stonetalon","thalanaar","thousand needles","waywarder","wisps"},rel={"subzone:thalanaar","quest:1057","quest:1100","quest:1101","zone:feralas","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:charred-vale","topic:night-elf"},src={"Falfindel Waywarder"}}
E["npc:kindal-moonweaver"] = {t="npc",n="Kindal Moonweaver",z="feralas",s="Kindal Moonweaver is a night elf secluded within a concealed nook in the craggy mountains of Feralas, just north of the Grimtotem Compound. Deeply troubled by the mistreatment of wildlife in the wilderness, she watches the aggressive tauren tribe below while seeking help to free captured beasts. She is kin to Jer'kai Moonweaver, sharing a mission to defend the forest's innocent creatures.",h="Kindal Moonweaver is a night elf secluded within a concealed nook in the craggy mountains of Feralas, just...",sec={{t="A Watcher in the Clifftops",b="Perched upon a narrow, winding mountain path partially hidden behind timber east of Dire Maul, Kindal Moonweaver maintains a secret vigil over the valley below. While much of Feralas is contested between the Horde, the night elves of Feathermoon, and the ancient ruins of Eldre'Thalas, Kindal focuses on a more localized and immediate cruelty. Down in the hollow, the Grimtotem tribe operates a fortified compound, capturing and penning up local fauna for reasons far from benign. From her concealed overlook, Kindal watches for anyone willing to brave the enemy camp and undo the suffering inside.",sp=0},{t="Compassion for the Wild",b="Kindal's primary concern lies with the sacred balance and gentle creatures of Feralas that cannot defend themselves against brutish captors. Along with her kin, Jer'kai Moonweaver, she seeks the emancipation of caged beasts and looks out for young animals left stranded by violent poaching. Rather than engaging in grand territorial war, her attention is fixed on compassion: freeing caged sprites and finding a home for an orphaned sprite darter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Kindal Moonweaver located?",a="Kindal hides along the northern cliffs of Feralas, just east of Dire Maul and above the Grimtotem Compound. You can reach her by finding a narrow, hidden mountain path that winds uphill behind a stand of trees.",al={"kindal moonweaver location","how to find kindal","where is kindal"}},{q="Who is Kindal Moonweaver?",a="She is a solitary night elf dedicated to animal welfare and natural preservation in Feralas. She keeps watch over the Grimtotem Compound to disrupt their capturing of local wildlife.",al={"kindal lore","who is kindal"}},{q="What is Kindal's goal in Feralas?",a="Kindal wants to free captive creatures trapped in cages within the nearby Grimtotem Compound and ensure that orphaned wilderness beasts are rescued and provided safe shelter.",al={"kindal quest purpose","why is kindal here"}},{q="Is Kindal Moonweaver related to Jer'kai Moonweaver?",a="Yes, Kindal is kin to Jer'kai Moonweaver. Both share the Moonweaver family name and collaborate in the effort to rescue mistreated and displaced woodland creatures in Feralas.",al={"jerkai moonweaver connection","kindal and jerkai"}},{q="Why is Kindal opposing the Grimtotem?",a="The Grimtotem clan occupying the compound below her mountain perch captures and cages wild beasts of Feralas. Kindal seeks to liberate these creatures from captivity and punish their captors.",al={"kindal grimtotem","grimtotem compound kindal"}},{q="Does Kindal Moonweaver offer quests to both factions?",a="No. Kindal's quests are offered only to the Alliance, whose adventurers she enlists to free the caged creatures from the Grimtotem.",al={"is kindal friendly to horde","can horde talk to kindal"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Kindal embodies the traditional kaldorei devotion to the natural world, standing as an isolated guardian for beasts imperiled by outside invaders.",["class:Druid"]="Druids will find common ground with Kindal's singular dedication to preserving forest life and liberating trapped nature spirits from cruel iron cages.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunters attuned to the beasts of Kalimdor can respect Kindal's efforts to protect wild young and punish those who capture game for sport or malice."},kw={"dire maul","feralas","freedom for all creatures","grimtotem compound","hidden path","jer'kai moonweaver","kindal moonweaver"},rel={"zone:feralas","subzone:grimtotem-compound","subzone:hidden-path","subzone:dire-maul","topic:night-elf"},src={"Kindal Moonweaver"}}
E["npc:lord-shalzaru"] = {t="npc",n="Lord Shalzaru",z="feralas",s="Lord Shalzaru is the tyrannical leader of the Hatecrest naga operating out of the Isle of Dread off the coast of Feralas. Ruling his serpentine followers with absolute cruelty, he oversees extensive excavations among the submerged and ruined elven settlements. His recent discovery of a strange, ancient relic has drawn the attention of outside investigators eager to wrest it from his grasp.",h="Lord Shalzaru is the tyrannical leader of the Hatecrest naga operating out of the Isle of Dread off the coast...",sec={{t="Master of the Hatecrest",b="Lord Shalzaru commands the Hatecrest naga, directing their presence along the southern coast of Feralas. From his subterranean lair within a cavern on the Isle of Dread, he enforces his rule through cruelty and ruthless authority. Under his command, the Hatecrest scour the ancient ruins of ancient Kalimdor, searching for forgotten treasures and powerful relics left behind from the Sundering.",sp=0},{t="The Mysterious Relic",b="During excavations south of the primary ruins across the Isle of Dread, Shalzaru personally uncovered a strange, ancient relic. The purpose and power of this artifact remain a mystery, but its recovery by such a powerful naga warlord presents a clear threat. Operatives on the mainland seek brave champions to venture into the serpent's den, end Shalzaru's command, and secure the odd relic before the Hatecrest can turn it to darker ends.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lord Shalzaru?",a="Lord Shalzaru is the cruel royal leader of the Hatecrest naga. He oversees naga forces and excavations on the Isle of Dread, situated off the coast of Feralas.",al={"lord shalzaru lore","shalzaru","who is shalzaru"}},{q="Where can Lord Shalzaru be found?",a="He lairs in a cave located south of the main elven ruins across the waters on the Isle of Dread, off the southwestern coast of Feralas.",al={"shalzaru location","where is lord shalzaru","isle of dread cave"}},{q="What is the Hatecrest?",a="The Hatecrest are a hostile tribe of naga occupying the coastline and islands of Feralas, known for scouring ancient ruins and terrorizing the coastal waters under Shalzaru's command.",al={"hatecrest naga","hatecrest tribe"}},{q="What relic does Lord Shalzaru possess?",a="During a recent excavation on the Isle of Dread, Shalzaru uncovered a mysterious, ancient relic of unknown origin and power, prompting mainland factions to dispatch adventurers to claim it.",al={"shalzaru relic","mysterious relic feralas"}},{q="Why must Lord Shalzaru be defeated?",a="Eliminating Shalzaru breaks the Hatecrest leadership on the Isle of Dread and allows adventurers to recover the mysterious relic he recently excavated before the naga can harness it.",al={"against lord shalzaru","kill lord shalzaru"}},{q="What are the Hatecrest digging for in Feralas?",a="The Hatecrest excavate the ruined Night Elf settlements shattered during the Great Sundering, seeking powerful magical relics and remnants of Highborne history hidden beneath the soil and waves.",al={"hatecrest excavation","why are naga in feralas"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Hatecrest naga violate the ancient ruins of ancient Kalimdor; reclaiming relics from Shalzaru prevents the Highborne's dark legacy from empowering his serpentine kin.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing Shalzaru's relic and neutralizing the Hatecrest warlord helps safeguard the remote Alliance outposts on the untamed coast of Feralas.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde scouts keep a watchful eye on coastal threats in Feralas, and striking down the naga lord removes an unpredictable danger near Camp Mojache's sphere of interest."},kw={"feralas","hatecrest","isle of dread","lord shalzaru","mysterious relic","naga","shalzaru"},rel={"subzone:isle-of-dread","zone:feralas","topic:naga"},src={"Lord Shalzaru"}}
E["npc:shandris-feathermoon"] = {t="npc",n="Shandris Feathermoon",z="feralas",s="Shandris Feathermoon is the General of the Sentinel Army and, for ten thousand years, Tyrande Whisperwind's right hand. She now commands night elf military forces throughout Kalimdor from Feathermoon Stronghold on Sardor Isle off the coast of Feralas.",h="Shandris Feathermoon is the General of the Sentinel Army and, for ten thousand years, Tyrande Whisperwind's...",sec={{t="Tyrande's Right Hand",b="Shandris Feathermoon is one of the oldest defenders of the night elves. For ten thousand years she has served at Tyrande Whisperwind's side as the high priestess's right hand among the Sentinels, through the long vigil that followed the Sundering.",sp=0},{t="Rise of the Sentinels",b="Following the Great Sundering and the founding of the Sentinels, Shandris became an indispensable commander within the night elf military.",sp=0},{t="The Bastion of Feralas",b="Today, General Feathermoon serves as the supreme field commander of the Sentinel army. Stationed on Sardor Isle, she oversees Feathermoon Stronghold, an imposing elven fortress that keeps watch over the primal wilds of Feralas. From this island outpost, she monitors the encroaching threats of savage gnolls, lingering Gordunni ogres, hate-fueled satyrs, and the expanding power of the Horde in southern Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Shandris Feathermoon?",a="Shandris Feathermoon is the General of the Sentinels, the standing military force of the night elves. An ancient night elf, she has served as High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind's right hand for ten thousand years and commands the Sentinels from Feathermoon Stronghold in Feralas.",al={"who is shandris","shandris lore","who is the night elf general in feralas"}},{q="Where can Shandris Feathermoon be found?",a="She commands from Feathermoon Stronghold, situated on Sardor Isle off the western coast of Feralas in southern Kalimdor.",al={"shandris location","where is shandris feathermoon","feathermoon stronghold leader"}},{q="What is Shandris's relationship to Tyrande Whisperwind?",a="Shandris has been Tyrande Whisperwind's right hand in the Sentinels for ten thousand years. Tyrande leads the night elves from Darnassus, while Shandris commands the Sentinel army in the field from Feathermoon Stronghold.",al={"is shandris tyrande daughter","tyrande and shandris","tyrande adopted child"}},{q="Did Shandris fight against the Burning Legion?",a="No battle of hers against the Legion is recorded in the histories told here. What is known is that she has served at Tyrande Whisperwind's side among the Sentinels for ten thousand years and now commands the Sentinel army from Feathermoon Stronghold.",al={"war of the ancients shandris","did shandris fight archimonde"}},{q="Why is she stationed in Feralas instead of Teldrassil?",a="As General of the Sentinels, Shandris must direct frontline military operations across Kalimdor. Feathermoon Stronghold serves as the Alliance's primary staging ground and bulwark in the wild southern forests, keeping watch on hostile ogres, satyrs, and Horde activity.",al={"why is shandris in feralas","why feathermoon stronghold"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="To the Kaldorei, General Feathermoon represents the pinnacle of Sentinel discipline and duty, having guarded the people since the dawn of the long vigil.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunters and rangers revere Shandris as one of the finest marksmen of the Sentinels, a general who has stood watch over the night elves for ten thousand years.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance forces venturing into southern Kalimdor, General Feathermoon provides essential naval presence, strategic leadership, and a heavily fortified sanctuary on Sardor Isle.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde views General Feathermoon as a dangerous and cunning military tactician whose fortress off the Feralas coast threatens their expansion in the region."},kw={"feathermoon","feralas","general","kaldorei","sardor isle","sentinels","shandris","tyrande"},rel={"subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","npc:tyrande-whisperwind","zone:feralas","topic:sentinels","quest:1043"},src={"Shandris Feathermoon"}}
E["npc:sprite-darter"] = {t="npc",n="Sprite Darter",z="feralas",s="Sprite Darters are small, iridescent faerie dragons native to the lush canopy of Feralas. Revered for their innate spiritual and magical qualities, they flit gracefully among the ancient trees. Recently, these rare creatures have become targets for local Grimtotem tauren who seek to capture and exploit them.",h="Sprite Darters are small, iridescent faerie dragons native to the lush canopy of Feralas.",sec={{t="Faerie Dragons of the Wild",b="Sprite Darters are elusive, winged woodland beasts native to the ancient forests of Feralas. Characterized by their gleaming, iridescent wings and mysterious spiritual essence, they embody the whimsical yet fierce magical ecology of Kalimdor's deep forests. Though generally peaceful and shy, their innate resistance to magical forces and natural power make them significant to those attuned to the wilderness.",sp=0},{t="Grimtotem Captivity",b="In recent times, the reclusive Sprite Darters have faced an unprecedented threat. The aggressive Grimtotem tauren clan inhabiting Feralas has begun rounding up and caging large numbers of these rare creatures for enigmatic purposes. Concerned night elves like Kindal Moonweaver actively recruit allies to disrupt the cages and liberate the trapped hatchlings before the Grimtotem bend them to their will.",sp=0},{t="Spiritual Interest",b="Beyond night elf efforts to safeguard them, the darters have caught the eye of outside observers studying primal power. Witch Doctor Uzer'i, a troll spiritualist operating out of Camp Mojache, takes a keen interest in the natural energies and muisek contained within the Sprite Darters, seeking their essence to unravel the unique magic thriving throughout Feralas.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Sprite Darters?",a="Sprite Darters are miniature faerie dragons found inhabiting the wilderness of Feralas. They are known for their shimmering wings, connection to nature, and elusive magical behavior.",al={"sprite darter info","what is a sprite darter","are sprite darters dragons"}},{q="Why are the Grimtotem tauren capturing them?",a="The exact reasons remain shrouded, but the Grimtotem clan has been netting and caging sprite darters in large numbers throughout the woods, likely seeking to exploit their rare spiritual and magical qualities.",al={"why grimtotem cages","grimtotem sprite darters","why are darters caged"}},{q="Who is trying to protect the Sprite Darters?",a="Kindal Moonweaver, an elf residing in Feralas, actively works to protect them by sending sympathetic adventurers to smash the Grimtotem cages and rescue captive darters.",al={"who protects sprite darters","kindal moonweaver sprite darters","alliance sprite darter quest"}},{q="Why is Witch Doctor Uzer'i interested in Sprite Darters?",a="Witch Doctor Uzer'i studies the primal spiritual forces of Feralas. He seeks the essence, or muisek, of the Sprite Darters to learn more about the intrinsic magical wildlife of the region.",al={"witch doctor uzeri sprite darter","uzeri darter quest"}},{q="Can you raise a Sprite Darter?",a="Those who aid Kindal Moonweaver in freeing the captive hatchlings and defending their nests may eventually be entrusted with a rare Sprite Darter Egg to rear and protect.",al={"sprite darter egg","sprite darter pet","can i get a sprite darter"},sp=1},{q="Are Sprite Darters hostile?",a="Wild sprite darters are generally skittish and passive toward travelers, but like all wild creatures, they will defend themselves using bursts of nature magic if threatened or provoked.",al={"are sprite darters dangerous","do sprite darters attack"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Night elves revere the sacred faerie dragons as natural wardens of the forest, making the liberation of captured Sprite Darters from the Grimtotem a matter of ecological stewardship.",["faction:Alliance"]="Allies of Kindal Moonweaver rally to the aid of the captive hatchlings in Feralas, thwarting the encroaching reach of the hostile Grimtotem tribe.",["faction:Horde"]="Troll spiritualists like Witch Doctor Uzer'i from Camp Mojache view Sprite Darters as prime subjects for harvesting spiritual muisek and harnessing the ancient essence of Feralas.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold faerie dragons in high regard as cousins of nature spirits, finding their capture by crude poachers deeply disruptive to the forest balance."},kw={"darter egg","faerie dragon","feralas","grimtotem","kindal moonweaver","muisek","sprite darter","witch doctor uzer'i"},rel={"zone:feralas","npc:kindal-moonweaver","npc:witch-doctor-uzer-i","topic:tauren","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Sprite Darter"}}
E["npc:witch-doctor-uzer-i"] = {t="npc",n="Witch Doctor Uzer'i",z="feralas",s="Witch Doctor Uzer'i is a jungle troll mystic residing at Camp Mojache in the primordial forests of Feralas. Dedicated to advancing the magical capabilities of the Horde, he researches techniques to trap and harness the muisek—the spiritual essence of powerful natural creatures. By capturing these ancient forest spirits, Uzer'i seeks to channel the raw primal energies traditionally favored by night elves directly into enchanted weapons.",h="Witch Doctor Uzer'i is a jungle troll mystic residing at Camp Mojache in the primordial forests of Feralas.",sec={{t="Harnessing the Muisek",b="Rooted in traditional troll spiritualism, Witch Doctor Uzer'i has spent considerable effort studying the natural magic inherent to the untamed wilderness of Feralas. He argues that night elves have drawn upon the spirits of forest beasts for millennia, and believes the time has come for the Horde to seize those same primal forces. Central to his study is the concept of muisek: the vibrant spiritual essence that remains within a creature. To harness it, Uzer'i crafts specialized vessels capable of rapidly shrinking fallen beings before their escaping spirit disperses, allowing the essence to be stored and studied.",sp=0},{t="Grisly Bargains and Ritual Vessels",b="Perfecting the containment vessels required dark and potent reagents that Uzer'i could not procure in the wilds alone. After slaying an Alliance dwarf wandering the Feralas timber, Uzer'i severed the intruder's head and arranged for it to be traded to Neeru Fireblade, a warlock dwelling in Orgrimmar's shadowy Cleft of Shadow. In return for the grisly prize, Neeru provided rare herbs necessary to finalize the binding enchantments. With these components, Uzer'i successfully completed his first vessels, opening the way to capture the spirits of regional wildkin, hippogryphs, faerie dragons, treants, and mountain giants.",sp=1},{t="Forging Weapons of Spirit",b="Extracting muisek was merely the first phase of Uzer'i's broader ambition. Gathering resilient sinew, enchanted minerals, and petrified splintered logs from the very creatures whose spirits he trapped, the witch doctor fused physical materials with bound muisek. Through these rites, he learned to permanently bind ancient forest spirits into arms and armaments, providing the Horde with magically charged weapons. Beyond his ritual craftsmanship, Uzer'i maintains a deep curiosity regarding hidden places of power throughout Azeroth, actively tracking rumors of the ancient, submerged Sunken Temple.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is muisek?",a="Muisek is the lingering spiritual essence of living creatures. Witch Doctor Uzer'i uses specially enchanted vessels to shrink the bodies of slain beasts and natural guardians, trapping their escaping spirits before they dissolve into the surrounding environment.",al={"what is muisek","muisek meaning","define muisek"}},{q="Why is Uzer'i trading dwarf heads to Orgrimmar?",a="Uzer'i needed specialized reagents to prepare his ritual vessels. After killing an Alliance dwarf in Feralas, he had the severed head delivered to Neeru Fireblade in Orgrimmar in exchange for rare herbs required to bind the muisek spirits.",al={"dwarf head quest","why send head to neeru","neeru fireblade trade"}},{q="What kind of creatures does Uzer'i target?",a="He targets creatures intrinsically tied to the natural world and long allied with the night elves, including wildkin from the Hinterlands, as well as hippogryphs, faerie dragons, treants, and mountain giants in Feralas.",al={"what beasts does uzeri hunt","uzeri spirit targets","which animals for muisek"}},{q="What does Uzer'i do with the captured spirits?",a="Once gathered alongside raw natural components like splintered logs, sinew, and minerals, Uzer'i permanently binds the muisek into weaponry, imbuing mundane arms with the raw mystical power of ancient forest guardians.",al={"weapons of spirit","why collect muisek","muisek weapon rewards"}},{q="Where is Witch Doctor Uzer'i located?",a="Witch Doctor Uzer'i resides within Camp Mojache, the primary Horde settlement situated in the lush, dangerous canopy of central Feralas.",al={"uzeri location","where is uzeri","witch doctor uzeri spot"}},{q="What does Uzer'i know about the Sunken Temple?",a="As a scholar of spirits and mystical sites across Azeroth, Uzer'i has caught wind of the submerged Atal'ai sanctuary known as the Sunken Temple, and directs interested adventurers to the goblin explorer Marvon Rivetseeker to investigate further.",al={"uzeri sunken temple","sunken temple feralas quest","temple of atal hakkar uzeri"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Uzer'i provides the Horde with an avenue to master the primal magic of Kalimdor's wilderness, turning the land's spiritual power against Alliance allies like the night elves.",["race:Troll"]="Uzer'i represents classic troll spiritual practices, employing traditional witch doctor rituals, shrunken vessels, and voodoo to harness raw life essences.",["class:Shaman"]="Shaman will recognize Uzer'i's relentless focus on communion with spirits, though his aggressive containment of elemental and wild essences leans toward forceful witchery rather than reverent balance.",["race:NightElf"]="Night elves view Uzer'i's practices as a blasphemy, watching in horror as sacred creatures like treants, hippogryphs, and mountain giants are slaughtered and bound into weapons."},kw={"camp mojache","faerie dragon","feralas","mountain giant","muisek","neeru fireblade","treant","uzer'i","witch doctor"},rel={"subzone:camp-mojache","zone:feralas","quest:829","topic:troll","topic:horde","subzone:high-wilderness","zone:hinterlands","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Witch Doctor Uzer'i"}}
E["quest:2766"] = {t="quest",n="Find OOX-22/FE!",z="feralas",s="You come across a strange egg-shaped device of metal. A voice inside it introduces itself as Oglethorpe Obnoticus, whose homing robot has crashed. You are asked to bring the beacon to the machine, which lies in a cave close to Feral Scar Vale.",h="You come across a strange egg-shaped device of metal.",sec={{t="A Voice in the Egg",b="Fiddling with a knob springs the metal egg open into a gnomish robotic contraption, and a crackling voice speaks from within. Oglethorpe Obnoticus says the homing robot has crashed, and promises payment if you recover it. The beacon is to be taken to the robot, and Oglethorpe has computed where it lies: a cave near Feral Scar Vale.",sp=0},{t="What the Cave Holds",b="In the cave you find wreckage that looks like a robotic chicken. Oglethorpe's voice confirms it is his homing robot, and says it must be jump-started before flying to Booty Bay for repairs. Placing the beacon inside brings the robot whirring to life, and Oglethorpe's voice then comes from the robot itself.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is speaking through the distress beacon?",a="Oglethorpe Obnoticus. His homing robot has crashed, and he asks you to bring the beacon to it.",al={"who made the beacon","who is talking","oglethorpe who"}},{q="Where does the beacon point you to go?",a="Oglethorpe has computed the robot's coordinates, and it lies in a cave by Feral Scar Vale in Feralas.",al={"where is the robot","homing robot location","where to take beacon"}},{q="What is the beacon?",a="A strange egg-shaped device of metal. When you fiddle with a knob it opens into a gnomish robotic contraption, and a voice speaks from inside.",al={"what is the egg","what is oox-22/fe","distress beacon"}},{q="What comes after this step?",a="Rescue OOX-22/FE! follows.",al={"next quest","what follows find oox-22/fe","after the cave"}}},kw={"distress beacon","feral scar vale","feralas","homing robot","mechanical chicken","oglethorpe obnoticus","oox-22/fe"},rel={"quest:2767","subzone:feral-scar-vale","zone:feralas","subzone:booty-bay"},m={start="OOX-22/FE Distress Beacon",["end"]="Feral Scar Vale",level="45",faction="Neutral",id=2766},src={"Find OOX-22/FE!"}}
E["quest:2767"] = {t="quest",n="Rescue OOX-22/FE!",z="feralas",s="After finding the homing robot OOX-22/FE in Feral Scar Vale, you hear the gnome's voice crackle from it once more. The robot is to be escorted to the Forgotten Coast dock, and afterwards Oglethorpe Obnoticus wants a word with you in Booty Bay.",h="After finding the homing robot OOX-22/FE in Feral Scar Vale, you hear the gnome's voice crackle from it once...",sec={{t="A Safe Place to Take Off",b="The gnome's voice says OOX-22/FE needs somewhere open and safe where a lengthy take-off can begin. The robot has built-in cloaking, but Oglethorpe Obnoticus needs time to make it work again. Oglethorpe suggests the Forgotten Coast dock, long enough for getting everything running, so the robot is to be walked there from where it stands.",sp=0},{t="Afterwards, Booty Bay",b="Once the robot is safely at the dock, Oglethorpe Obnoticus wants you to come and talk in Booty Bay.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does OOX-22/FE need to go?",a="The dock along the Forgotten Coast. It is escorted there from Feral Scar Vale, where you found it.",al={"where do i take the chicken","oox-22/fe destination","feralas chicken escort path"}},{q="Who is Oglethorpe Obnoticus?",a="A master inventor whose homing robot series includes OOX-22/FE. Oglethorpe speaks through the robot and is found in Booty Bay.",al={"who made the robot chicken","who is oglethorpe obnoticus","chicken inventor"}},{q="Why does the robot need to reach the dock?",a="A lengthy take-off needs an open, safe place, and Oglethorpe says the dock is long enough to get things online. The robot's built-in cloaking needs time before it works again.",al={"why escort oox-22","why walk to the dock"}},{q="Where do I report afterwards?",a="Once the robot is safely at the dock, speak to Oglethorpe Obnoticus in Booty Bay.",al={"where is oglethorpe","turn in location","who do i talk to after"}}},kw={"booty bay","feral scar vale","feralas","forgotten coast","homing robot","oglethorpe obnoticus","oox-22/fe","robot chicken"},rel={"quest:2766","subzone:feral-scar-vale","subzone:forgotten-coast","subzone:booty-bay","zone:feralas"},m={start="Homing Robot OOX-22/FE, Feral Scar Vale",["end"]="Oglethorpe Obnoticus, Booty Bay",level="45",id=2767},src={"Rescue OOX-22/FE!"}}
E["quest:2821"] = {t="quest",n="The Mark of Quality",z="feralas",s="At Feathermoon Stronghold, the leatherworker Pratt McGrubben will not compromise on quality. Pratt has come across thick yeti hides and wants a stack of ten.",h="At Feathermoon Stronghold, the leatherworker Pratt McGrubben will not compromise on quality.",sec={{t="Pratt's Philosophy",b="Pratt McGrubben will not compromise on leatherwork: only the finest will do. While hunting for fine materials, Pratt came across thick yeti hides. The yetis are native to Feralas, with many around Feral Scar Vale, just inland of the Forgotten Coast.",sp=0},{t="The Offer",b="For a stack of ten hides, Pratt will let you choose one of the leather goods Pratt has crafted. Bring them back to Feathermoon Stronghold.",sp=0},{t="Pratt's Thoughts on the Hides",b="Pratt asks whether you stopped to feel the texture of the hides. Properly treated, they could prove tougher than iron, and few people know of them. With a wide knowledge of treating solutions, Pratt hopes to make pieces that carry a true mark of quality.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the hides?",a="Pratt McGrubben, a leatherworker at Feathermoon Stronghold.",al={"quest giver","pratt mcgrubben","who gives the mark of quality"}},{q="Where can the yetis be found?",a="Yetis are native to Feralas, and many are found around Feral Scar Vale, just inland of the Forgotten Coast.",al={"yeti location","where are yetis","feral scar vale"}},{q="How many hides does Pratt want?",a="Ten of them, as one stack.",al={"how many yeti hides","hide count"}},{q="What do I get for the hides?",a="Pratt offers a choice among the leather goods Pratt has crafted, in exchange for the stack.",al={"what does pratt give","mark of quality payment"}}},kw={"feathermoon stronghold","feral scar vale","feralas","forgotten coast","pratt mcgrubben","the mark of quality","thick yeti hide","yetis"},rel={"subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","subzone:feral-scar-vale","zone:feralas","subzone:forgotten-coast"},m={start="Pratt McGrubben",["end"]="Pratt McGrubben",level="46",faction="Alliance",id=2821},src={"The Mark of Quality (Classic Alliance)"}}
E["quest:2822"] = {t="quest",n="The Mark of Quality",z="feralas",s="In Camp Mojache, the leatherworker Jangdor Swiftstrider holds that quality should never be compromised. Jangdor has found thick yeti hides and wants a stack of ten.",h="In Camp Mojache, the leatherworker Jangdor Swiftstrider holds that quality should never be compromised.",sec={{t="A Matter of Pride",b="Jangdor Swiftstrider takes pride in leatherwork and says quality should never be compromised. Lately Jangdor has discovered thick yeti hides. Feralas is home to the yetis, and they are often found west of Camp Mojache in Feral Scar Vale, just inland of the Forgotten Coast.",sp=0},{t="The Offer",b="For a stack of ten hides, Jangdor will let you choose one of the leather goods Jangdor has made. Bring them back to Camp Mojache.",sp=0},{t="Jangdor's Thoughts on the Hides",b="Jangdor declares that, given a special treatment, the hides hold up as well as iron. Finding the right tanning mix will take many attempts, yet Jangdor is sure the hides will raise the mark of quality higher than before.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the hides?",a="Jangdor Swiftstrider, a leatherworker at Camp Mojache in Feralas.",al={"who gives the quest","quest giver mark of quality","where is jangdor"}},{q="Where can the yetis be found?",a="Yetis are native to Feralas. Many are found to the west of Camp Mojache in Feral Scar Vale, just inland of the Forgotten Coast.",al={"where are the yetis","yeti hide location","where is feral scar vale"}},{q="How many hides are required?",a="Ten of them, as one stack.",al={"how many yeti hides","yeti hide count","mark of quality requirement"}},{q="What do I get for the hides?",a="Jangdor offers a choice among the leather goods Jangdor has made, in exchange for the stack.",al={"what does jangdor give","mark of quality payment"}}},kw={"camp mojache","feral scar vale","feralas","forgotten coast","jangdor swiftstrider","leatherworking","thick yeti hide","yeti"},rel={"subzone:camp-mojache","subzone:feral-scar-vale","subzone:forgotten-coast","zone:feralas"},m={start="Jangdor Swiftstrider",["end"]="Jangdor Swiftstrider",level="46",faction="Horde",id=2822},src={"The Mark of Quality (Classic Horde)"}}
E["quest:2844"] = {t="quest",n="The Giant Guardian",z="feralas",s="Rockbiter, a giant, was supposed to be watching over his little friend Shay, a night elf girl, but somehow she got away. Worried and unsure what to do, he asks you to go and look for her.",h="Rockbiter, a giant, was supposed to be watching over his little friend Shay, a night elf girl, but somehow...",sec={{t="Gone While His Back Was Turned",b="Rockbiter was supposed to look after Shay. The last time he saw her, the two of them were walking through the ruins just north of where he stands. All was well until he turned around and found her gone. He cannot work out what to do, but he knows your legs travel much faster than his, so he asks you to search for her.",sp=0},{t="When You Find Her",b="Shay is glad to be found. She admits she is a bit lost, yet cannot help remarking on what a beautiful place this is.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Rockbiter looking for?",a="A little night elf girl named Shay, his friend, whom he was supposed to be watching over.",al={"who is shay","who is the missing girl","who got lost"}},{q="Where was Shay last seen?",a="Rockbiter says they were walking through the ruins just north of where he is when she disappeared.",al={"where did shay go","last seen location","where are the ruins"}},{q="Why does Rockbiter ask someone else to search?",a="He is worried and unsure what to do, and he figures your legs can travel much faster than his.",al={"why cant rockbiter search","why send an adventurer"}}},kw={"feralas","giant guardian","lost girl","rockbiter","ruins","shay","shay leafrunner"},rel={"quest:2845","zone:feralas"},m={start="Rockbiter",["end"]="Shay Leafrunner",level="49",faction="Alliance",id=2844},src={"The Giant Guardian"}}
E["quest:2845"] = {t="quest",n="Wandering Shay",z="feralas",s="Shay Leafrunner, once found, asks you to help her get back to her friend Rockbiter. She admits she wanders off whenever there is something to see, but she has a bell whose sound brings her running back.",h="Shay Leafrunner, once found, asks you to help her get back to her friend Rockbiter.",sec={{t="A Girl Easily Distracted",b="Shay wants to find her way back to Rockbiter, who was supposed to be watching her. She admits she tends to wander off now and then, since there are so many things to see and she gets distracted.",sp=0},{t="The Bell in the Chest",b="Shay says one thing always gets her attention. In a chest beside her lies a bell she treasures, and she loves its sound. She gives her word that if she wanders off, ringing it will bring her running back. The bell is yours to carry, and Rockbiter's camp is where she hopes to be taken.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Shay Leafrunner trying to get back to?",a="Her friend Rockbiter, who was meant to be watching her. You are to take her to his camp.",al={"who is rockbiter","shay friend","where does shay go"}},{q="Why does Shay wander off?",a="She says there are so many things to see that she gets distracted.",al={"why is shay lost","how did shay get lost","why did shay wander off"}},{q="How do I keep Shay from straying?",a="Shay's bell sits in a chest by her. She loves its sound and promises that if she wanders off, ringing it will bring her running back.",al={"how to control shay","shay bell","what does the bell do"}},{q="What comes before this?",a="It follows The Giant Guardian, in which Rockbiter sends you to look for Shay.",al={"previous quest","giant guardian","what leads to wandering shay"}}},kw={"escort","feralas","giant guardian","rockbiter","shay leafrunner","shay's bell"},rel={"quest:2844","zone:feralas"},m={start="Shay Leafrunner",["end"]="Rockbiter",level="49",faction="Alliance",id=2845},src={"Wandering Shay"}}
E["quest:2862"] = {t="quest",n="War on the Woodpaw",z="feralas",s="At Camp Mojache, Hadoken Swiftstrider calls the gnolls a lasting danger to the camp itself, with attacks growing more fevered of late. Hadoken asks you for ten Woodpaw Gnoll Manes to thin their numbers.",h="At Camp Mojache, Hadoken Swiftstrider calls the gnolls a lasting danger to the camp itself, with attacks...",sec={{t="A Threat to the Camp",b="To Hadoken, it makes no difference whether the gnolls belong in Feralas. If the camp does not harden its resolve, he warns, it will be pushed out of the whole region. With the attacks on the camp growing more fevered, he wants their numbers thinned and offers generous pay for ten Woodpaw gnoll manes.",sp=0},{t="Hadoken's Response",b="Hadoken calls the manes a good start. He has put the same ask to others; many have fought the gnolls before, and past efforts held them back. Lately the gnolls have pushed north into the area the camp holds sway over far more often, and their attacks have turned savage, almost desperate. Hadoken says he has a plan that might settle the matter.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who offers this bounty in Feralas?",a="Hadoken Swiftstrider at Camp Mojache.",al={"who gives war on the woodpaw","where to turn in war on the woodpaw","quest giver war on the woodpaw"}},{q="Why is Camp Mojache targeting the Woodpaw gnolls?",a="Hadoken regards them as a constant danger to the camp, with attacks growing more fevered, and fears the camp will be driven out of the whole region unless it stands firm.",al={"why fight woodpaw","woodpaw problem","why are gnolls attacking"}},{q="What proof does Hadoken Swiftstrider require?",a="Ten Woodpaw Gnoll Manes.",al={"what items needed war on the woodpaw","woodpaw quest items","what do i bring hadoken"}}},kw={"alpha strike","camp mojache","feralas","gnolls","hadoken swiftstrider","manes","woodpaw"},rel={"subzone:camp-mojache","zone:feralas","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Hadoken Swiftstrider",["end"]="Hadoken Swiftstrider",level="42",id=2862},src={"Classic quest text: War on the Woodpaw"}}
E["quest:2863"] = {t="quest",n="Alpha Strike",z="feralas",s="Hadoken Swiftstrider has a plan to break the impasse with the Woodpaw gnolls: strike down several of their leaders, who call themselves Alphas, in quick succession. Hadoken wants you to be the one to carry it out.",h="Hadoken Swiftstrider has a plan to break the impasse with the Woodpaw gnolls: strike down several of their...",sec={{t="Five Alphas in an Hour",b="Hadoken reasons that if the gnoll leaders, who call themselves Alphas, fall one after another, their ranks will be thrown into chaos. It might also send the message that the Horde can and will destroy them. You are to carry out Hadoken's will: five Alphas down inside a single hour, or the stalemate stays.",sp=0},{t="Afterwards",b="Thinned ranks and slain leaders, Hadoken expects, will make the gnolls hesitate before storming the camp. Yet the trouble is not over. Hadoken wants to learn what has driven the gnolls into such a frenzy, and to do so ahead of their regrouping.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Hadoken Swiftstrider, who is dealing with the stalemate against the Woodpaw gnolls for the Horde.",al={"who gives alpha strike","hadoken swiftstrider","quest giver"}},{q="Why the one-hour limit?",a="The plan only works if the Alphas fall in swift succession, since that is what should throw the gnoll ranks into chaos. Five must fall within an hour.",al={"why one hour","why rapid succession","alpha strike timer"}},{q="What are the Alphas?",a="They are leaders among the Woodpaw gnolls, who call themselves Alphas.",al={"woodpaw alphas","gnoll alphas","who are the targets"}},{q="How many Alphas must I kill?",a="Five, all within one hour, before returning to Hadoken Swiftstrider.",al={"how many alphas","alpha count"}}},kw={"alpha strike","feralas","gnolls","hadoken swiftstrider","woodpaw","woodpaw alpha"},rel={"zone:feralas","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Hadoken Swiftstrider",["end"]="Hadoken Swiftstrider",level="43",faction="Horde",id=2863},src={"Alpha Strike (Classic)"}}
E["quest:2866"] = {t="quest",n="The Ruins of Solarsal",z="feralas",s="Shandris Feathermoon tells you that the Ruins of Solarsal, to the south, are now crowded with Hatecrest naga. You are sent to walk through the ruins and notice whatever seems out of the ordinary.",h="Shandris Feathermoon tells you that the Ruins of Solarsal, to the south, are now crowded with Hatecrest naga.",sec={{t="Naga in the Old Stones",b="The Ruins of Solarsal far pre-date modern times. Shandris says they explored the place at first, found nothing of note and left it alone. Very recently, though, Hatecrest naga have taken it over in alarming numbers. At first that looked like the prelude to an attack, a threat that is still possible, but Shandris believes something else may be going on. You are to walk through the ruins and notice whatever seems out of the ordinary.",sp=0},{t="What Stands Out",b="Looking over the gazebo, you find it stands apart from the stonework around it. It is plainly a newer construction. Small glyphs run along its sides in a repeating pattern, and nobody knows where they come from or what they mean. The stone itself is warm to the touch.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where are the Ruins of Solarsal?",a="They lie to the south of Shandris Feathermoon.",al={"ruins of solarsal location","where is solarsal","where to find solarsal"}},{q="Why is Shandris Feathermoon concerned about the ruins?",a="Hatecrest naga have lately occupied the ruins in alarming numbers. At first this looked like preparation for an attack, and that is still possible, but Shandris believes something else may be going on.",al={"why send me to solarsal","shandris feathermoon solarsal reason","why investigate solarsal"}},{q="What were the Ruins of Solarsal before the naga arrived?",a="The ruins far pre-date modern times. Shandris says they were explored at first, nothing of note turned up, and they were left in peace.",al={"solarsal history","what is solarsal"}},{q="Which naga are in the ruins?",a="The Hatecrest naga.",al={"who is at solarsal","solarsal enemies","naga tribe in solarsal"}}},kw={"feathermoon stronghold","feralas","gazebo","glyphs","hatecrest","naga","shandris feathermoon","solarsal"},rel={"npc:shandris-feathermoon","quest:2867","topic:naga","zone:feralas"},m={start="Shandris Feathermoon",["end"]="Solarsal Gazebo",level="43",faction="Alliance",id=2866},src={"The Ruins of Solarsal"}}
E["quest:2867"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Feathermoon Stronghold",z="feralas",s="Your search turned up a strange gazebo at the center of the Ruins of Solarsal. Now it is time to head back to Feathermoon Stronghold and tell General Shandris Feathermoon about it.",h="Your search turned up a strange gazebo at the center of the Ruins of Solarsal.",sec={{t="Carrying the Report Home",b="General Shandris Feathermoon waits at Feathermoon Stronghold to hear about the strange gazebo you discovered in the heart of the ruins. Make your way back to the stronghold with your findings.",sp=0},{t="On Your Return",b="Shandris calls your report on the gazebo disturbing. Even if the naga never meant to attack, that they stay on is a bad sign for the push into Feralas. The stronghold is in dire need of more help against the Hatecrest naga, and Shandris offers you more to do, if you are willing.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who do I report to after the ruins?",a="General Shandris Feathermoon, at Feathermoon Stronghold.",al={"who do i turn this in to","who wants the report","where to turn in return to feathermoon stronghold"}},{q="What should I report?",a="That strange gazebo, standing at the center of the Ruins of Solarsal.",al={"what do i tell shandris","what was found at solarsal"}},{q="What comes before this?",a="It follows The Ruins of Solarsal, where Shandris sent you to explore the ruins and look into the naga there.",al={"previous quest","what leads here"}}},kw={"feathermoon stronghold","feralas","hatecrest","naga","ruins of solarsal","shandris feathermoon","solarsal gazebo"},rel={"quest:2866","npc:shandris-feathermoon","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","zone:feralas","topic:naga"},m={start="Solarsal Gazebo",["end"]="Shandris Feathermoon",level="43",faction="Alliance",id=2867},src={"Return to Feathermoon Stronghold"}}
E["quest:2869"] = {t="quest",n="Against the Hatecrest",z="feralas",s="Latronicus Moonspear at Feathermoon Stronghold wants to meet the Hatecrest naga head-on rather than wait for them. He asks you for ten Hatecrest Scales in good condition.",h="Latronicus Moonspear at Feathermoon Stronghold wants to meet the Hatecrest naga head-on rather than wait for...",sec={{t="Acting Before It Is Too Late",b="Whatever the naga are up to, Latronicus Moonspear assumes they will eventually try to claim the island for themselves, and aggressive steps are needed before it is too late. He wants ten Hatecrest Scales in good condition, and expects you to see for yourself how to get them. He counts on it weakening the naga presence on Sardor Isle and on it being your first time cutting your teeth on the naga.",sp=0},{t="Peace and Duty",b="Latronicus is clear that night elves are not warmongers and are devoted to peace and harmony. That does not mean they will leave their own interests unguarded, he says, and guarding them is his duty to General Feathermoon and the stronghold.",sp=0},{t="Afterwards",b="Latronicus pronounces the scales more than satisfactory and means to send them down to Pratt, in case something useful can be crafted from them. He has something else for you to do as well.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest and where?",a="Latronicus Moonspear, at Feathermoon Stronghold, both asks for the scales and receives them.",al={"who starts against the hatecrest","latronicus moonspear location","where to turn in against the hatecrest"}},{q="Why does Latronicus Moonspear want Hatecrest scales?",a="He assumes the naga will eventually move to secure Sardor Isle, and wants aggressive steps taken first. Gathering scales means weakening them there.",al={"why kill hatecrest","hatecrest scale purpose","why collect naga scales"}},{q="How many scales are needed?",a="Ten Hatecrest Scales, in good condition.",al={"how many scales","scale count"}},{q="Where are the Hatecrest naga found?",a="Latronicus speaks of a naga presence on Sardor Isle.",al={"hatecrest location","where to find hatecrest","sardor isle naga"}}},kw={"against the hatecrest","feathermoon stronghold","feralas","hatecrest","hatecrest naga scale","latronicus moonspear","naga","sardor isle"},rel={"subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","subzone:sardor-isle","topic:naga","zone:feralas"},m={start="Latronicus Moonspear",["end"]="Latronicus Moonspear",level="43",faction="Alliance",id=2869},src={"Against the Hatecrest (2)"}}
E["quest:2870"] = {t="quest",n="Against Lord Shalzaru",z="feralas",s="Latronicus Moonspear at Feathermoon Stronghold tells you that scouts have identified one of the crueler naga royals, Lord Shalzaru. He asks you to put a stop to Shalzaru and bring back the relic the naga lord uncovered.",h="Latronicus Moonspear at Feathermoon Stronghold tells you that scouts have identified one of the crueler naga...",sec={{t="The Naga Chain of Command",b="New scouting reports have given Latronicus Moonspear a good picture of how the naga are led. Royals sit among their ranks, and it is they who give the orders. One of the crueler of them is Lord Shalzaru.",sp=0},{t="An Odd Relic",b="Scouts report that Shalzaru himself uncovered an odd relic while the naga were digging, in a cave on the Isle of Dread, over the water and south of the main ruins. Latronicus wants an end put to the dig by putting an end to Shalzaru, and wants the Mysterious Relic brought to him at Feathermoon Stronghold so it can be studied.",sp=0},{t="When It Is Done",b="Latronicus believes that Shalzaru's fall will leave the naga in disarray for a while, perhaps for good, and that the threat is now more under control than it has ever been. He then has one more thing to ask of you.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Lord Shalzaru?",a="One of the crueler naga royals, identified by scouts. Royals sit among the naga ranks and give the orders.",al={"shalzaru","who is shalzaru","lord shalzaru lore"}},{q="Where is Lord Shalzaru located?",a="Scouts place the dig in a cave on the Isle of Dread, over the water and south of the main ruins.",al={"where is shalzaru","shalzaru cave location","find shalzaru"}},{q="What is the relic?",a="An odd relic that Shalzaru himself uncovered while the naga were digging. Latronicus wants it brought to him so it can be studied.",al={"mysterious relic feralas","what is the relic","shalzaru relic"}},{q="Where do I deliver the relic?",a="To Latronicus Moonspear in Feathermoon Stronghold.",al={"who gets the relic","turn in shalzaru"}}},kw={"feathermoon stronghold","feralas","hatecrest","isle of dread","latronicus moonspear","lord shalzaru","mysterious relic","naga","shalzaru"},rel={"npc:lord-shalzaru","subzone:isle-of-dread","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","quest:2871","quest:2869","topic:naga","zone:feralas"},m={start="Latronicus Moonspear",["end"]="Latronicus Moonspear",level="45",faction="Alliance",id=2870},src={"Against Lord Shalzaru"}}
E["quest:2871"] = {t="quest",n="Delivering the Relic",z="feralas",s="Latronicus Moonspear asks you to carry the Mysterious Relic to his wife, Vestia Moonspear, at Feathermoon Stronghold. He cannot make heads or tails of the device and hopes she can tell what it is.",h="Latronicus Moonspear asks you to carry the Mysterious Relic to his wife, Vestia Moonspear, at Feathermoon...",sec={{t="A Scholar's Eye",b="Latronicus Moonspear could not make sense of the device even with a wager riding on it. His wife Vestia, he says, is a fine priestess for their community and one of the most learned scholars to be found anywhere. If anyone can work out what the relic is, she can, and they need to know. She is only a short walk away and no doubt busy studying.",sp=0},{t="Vestia's First Look",b="Vestia knows of you as the one who has aided General Feathermoon and Latro against the naga. With the relic in her hands, she judges at first glance that it does not seem native to the ruins it came from, nor is it of naga design, being something far more alien. Researching it will take time, and once she is done she may call on your talents if you are around.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Vestia Moonspear?",a="Latronicus Moonspear's wife. Latronicus calls her a fine priestess for their community and as learned a scholar as any. She is at Feathermoon Stronghold.",al={"vestia moonspear","who is vestia","latro wife"}},{q="Where does the Mysterious Relic come from?",a="It is the relic Lord Shalzaru uncovered when the naga were digging in a cave on the Isle of Dread.",al={"where did the relic come from","relic origin","mysterious relic source"}},{q="What does Latronicus Moonspear know about the relic?",a="Little. He says he could not make heads or tails of the device, which is why he wants his wife to look at it.",al={"what does latronicus know","latro device"}},{q="Where do I take the relic?",a="To Vestia Moonspear in Feathermoon Stronghold. Latronicus says she is just around the bend.",al={"who gets the relic","delivering the relic destination"}}},kw={"delivering the relic","feathermoon stronghold","feralas","latronicus moonspear","mysterious relic","vestia moonspear"},rel={"quest:2870","npc:lord-shalzaru","topic:naga","zone:feralas"},m={start="Latronicus Moonspear",["end"]="Vestia Moonspear",level="45",faction="Alliance",id=2871},src={"Delivering the Relic"}}
E["quest:2879"] = {t="quest",n="The Stave of Equinex",z="feralas",s="Troyas Moonbreeze thinks his stave may be the Stave of Equinex, a key to a monument in the Ruins of Ravenwind. To find out, you are to gather the essence of four flames that still burn among those ruins.",h="Troyas Moonbreeze thinks his stave may be the Stave of Equinex, a key to a monument in the Ruins of Ravenwind.",sec={{t="A Key for the Monolith",b="After your return to Troyas Moonbreeze, he says his stave could be the Stave of Equinex, which is in fact a key to the Equinex Monolith. The monolith stands in the Ruins of Ravenwind. Among those ruins, four flames are still alight, named Samha, Imbel, Byltan and Lahassa. Each yields an essence, and standing by the monolith you are to use all four to energize the stave. If it truly is the Stave of Equinex, the monolith will open and give up a sacred artifact.",sp=0},{t="At the Stone",b="The energized stave is almost impossible to hold, its power rumbling through you. You reach for the cold surface of the monolith, and a small door opens so you can take what lies inside. Beams of light spill out around the stone.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Equinex Monolith located?",a="West of the Dream Bough on the mainland, in the Ravenwind ruins.",al={"equinex monolith location","where is monolith","find equinex monolith"}},{q="What are the four flames I need?",a="Samha, Imbel, Byltan and Lahassa, flames that still burn in the Ruins of Ravenwind. You gather the essence of each.",al={"four flames","flame names feralas","ravenwind flames"}},{q="What is the Stave of Equinex for?",a="Troyas Moonbreeze says it is a key for unlocking the Equinex Monolith, which holds a sacred artifact.",al={"what does the stave do","stave of equinex purpose","why energize stave"}},{q="Where do I energize the stave?",a="While standing by the Equinex Monolith, using the essences of the four flames.",al={"where to use essences","energize stave location"}}},kw={"byltan","dream bough","equinex monolith","feralas","imbel","lahassa","ruins of ravenwind","samha","stave of equinex","troyas moonbreeze"},rel={"quest:2943","subzone:ruins-of-ravenwind","subzone:dream-bough","zone:feralas"},m={start="Troyas Moonbreeze",["end"]="Equinex Monolith",level="50",faction="Alliance",id=2879},src={"The Stave of Equinex"}}
E["quest:2902"] = {t="quest",n="Woodpaw Investigation",z="feralas",s="Hadoken Swiftstrider is sure the Woodpaw gnolls follow some written strategy. He sends you to search the gnoll camps south of Camp Mojache for anything resembling battle plans.",h="Hadoken Swiftstrider is sure the Woodpaw gnolls follow some written strategy.",sec={{t="A Search for Plans",b="This comes after Alpha Strike. Hadoken has little respect for gnoll brains, yet he is sure they keep some record of their strategy, as their recent assaults are too well coordinated to be improvised. If he could see those plans, he would better understand what stirred them up. He sends you back to the Woodpaw to find whatever looks like battle plans and bring it to him.",sp=0},{t="What the Map Shows",b="The map is indeed what Hadoken wanted. Arrows cross it that might show troop movements, but most run south, away from Camp Mojache in the north. Elsewhere on the map is a drawing of what you take to be a big insect, with tick marks beneath it, maybe a count of the gnolls' losses to unknown bugs.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to investigate the Woodpaw gnolls?",a="Hadoken Swiftstrider at Camp Mojache.",al={"who gives woodpaw investigation","quest giver woodpaw investigation"}},{q="Why does Hadoken believe the gnolls have battle plans?",a="Their assaults have been too well coordinated to be improvised, so Hadoken expects a written strategy that would show what has them so stirred up.",al={"why do gnolls have plans","woodpaw strategy"}},{q="Where are the battle plans located?",a="In the gnoll camps south of Camp Mojache.",al={"where are woodpaw plans","where to find woodpaw battle map"}},{q="What came before Woodpaw Investigation?",a="Alpha Strike is the step that comes right before this search.",al={"previous quest woodpaw investigation","woodpaw chain prerequisite"}}},kw={"battle map","battle plans","camp mojache","feralas","gnolls","hadoken swiftstrider","woodpaw"},rel={"subzone:camp-mojache","quest:2903","topic:gnoll","zone:feralas"},m={start="Hadoken Swiftstrider",["end"]="Woodpaw Battle Map",level="43",id=2902},src={"Classic quest text: Woodpaw Investigation"}}
E["quest:2903"] = {t="quest",n="The Battle Plans",z="feralas",s="You have the gnolls' battle plans. What is left is to carry them back to Hadoken Swiftstrider at Camp Mojache, where he or someone there may puzzle out what the gnolls are after.",h="You have the gnolls' battle plans.",sec={{t="Back to Camp Mojache",b="After Woodpaw Investigation, you hold the Woodpaw battle plans, and the only step left is returning them to Hadoken Swiftstrider at the camp. Hadoken is looking for solid evidence of the gnolls' intentions.",sp=0},{t="Hadoken's Reading",b="Hadoken says this is just what they needed. Most of the scrawl is beyond him, but he has seen enough battle plans to read the situation: the gnolls fight on two fronts. The camp is one, yet the bulk of their strength is turned on an enemy to the south. He senses something bigger behind it all, and thinks it is time to learn who that second enemy is.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do these battle plans need to go?",a="To Hadoken Swiftstrider at Camp Mojache.",al={"who gets the plans","where to turn in the battle plans","the battle plans turn in"}},{q="What came before this step?",a="Woodpaw Investigation, the search for the gnolls' plans.",al={"previous quest","what leads to battle plans","battle plans prerequisite"}},{q="Where did the battle plans come from?",a="They are the gnolls' own plans, turned up in the gnoll camps south of Camp Mojache during Woodpaw Investigation.",al={"who made the map","which gnolls made the plans","woodpaw plans origin"}}},kw={"battle plans","camp mojache","feralas","gnolls","hadoken swiftstrider","woodpaw"},rel={"quest:2902","subzone:camp-mojache","zone:feralas","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Woodpaw Battle Map",["end"]="Hadoken Swiftstrider",level="43",id=2903},src={"Classic quest text: The Battle Plans"}}
E["quest:2939"] = {t="quest",n="In Search of Knowledge",z="feralas",s="Troyas Moonbreeze found what looks like an ordinary stave in the rubble of the Feralas ruins, but he cannot shake the feeling there is more to it. He sends you to talk to his colleague Daryn Lightwind in Rut'theran Village.",h="Troyas Moonbreeze found what looks like an ordinary stave in the rubble of the Feralas ruins, but he cannot...",sec={{t="An Ordinary Stave",b="Troyas Moonbreeze says the Feralas ruins are dangerous but have much to tell about what has happened there. A few days ago, searching the rubble to the south, he came upon a stave that seems ordinary, yet he cannot shake the feeling there is more to it. He and Angelas have pored over their books without finding a word about it.",sp=0},{t="A Colleague in Darnassus",b="Troyas has a colleague in Darnassus who may be able to say what the stave is. He asks you to go and talk to her, Daryn Lightwind, in Rut'theran Village.",sp=0},{t="Daryn's Reply",b="Daryn grumbles that Troyas keeps pestering her with wild notions that he has found something important. In her view, the ogres or harpies living in those ruins now probably carried off anything truly valuable long ago. You are welcome to look around, she adds, though she doubts any books there will help.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Daryn Lightwind?",a="Troyas Moonbreeze, who wants to know what the stave he found in the Feralas ruins really is.",al={"who starts in search of knowledge","quest giver"}},{q="What did Troyas find?",a="A stave that seems ordinary, found in the rubble to the south of where Troyas works. He feels there is something more to it.",al={"what did troyas find","feralas stave"}},{q="Where is Daryn Lightwind?",a="In Rut'theran Village. Troyas describes her as a colleague in Darnassus.",al={"daryn lightwind location","where is daryn"}},{q="Why does Troyas send you to Daryn?",a="He and Angelas could find nothing about the stave in their books, and Daryn may be able to tell them what it is.",al={"why visit daryn lightwind","why darnassus"}}},kw={"angelas","darnassus","daryn lightwind","feralas","ruins","rut'theran village","stave","troyas moonbreeze"},rel={"zone:feralas","subzone:rut-theran-village","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Troyas Moonbreeze",["end"]="Daryn Lightwind",level="47",faction="Alliance",id=2939},src={"In Search of Knowledge"}}
E["quest:2940"] = {t="quest",n="Feralas: A History",z="feralas",s="You find a book that looks as if nobody has opened it in ages, and it may be exactly what Troyas needs. It belongs to Daryn Lightwind, so you need to ask whether you may borrow it.",h="You find a book that looks as if nobody has opened it in ages, and it may be exactly what Troyas needs.",sec={{t="A Neglected Book",b="The book's covers are badly worn and its pages have yellowed. After looking it over, you suspect it may be what Troyas is searching for. You pick it up, then think better of borrowing it without asking. It is Daryn Lightwind's, so she should be asked first.",sp=0},{t="Daryn's Answer",b="Daryn Lightwind takes a moment to think it over. She will let you borrow Feralas: A History, though only after you have done a favor for her.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the book Feralas: A History?",a="A book with worn covers and yellowed pages, which looks as if it has not been opened for ages. It may be exactly what Troyas is searching for.",al={"what is the book","feralas a history book","troyas book"}},{q="Who owns the book?",a="Daryn Lightwind. You should ask her before borrowing it.",al={"who owns feralas a history","who has the book","who is daryn lightwind"}},{q="What comes before this?",a="It follows In Search of Knowledge, in which Troyas Moonbreeze sent you to talk to Daryn Lightwind about his stave.",al={"previous quest","what was the last quest","chain before this"}}},kw={"book","daryn lightwind","feralas","history","in search of knowledge","lore","troyas"},rel={"quest:2939","quest:2941","zone:feralas"},m={start="Feralas: A History",["end"]="Daryn Lightwind",level="47",faction="Alliance",id=2940},src={"Feralas: A History (quest)"}}
E["quest:2941"] = {t="quest",n="The Borrower",z="feralas",s="Daryn Lightwind is fascinated by the snapjaws on the beach in the Hinterlands, and above all by a giant one named Gammerita. Her research keeps her where she is, so she gives you a letter to carry to Curgle Cranklehop in Tanaris.",h="Daryn Lightwind is fascinated by the snapjaws on the beach in the Hinterlands, and above all by a giant one...",sec={{t="A Picture of Gammerita",b="Daryn Lightwind says she has studied many subjects, and her latest fascination is the snapjaws that live along the beach in the Hinterlands. One she especially wants to see is a giant snapjaw called Gammerita. She would go herself, but her research keeps her here, so a picture of Gammerita would be the next best thing.",sp=0},{t="The Letter to Tanaris",b="Daryn hands you a letter for Curgle Cranklehop in Tanaris. Curgle has made an invention for Daryn that can capture a picture, which Daryn believes Curgle calls a snapshot.",sp=0},{t="Curgle's Reaction",b="Curgle takes you for one of Daryn's interns and speaks well of Daryn as a knowledgeable historian. Then Curgle goes off to fetch the Super Snapper FX, certain you will love it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Tanaris?",a="Daryn Lightwind, who gives you a letter to carry. Her research keeps her from going herself.",al={"quest giver","who gives the borrower","daryn lightwind"}},{q="Who is Curgle Cranklehop?",a="Someone in Tanaris who has made an invention for Daryn that can capture a picture, which Daryn believes is called a snapshot.",al={"who is curgle","curgle cranklehop location","curgle tanaris"}},{q="Why does Daryn want a picture of Gammerita?",a="Daryn is fascinated by the snapjaws along the Hinterlands beach, and wants to see Gammerita in particular. Research keeps Daryn from going, so a picture is the next best thing.",al={"gammerita snapjaw","why gammerita","giant snapjaw"}},{q="What is Gammerita?",a="A giant snapjaw on the beach in the Hinterlands.",al={"who is gammerita","gammerita"}}},kw={"curgle cranklehop","daryn lightwind","gammerita","snapjaw","snapshot","super snapper fx","tanaris","the borrower"},rel={"quest:2944","zone:tanaris","zone:hinterlands"},m={start="Daryn Lightwind",["end"]="Curgle Cranklehop",level="48",faction="Alliance",id=2941},src={"The Borrower"}}
E["quest:2942"] = {t="quest",n="The Morrow Stone",z="feralas",s="The moment you take the artifact from the Equinex Monolith, the power in the Stave of Equinex starts to fade. You are to bring the Sparkling Stone and the stave back to Troyas Moonbreeze at Feathermoon Stronghold.",h="The moment you take the artifact from the Equinex Monolith, the power in the Stave of Equinex starts to fade.",sec={{t="Back to Feathermoon Stronghold",b="As the artifact leaves the monolith, the stave's energy starts to fade. Troyas Moonbreeze at Feathermoon Stronghold is eager to hear what you found, so bring both the Sparkling Stone and the stave to him.",sp=0},{t="Troyas's Findings",b="Troyas has been reading since you left, and he names the stone the Morrow Stone. He is not yet sure of its purpose, but anything hidden inside the monolith the way it was must carry great significance. He will go on with his studies and hopes you will stand with him.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does this begin?",a="At the Equinex Monolith, once the artifact has been taken from it.",al={"where do I get this quest","where to start morrow stone","equinex monolith start"}},{q="Who do I bring the stone to?",a="Troyas Moonbreeze, in Feathermoon Stronghold. Bring the Stave of Equinex too.",al={"who turns in morrow stone","where is troyas moonbreeze","who gets the sparkling stone"}},{q="What happens to the Stave of Equinex?",a="Its energy starts to fade the moment the artifact is taken from the monolith.",al={"stave of equinex energy","what happens to the staff","why did the stave lose power"}},{q="What comes before this?",a="It follows The Stave of Equinex, in which you energized the stave beside the monolith.",al={"previous quest","what quest comes before the morrow stone","prerequisite quest"}}},kw={"equinex monolith","feathermoon stronghold","feralas","morrow stone","sparkling stone","stave of equinex","troyas moonbreeze"},rel={"quest:2879","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","zone:feralas"},m={start="Equinex Monolith",["end"]="Troyas Moonbreeze",level="50",faction="Alliance",id=2942},src={"The Morrow Stone"}}
E["quest:2943"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Troyas",z="feralas",s="Daryn Lightwind hands over her book, Feralas: A History, and asks you to take care of it. It goes to Troyas Moonbreeze at Feathermoon Stronghold, who is surely eager for your return.",h="Daryn Lightwind hands over her book, Feralas: A History, and asks you to take care of it.",sec={{t="A Borrowed Book",b="With the Super Snapper FX behind you, Daryn Lightwind gives you her book and asks that you look after it. She urges you to hurry along, sure that Troyas is eager for your return. The book is bound for Troyas Moonbreeze at Feathermoon Stronghold.",sp=0},{t="Troyas Reads",b="Troyas is glad you brought the book. He looks it over, skims its pages, and exclaims that he thinks he has found it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What am I delivering?",a="Daryn Lightwind's book, Feralas: A History.",al={"what book is this","what do i bring troyas","feralas a history book"}},{q="Where is Troyas Moonbreeze?",a="At Feathermoon Stronghold.",al={"troyas location","where is troyas moonbreeze","where do i go"}},{q="Who gives you the book?",a="Daryn Lightwind, who asks you to take care of it.",al={"who gives the quest","quest giver","daryn lightwind"}},{q="What came before this?",a="It follows The Super Snapper FX.",al={"previous quest","what did i just do","chain before this"}}},kw={"darnassus","daryn lightwind","feathermoon stronghold","feralas","feralas: a history","troyas moonbreeze"},rel={"quest:2944","quest:2879","quest:2940","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","zone:darnassus","zone:feralas"},m={start="Daryn Lightwind",["end"]="Troyas Moonbreeze",level="48",faction="Alliance",id=2943},src={"Return to Troyas"}}
E["quest:2944"] = {t="quest",n="The Super Snapper FX",z="feralas",s="Curgle Cranklehop has a new picture-taking device ready, the Super Snapper FX, and hands it to you to try out. The subject is Gammerita, a creature from the Hinterlands. With her snapshot in hand, you bring it and the device to Daryn Lightwind in Rut'theran Village. This follows The Borrower.",h="Curgle Cranklehop has a new picture-taking device ready, the Super Snapper FX, and hands it to you to try out.",sec={{t="A Device to Test",b="After The Borrower, Curgle Cranklehop presents you with the Super Snapper FX, a new invention of theirs. Using it is simple: aim at whatever you want pictured and press the button. Curgle gives it to you to try out.",sp=0},{t="The Subject",b="The subject is Gammerita, a creature from the Hinterlands that you had mentioned to Curgle. Curgle wishes you luck in finding her, and expects Daryn Lightwind to be pleased with the snapshot. Once you have it, the picture and the device go to Daryn in Rut'theran Village.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the Super Snapper FX?",a="Curgle Cranklehop hands you the device, a new invention, for you to try out.",al={"who gives super snapper","curgle quest giver","where to get super snapper fx"}},{q="What do I photograph with the Super Snapper FX?",a="Gammerita, a creature from the Hinterlands. Curgle wishes you luck finding her.",al={"gammerita location","where is gammerita","gammerita snapshot"}},{q="Who receives the snapshot?",a="Daryn Lightwind in Rut'theran Village. You bring her both the snapshot and the device.",al={"turn in super snapper fx","where does the picture go","who is daryn lightwind"}},{q="What comes next in the chain?",a="The chain goes on with Return to Troyas.",al={"next quest after super snapper","what follows super snapper fx"}}},kw={"curgle cranklehop","daryn lightwind","gammerita","rut'theran village","snapshot","super snapper fx","the hinterlands"},rel={"quest:2941","quest:2943","zone:hinterlands","subzone:rut-theran-village","zone:feralas"},m={start="Curgle Cranklehop",["end"]="Daryn Lightwind",level="48",faction="Alliance",id=2944},src={"The Super Snapper FX"}}
E["quest:2969"] = {t="quest",n="Freedom for All Creatures",z="feralas",s="The Grimtotem clan is capturing faerie dragons, and Kindal Moonweaver and Jer'kai do not know what for. Kindal asks you to bring strong friends, open the pen in the Grimtotem camp with a key and see the sprite darters out alive. Kindal comes with you; Jer'kai stays behind.",h="The Grimtotem clan is capturing faerie dragons, and Kindal Moonweaver and Jer'kai do not know what for.",sec={{t="Dragons in the Pen",b="Kindal Moonweaver calls the Grimtotem clan filthy for taking faerie dragons, and says that neither Kindal nor Jer'kai can guess their plans, only that they are up to no good. The two are not strong enough to fight their way into the camp, so Kindal turns to you. The Bamboo Cage Key opens the pen, and Kindal wants the sprite darters to escape with their lives. Strong friends at your side are welcome.",sp=0},{t="Kindal's Lookout",b="Kindal is found on the ledge behind the Grimtotem Compound, above the water, reached by a path up the cliff face. Kindal fights beside you through the camp, while Jer'kai stays behind.",sp=0},{t="Afterward",b="Once the darters are free, Kindal gives thanks to Elune. The danger has not ended: freed dragons will not necessarily stay free, so Kindal and Jer'kai mean to take the fight to the Grimtotem. Kindal sends you to speak with Jer'kai.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is capturing the faerie dragons?",a="The Grimtotem clan, according to Kindal Moonweaver. What they want with the dragons, Kindal and Jer'kai cannot say.",al={"who captured the faerie dragons","who has the sprite darters","grimtotem cages"}},{q="Where is Kindal Moonweaver?",a="On a ledge behind the Grimtotem Compound, above the water. A path behind a tree climbs the cliff face, reached by going left of the compound.",al={"where is kindal","kindal moonweaver location","how to get to kindal moonweaver"}},{q="Does Jer'kai come along?",a="No. Jer'kai stays behind, while Kindal goes with you.",al={"does jerkai help","jerkai involvement"}},{q="What do I need to free the sprite darters?",a="The Bamboo Cage Key, which Kindal gives you, opens the pen in the Grimtotem camp. Kindal wants you to bring strong friends.",al={"bamboo cage key","how to free sprite darters"}},{q="What follows this quest?",a="Doling Justice is the next step of the chain.",al={"next quest freedom for all creatures","what next after saving sprite darters"}}},kw={"bamboo cage","elune","faerie dragon","feralas","grimtotem compound","jer'kai","kindal moonweaver","sprite darter"},rel={"npc:kindal-moonweaver","npc:sprite-darter","subzone:grimtotem-compound","quest:2970","zone:feralas","topic:elune"},m={start="Kindal Moonweaver",["end"]="Kindal Moonweaver",level="47",faction="Alliance",id=2969},src={"Freedom for All Creatures"}}
E["quest:2970"] = {t="quest",n="Doling Justice",z="feralas",s="With the sprite darters freed, Jer'kai Moonweaver and Kindal mean to take the fight to the Grimtotem clan. Jer'kai asks you to cut down Grimtotem Naturalists, Raiders and Shamans, then return to Jer'kai. This follows Freedom for All Creatures.",h="With the sprite darters freed, Jer'kai Moonweaver and Kindal mean to take the fight to the Grimtotem clan.",sec={{t="Taking the Fight to the Grimtotem",b="After Freedom for All Creatures, Jer'kai Moonweaver tells you that Kindal and Jer'kai will now strike back at the Grimtotem. Together they can thin out some of the tauren without much risk to themselves, but they would welcome your help. You have seen the camp below, and there are more to the east. Use your own tactics against Grimtotem Naturalists, Raiders and Shamans, then meet back where Jer'kai waits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives Doling Justice?",a="Jer'kai Moonweaver, in Feralas, once Kindal has told you what the pair intend after the sprite darter rescue.",al={"who gives doling justice","quest giver doling justice","jer'kai moonweaver"}},{q="Which Grimtotem are targeted?",a="Grimtotem Naturalists, Grimtotem Raiders and Grimtotem Shamans, among the tauren of the Grimtotem clan.",al={"what enemies do i kill","doling justice targets","grimtotem kills"}},{q="Where are the Grimtotem camps?",a="One camp lies in sight below Jer'kai, and Jer'kai says there are more to the east.",al={"where are the grimtotem","grimtotem camp location","where do i go"}},{q="What comes before Doling Justice?",a="Freedom for All Creatures, in which you freed the sprite darters from the Grimtotem camp.",al={"prior quest","doling justice prerequisite","previous step"}}},kw={"doling justice","feralas","grimtotem","jer'kai moonweaver","kindal moonweaver","naturalist","raider","shaman"},rel={"quest:2969","zone:feralas","topic:tauren"},m={start="Jer'kai Moonweaver",["end"]="Jer'kai Moonweaver",level="47",faction="Alliance",id=2970},src={"Doling Justice"}}
E["quest:2972"] = {t="quest",n="Doling Justice",z="feralas",s="Out in the wilderness, Jer'kai Moonweaver and Kindal have little to give in thanks, so Jer'kai hands you a signet ring. It is yours to carry to High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind at the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, where it will tell her that the two of them are well and lend weight to your story. This follows Doling Justice.",h="Out in the wilderness, Jer'kai Moonweaver and Kindal have little to give in thanks, so Jer'kai hands you a...",sec={{t="A Ring for the High Priestess",b="Jer'kai Moonweaver and Kindal cannot offer much out in the wilds of Feralas, but they do not want you to feel unappreciated. Jer'kai hands over a signet ring and points you toward Darnassus, where High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind waits in the Temple of the Moon. The ring will show her that the pair are well, and it backs up the tale you will tell.",sp=0},{t="Tyrande's Answer",b="Tyrande is pleased that you helped dragonkind and one of her own priestesses, and says Jer'kai was right to send you. She promises that the ring will be returned to Jer'kai. Scouts are soon to head toward Feralas, and the ring will be one more matter for them to look into.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the signet ring?",a="Jer'kai Moonweaver, in Feralas, as thanks from Jer'kai and Kindal.",al={"who starts this quest","quest giver"}},{q="Where does the signet ring go?",a="To High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind, found at the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.",al={"where do I take the ring","turn in location","who gets jerkai's signet ring"}},{q="Why does Jer'kai give you the ring?",a="Jer'kai and Kindal have little to give in the wilderness. The ring shows Tyrande that they are well and gives credit to your story.",al={"purpose of the signet ring","why jerkai signet ring"}},{q="What comes next in the chain?",a="The chain goes on with An Orphan Looking For a Home.",al={"next quest","where to go next"}}},kw={"darnassus","feralas","jer'kai moonweaver","kindal moonweaver","signet ring","teldrassil","temple of the moon","tyrande whisperwind"},rel={"npc:tyrande-whisperwind","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","quest:3841","quest:2970","quest:2969","zone:feralas","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Jer'kai Moonweaver",["end"]="Tyrande Whisperwind",level="47",faction="Alliance",id=2972},src={"Doling Justice (2)"}}
E["quest:2973"] = {t="quest",n="A New Cloak's Sheen",z="feralas",s="Krueg Skullsplitter has come down to Feralas with companions, sent by their masters in Orgrimmar. Krueg plans a cloak for life-mate Korrin and asks you for ten Iridescent Sprite Darter Wings.",h="Krueg Skullsplitter has come down to Feralas with companions, sent by their masters in Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Cloak for Korrin",b="Krueg and companions came down to Feralas, sent by their masters in Orgrimmar. Krueg's life-mate Korrin loves new clothes, so Krueg plans a cloak adorned with the delicate wings of faerie dragons. The sprite darters with the beautiful wings Krueg wants live west of Camp Mojache, and Krueg asks you for ten Iridescent Sprite Darter Wings.",sp=0},{t="Krueg's Warning",b="Krueg cautions that provoked sprite darters are risky. Krueg says to be even more careful around night elves nearby, who tend to hole up in the forests too.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Krueg Skullsplitter?",a="Krueg Skullsplitter is at Camp Mojache. Krueg came down to Feralas with companions, sent by their masters in Orgrimmar.",al={"who is krueg","krueg skullsplitter lore","krueg in feralas"}},{q="Why does Krueg want sprite darter wings?",a="Krueg plans a cloak for life-mate Korrin, who loves new clothes, adorned with faerie dragon wings.",al={"why need darter wings","sprite darter wing purpose","what is krueg making"}},{q="Where are the sprite darters located?",a="West of Camp Mojache.",al={"where to find sprite darters","sprite darter location","where are faerie dragons in feralas"}},{q="What dangers does Krueg warn about?",a="Krueg says provoked sprite darters are risky, and that night elves nearby, who also tend to hole up in the forests, call for even more care.",al={"krueg warnings","threats in the forest feralas"}}},kw={"camp mojache","cloak","faerie dragon","feralas","iridescent wings","korrin","krueg skullsplitter","sprite darter"},rel={"subzone:camp-mojache","npc:sprite-darter","zone:feralas","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Krueg Skullsplitter",["end"]="Krueg Skullsplitter",level="45",id=2973},src={"Classic quest text: A New Cloak's Sheen"}}
E["quest:2974"] = {t="quest",n="A Grim Discovery",z="feralas",s="Krueg Skullsplitter in Camp Mojache is startled to hear that you met tauren in Feralas, and more so on learning they are Grimtotem. Belgrom, one of Krueg's masters, has put a bounty on their kind. Krueg wants you to go back and bring him twenty Grimtotem horns.",h="Krueg Skullsplitter in Camp Mojache is startled to hear that you met tauren in Feralas, and more so on...",sec={{t="Word of the Grimtotem",b="You tell Krueg Skullsplitter of tauren you came across in the area, and Krueg is quick to name them as the Grimtotem clan. Belgrom, one of Krueg's masters, takes a keen interest in their kind and has put a bounty on them. Krueg tells you the Grimtotem are not to be underestimated, and that they are evil. You go back, slay them and bring twenty horns to Camp Mojache, so the first blow falls before they can raze villages or pilfer land.",sp=0},{t="The Horns Delivered",b="Krueg judges the horns good and says you have now helped twice. Belgrom will hear of it as soon as Krueg is back in Orgrimmar.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives A Grim Discovery?",a="Krueg Skullsplitter in Camp Mojache, after you tell Krueg that you met tauren in the area.",al={"who gives grim discovery","krueg skullsplitter quest","quest giver grim discovery"}},{q="Why does Krueg want Grimtotem horns?",a="Krueg calls the Grimtotem clan evil and wants them struck before they can raze villages or pilfer land. Belgrom, one of the masters in Orgrimmar, has also put a bounty on them.",al={"why kill grimtotem","grimtotem threat feralas","why grimtotem horns"}},{q="Who is Belgrom?",a="Krueg calls Belgrom one of the masters, who has an interest in the Grimtotem and has put a bounty on them.",al={"belgrom orgrimmar","who is belgrom"}},{q="How many horns does Krueg want?",a="Twenty Grimtotem horns, brought to Krueg in Camp Mojache. Krueg would like piles of them if you can manage.",al={"grimtotem horn count","how many grimtotem horns"}},{q="What follows A Grim Discovery?",a="The chain goes on with A Grim Discovery (2).",al={"next quest grim discovery","grim discovery chain"}}},kw={"belgrom","camp mojache","feralas","grimtotem","horns","krueg skullsplitter"},rel={"subzone:camp-mojache","zone:feralas","topic:tauren","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Krueg Skullsplitter",["end"]="Krueg Skullsplitter",level="45",faction="Horde",id=2974},src={"A Grim Discovery (Classic)"}}
E["quest:2975"] = {t="quest",n="The Ogres of Feralas",z="feralas",s="Rok Orhan at Camp Mojache wants the Gordunni ogres pushed back before they spread further into Feralas. Following the river north leads to their outpost, where ogres, ogre-magi and brutes are to be thinned out.",h="Rok Orhan at Camp Mojache wants the Gordunni ogres pushed back before they spread further into Feralas.",sec={{t="The Mark of the Gordunni",b="Rok Orhan points out that the Gordunni ogre tribe is hard to miss around here, since their very presence scars the land. They must be driven back before they reach deeper into Feralas. Their outpost lies up the river to the north. There you cut down ten Gordunni Ogres, ten Gordunni Ogre-Magi and five Gordunni Brutes, to show the tribe they are unwelcome.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants the Gordunni ogres driven back?",a="Rok Orhan at Camp Mojache.",al={"who gives the quest","quest giver","rok orhan"}},{q="Why does Rok Orhan want the Gordunni pushed back?",a="Rok Orhan says their very presence scars the land, and they must be stopped before they expand further into Feralas.",al={"why kill the ogres","gordunni motive","why fight gordunni"}},{q="Where is the Gordunni outpost?",a="Follow the river north, says Rok Orhan, and the outpost will be found there.",al={"ogre outpost location","where are the ogres","gordunni location feralas"}},{q="Which Gordunni must be slain?",a="Ten Gordunni Ogres, ten Gordunni Ogre-Magi and five Gordunni Brutes.",al={"how many ogres","gordunni kill count"}},{q="What follows this quest?",a="The chain goes on with The Ogres of Feralas (2).",al={"next quest ogres of feralas","ogres of feralas chain"}}},kw={"brute","camp mojache","feralas","gordunni","ogre","ogre mage","rok orhan"},rel={"subzone:camp-mojache","zone:feralas"},m={start="Rok Orhan",["end"]="Rok Orhan",level="43",faction="Horde",id=2975},src={"The Ogres of Feralas (1)"}}
E["quest:2976"] = {t="quest",n="A Grim Discovery",z="feralas",s="Krueg Skullsplitter admits to having mentioned a bounty, and says the one who did the work deserves the best of the payoff. The horns are put in a crate for you to carry to Belgrom Rockmaul, found in the Valley of Honor in Orgrimmar, who will want your account. This follows the first A Grim Discovery.",h="Krueg Skullsplitter admits to having mentioned a bounty, and says the one who did the work deserves the best...",sec={{t="The Crate of Horns",b="After the first A Grim Discovery, Krueg Skullsplitter is taken aback, then admits to mentioning a bounty. You did the work, so Krueg feels it only right that you take the best of the payoff. The horns are packed into a crate for you. The crate goes to Belgrom Rockmaul, found in the Valley of Honor, who wishes to hear what you saw and will make your hard work worth it.",sp=0},{t="Belgrom's Interest",b="Belgrom Rockmaul is struck by news of the Grimtotem and asks whether you truly met them out on a hunt in Feralas. Belgrom's peers will want the story, so you are asked to tell more while the coin is counted out. Belgrom ends with thanks for the information.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives this part of A Grim Discovery?",a="Krueg Skullsplitter, who has the horns put in a crate for you.",al={"who gives a grim discovery","krueg skullsplitter quest","quest giver a grim discovery 2"}},{q="Where does the crate of Grimtotem horns go?",a="To Belgrom Rockmaul, who waits in the Valley of Honor in Orgrimmar.",al={"where do i take the horns","belgrom rockmaul location","turn in grim discovery 2"}},{q="Why is the bounty yours?",a="Krueg says you did the work, so the best of the payoff should rightly be yours.",al={"why grimtotem horns","bounty grim discovery"}},{q="What does Belgrom want from you?",a="Krueg says Belgrom will be eager to hear what you saw, and will make your hard work worth it.",al={"belgrom rockmaul grimtotem","why care about feralas grimtotem"}},{q="What comes before this step?",a="The first A Grim Discovery, in which you brought Krueg Grimtotem horns.",al={"grim discovery chain","prerequisite for grim discovery 2","prior quests"}}},kw={"belgrom rockmaul","bounty","feralas","grimtotem","horns","krueg skullsplitter","orgrimmar","valley of honor"},rel={"quest:2974","zone:feralas","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:valley-of-honor"},m={start="Krueg Skullsplitter",["end"]="Belgrom Rockmaul",level="45",faction="Horde",id=2976},src={"A Grim Discovery (2)"}}
E["quest:2978"] = {t="quest",n="The Gordunni Scroll",z="feralas",s="A soiled scroll lies in the Gordunni Outpost, and picking it up shows what seems to be a meeting or ceremony. Rok Orhan at Camp Mojache would be interested in it, and in what it might mean for the Gordunni.",h="A soiled scroll lies in the Gordunni Outpost, and picking it up shows what seems to be a meeting or ceremony.",sec={{t="The Soiled Scroll",b="Taking up the soiled scroll, you see that it appears to depict a gathering or ceremony of some kind. Rok Orhan in Camp Mojache, you judge, would want to see it, and to learn what it might mean for the Gordunni.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the Gordunni Scroll show?",a="It seems to show some sort of meeting or ceremony.",al={"what does the scroll show","gordunni scroll contents","scroll drawing"}},{q="Who wants the Gordunni Scroll?",a="Rok Orhan, in Camp Mojache.",al={"who wants the scroll","where do i take the scroll","turn in gordunni scroll"}},{q="Where is the Gordunni Scroll found?",a="In the Gordunni Outpost, where you can pick it up.",al={"where is the gordunni scroll","gordunni scroll location"}},{q="What follows the Gordunni Scroll?",a="The chain goes on with Dark Ceremony.",al={"what is the next quest","after the gordunni scroll","gordunni scroll chain"}}},kw={"camp mojache","ceremony","feralas","gordunni outpost","gordunni scroll","ogres","rok orhan"},rel={"quest:2979","subzone:camp-mojache","subzone:gordunni-outpost","zone:feralas","quest:3002"},m={start="Gordunni Scroll",["end"]="Rok Orhan",level="43",faction="Horde",id=2978},src={"The Gordunni Scroll"}}
E["quest:2979"] = {t="quest",n="Dark Ceremony",z="feralas",s="After the Gordunni Scroll, Rok Orhan at Camp Mojache reads it as plans for a dark ceremony led by the Gordunni mage-lords. Rok Orhan wants you to take an orb from one of those mage-lords, to learn more about the ceremony and the Gordunni's magic.",h="After the Gordunni Scroll, Rok Orhan at Camp Mojache reads it as plans for a dark ceremony led by the...",sec={{t="Plans for a Dark Ceremony",b="Rok Orhan has looked over the Gordunni Scroll you brought and reads it as the plans for a dark ceremony. As far as Rok can tell, the Gordunni mage-lords are the ones who conduct it. A mage-lord must be found, and an orb taken from him. A mage's orb holds great power, and it should reveal more about the ceremony and the magic the Gordunni wield.",sp=0},{t="When the Orb Is Delivered",b="Once the orb is in hand, Rok Orhan says it will tell more about the Gordunni, and the knowledge will go into planning their downfall.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives Dark Ceremony?",a="Rok Orhan at Camp Mojache, following the Gordunni Scroll you brought.",al={"who gives dark ceremony","dark ceremony questgiver"}},{q="Who carries out the dark ceremony?",a="Rok Orhan makes out from the plans that the Gordunni mage-lords conduct it.",al={"who is performing the dark ceremony","gordunni ritual leader"}},{q="What orb is Rok Orhan after?",a="An orb taken from one of the Gordunni mage-lords. The orb of a mage holds great power, and Rok Orhan expects it to teach more about the ceremony and the Gordunni's magic.",al={"why get gordunni orb","purpose of gordunni orb"}},{q="What follows Dark Ceremony?",a="The chain goes on with The Gordunni Orb.",al={"next quest after dark ceremony","dark ceremony chain"}}},kw={"camp mojache","dark ceremony","feralas","gordunni","gordunni orb","mage-lord","rok orhan"},rel={"quest:2978","quest:3002","subzone:camp-mojache","zone:feralas"},m={start="Rok Orhan",["end"]="Rok Orhan",level="46",faction="Horde",id=2979},src={"Dark Ceremony"}}
E["quest:2980"] = {t="quest",n="The Ogres of Feralas",z="feralas",s="Rok Orhan at Camp Mojache, satisfied that you are a true fighter, sends you on to the High Wilderness, southwest of the camp. Among ruined structures once held by the night elves, Gordunni ogres far tougher than before are to be pushed back. This follows The Ogres of Feralas.",h="Rok Orhan at Camp Mojache, satisfied that you are a true fighter, sends you on to the High Wilderness...",sec={{t="Into the High Wilderness",b="Rok Orhan judges that you have proven yourself a true fighter, and trusts you with the next part of the work. The High Wilderness lies southwest of the camp, where abandoned, wrecked structures stand on ground the night elves once owned. Withered trees and desecrated ground show where the Gordunni are. Rok warns that these ogres are far tougher than the earlier ones. Ten Gordunni Shamans, ten Gordunni Warlocks and five Gordunni Maulers are to fall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to the High Wilderness?",a="Rok Orhan at Camp Mojache.",al={"quest giver","rok orhan","who starts this"}},{q="Where are these Gordunni?",a="In the High Wilderness, southwest of Camp Mojache, around wrecked structures on ground the night elves once owned. Withered trees and desecrated ground mark the spot.",al={"where are the ogres","high wilderness location","ruins location"}},{q="Which ogres must be killed?",a="Ten Gordunni Shamans, ten Gordunni Warlocks and five Gordunni Maulers.",al={"who do i kill","ogre targets","gordunni types"}},{q="What comes before this step?",a="The first The Ogres of Feralas, in which Rok Orhan sent you against the ogres at their outpost to the north.",al={"prerequisite","previous quest","chain order"}}},kw={"camp mojache","feralas","gordunni","high wilderness","maulers","rok orhan","shamans","warlocks"},rel={"quest:2975","subzone:camp-mojache","subzone:high-wilderness","zone:feralas","quest:2982"},m={start="Rok Orhan",["end"]="Rok Orhan",level="44",faction="Horde",id=2980},src={"The Ogres of Feralas (2)"}}
E["quest:2982"] = {t="quest",n="The High Wilderness",z="feralas",s="Angelas Moonbreeze and Troyas look into old ruins in the forests of Feralas, yet lately Troyas goes alone to the High Wilderness, which worries Angelas. Gordunni ogres hold that ground. Angelas hopes you will make the ruins to the southeast a little safer by culling the ogres.",h="Angelas Moonbreeze and Troyas look into old ruins in the forests of Feralas, yet lately Troyas goes alone to...",sec={{t="Worry for Troyas",b="Angelas Moonbreeze admits the work is dangerous, but Angelas and Troyas keep exploring the ruins scattered through the forests of Feralas. Lately Troyas goes to the High Wilderness alone, and Angelas worries. The Gordunni ogres have taken over there and do not take kindly to anyone who enters their territory. Angelas hopes you will go to the ruins southeast of here and cull some of them, to make it safer for Troyas: eight Gordunni Warlocks, eight Gordunni Shamans and eight Gordunni Brutes.",sp=0},{t="Afterward",b="Once it is done, Angelas is very grateful, and asks you not to mention a word of it to Troyas.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who asks you to clear out the High Wilderness?",a="Angelas Moonbreeze, who investigates the ruins of Feralas together with Troyas.",al={"who is angelas","angelas moonbreeze","who gives the high wilderness quest"}},{q="Why does Angelas want the Gordunni ogres thinned out?",a="Troyas has been going alone to the High Wilderness, and Angelas worries. The Gordunni ogres have taken the area and do not welcome visitors in their territory.",al={"why kill gordunni","why kill ogres in high wilderness","angelas reason"}},{q="Where is the High Wilderness ruin?",a="Angelas points you to the ruins to the southeast.",al={"where is high wilderness","high wilderness location","ruins to the southeast"}},{q="Which Gordunni must be slain?",a="Eight Gordunni Warlocks, eight Gordunni Shamans and eight Gordunni Brutes.",al={"who do i kill high wilderness","gordunni targets high wilderness"}},{q="What is said about the Gordunni's magic?",a="Angelas warns that the magic of the Gordunni seems to ravage the very ground beneath them, and bids you be watchful around them.",al={"gordunni magic","ogre spells","what magic wreaks havoc"}}},kw={"angelas moonbreeze","feralas","gordunni","gordunni brute","gordunni shaman","gordunni warlock","high wilderness","ogres","troyas"},rel={"subzone:high-wilderness","zone:feralas"},m={start="Angelas Moonbreeze",["end"]="Angelas Moonbreeze",level="44",faction="Alliance",id=2982},src={"The High Wilderness (quest)"}}
E["quest:2987"] = {t="quest",n="Gordunni Cobalt",z="feralas",s="Orwin Gizzmick has just arrived in Feralas and heard that the Gordunni ogres keep interesting minerals buried. Orwin offers a shovel and asks you to head for the Gordunni Outpost, north of Camp Mojache, and dig up twelve samples of Gordunni cobalt, following the blue glow.",h="Orwin Gizzmick has just arrived in Feralas and heard that the Gordunni ogres keep interesting minerals buried.",sec={{t="Buried Minerals",b="Orwin Gizzmick has only just reached Feralas and has heard the Gordunni ogres possess some interesting minerals. Orwin does not know what the ogres are up to, but they guard it fiercely and do not leave it lying about. They bury it, to keep folks like Orwin from getting hold of it. Orwin gives you a shovel. The Gordunni Outpost lies north of the camp; a blue glow shows where to dig. Twelve samples of Gordunni cobalt are wanted.",sp=0},{t="When the Cobalt Is Delivered",b="Orwin means to carry the cobalt along on further travels, certain someone will pay a pretty penny for it, and gives you something for your trouble.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who wants Gordunni cobalt?",a="Orwin Gizzmick, at Camp Mojache, who has just arrived in Feralas.",al={"who starts gordunni cobalt","orwin gizzmick quest","who wants cobalt"}},{q="Where is the Gordunni cobalt?",a="Buried in the Gordunni Outpost, north of Camp Mojache.",al={"gordunni cobalt location","where to find cobalt feralas","where is gordunni outpost"}},{q="How do you spot the buried cobalt?",a="A blue glow gives away the spot, and then you dig.",al={"how to spot cobalt","finding cobalt feralas","blue glow ogre dirt"}},{q="Why do the ogres bury their cobalt?",a="Orwin says the ogres are protective of it and bury it to keep folks like Orwin from getting hold of it. What they want it for, Orwin cannot say.",al={"why is cobalt buried","why do gordunni bury cobalt","ogre cobalt buried"}},{q="How much cobalt does Orwin want?",a="Twelve samples, dug up with Orwin's shovel.",al={"cobalt count","how many gordunni cobalt"}}},kw={"camp mojache","cobalt","feralas","gizzmick","gordunni","gordunni outpost","ogres","orwin","shovel"},rel={"zone:feralas","subzone:camp-mojache","subzone:gordunni-outpost"},m={start="Orwin Gizzmick",["end"]="Orwin Gizzmick",level="43",faction="Horde",id=2987},src={"Gordunni Cobalt (quest)"}}
E["quest:3002"] = {t="quest",n="The Gordunni Orb",z="feralas",s="Rok Orhan knows the enemy well, but is a warrior and cannot say what the Gordunni orb is capable of. Rok knows of a mage in Orgrimmar who can tell more. The orb is yours to carry to Uthel'nay, at Orgrimmar's Darkbriar Lodge. This follows Dark Ceremony.",h="Rok Orhan knows the enemy well, but is a warrior and cannot say what the Gordunni orb is capable of.",sec={{t="Beyond a Warrior's Knowledge",b="After Dark Ceremony, Rok Orhan holds the orb, but admits to being a warrior who cannot begin to say what it can do. Rok knows a mage in Orgrimmar who will be able to say more, and sends you off with the orb to find Uthel'nay at the Darkbriar Lodge.",sp=0},{t="Uthel'nay's Verdict",b="Uthel'nay finds the orb fascinating. It is very powerful, Uthel'nay says, but also very dangerous.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Uthel'nay?",a="Rok Orhan, once you have the orb that Dark Ceremony sent you for.",al={"gordunni orb chain","dark ceremony followup","prerequisites for the gordunni orb"}},{q="Why does Rok Orhan not examine the orb?",a="Rok Orhan is a warrior and cannot begin to say what the orb can do, but knows a mage in Orgrimmar who can tell more.",al={"why send orb to orgrimmar","why rok orhan gives orb away","why uthel'nay"}},{q="Where is Uthel'nay?",a="In the Darkbriar Lodge in Orgrimmar.",al={"uthel'nay location","where is uthelnay","darkbriar lodge location"}},{q="What comes before The Gordunni Orb?",a="Dark Ceremony, in which Rok Orhan sent you to take an orb from a Gordunni mage-lord.",al={"gordunni orb prerequisite","gordunni orb previous quest"}}},kw={"darkbriar lodge","feralas","gordunni","gordunni orb","orgrimmar","rok orhan","uthel'nay"},rel={"quest:2979","quest:2978","zone:feralas","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Rok Orhan",["end"]="Uthel'nay",level="47",faction="Horde",id=3002},src={"The Gordunni Orb (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3062"] = {t="quest",n="Dark Heart",z="feralas",s="Talo Thornhoof at Camp Mojache wants the dark heart of Edana Hatetalon, who is queen of the harpies of Northspring, living in ruins to the west. Talo calls her pure evil.",h="Talo Thornhoof at Camp Mojache wants the dark heart of Edana Hatetalon, who is queen of the harpies of...",sec={{t="The Harpy Queen",b="Edana Hatetalon is the harpies' queen, ruling the Northspring brood in ruins lying west. Talo calls her pure evil, with no feeling in her except hatred for everyone, and has heard her heart is made of crystal. Talo wants you to face her and bring back her dark heart, because the hatred she spreads must be stopped.",sp=0},{t="A Summons",b="Talo has heard of a horn the harpies carry. Sounded near the Hatetalon stones, up in the ruins' northern part, it is said to draw the queen out. Talo relishes the thought that her kin will not be the ones to answer, but her death.",sp=0},{t="On Your Return",b="Talo is certain now that Edana is gone for good, and says the heart will be kept in memory of what you did.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Edana Hatetalon?",a="She rules the Northspring harpies in the western ruins. Talo calls her pure evil and says she feels only hatred, and has heard her heart is crystal.",al={"edana hatetalon","harpy queen feralas","who is the harpy queen"}},{q="How can Edana Hatetalon be summoned?",a="Talo has heard that harpies carry a horn, and that sounding it near the Hatetalon stones at the northern end of the ruins will call the queen.",al={"how to summon edana","blow horn feralas","hatetalon stones"}},{q="Who gives the hunt for Edana Hatetalon?",a="Talo Thornhoof, at Camp Mojache.",al={"who gives dark heart","talo thornhoof","where to get dark heart"}},{q="Why does Talo Thornhoof want Edana's heart?",a="Talo wants an end to the hatred Edana spreads over the land, and asks for her dark heart.",al={"why dark heart","talo thornhoof motive"}}},kw={"camp mojache","dark heart","edana hatetalon","feralas","harpy","hatetalon stones","northspring","talo thornhoof"},rel={"subzone:camp-mojache","zone:feralas","topic:harpy"},m={start="Talo Thornhoof",["end"]="Talo Thornhoof",level="50",id=3062},src={"Classic quest text: Dark Heart"}}
E["quest:3063"] = {t="quest",n="Vengeance on the Northspring",z="feralas",s="Talo Thornhoof was once a seasoned hunter who feared no creature, until harpies ambushed Talo in the forest. The hate has boiled inside ever since, and Talo asks you to take revenge on the Northspring harpies, found to the west.",h="Talo Thornhoof was once a seasoned hunter who feared no creature, until harpies ambushed Talo in the forest.",sec={{t="An Old Hunter's Grudge",b="Talo remembers being a seasoned hunter who feared nothing that lived. Then came a day in the forest, honing a weapon once a hard fight was over, when harpies surrounded Talo. Talo barely dragged to safety, still hears their cries echoing, and was never the same afterward. All this time later the hate still boils, and Talo wants revenge.",sp=0},{t="The Northspring Harpies",b="The Northspring harpies live to the west. Talo wants four each of the Northspring Harpies, Roguefeathers, Windcallers and Slayers dead. Their wings are black as night, Talo warns, and they can slip out of sight into the darkness.",sp=0},{t="After the Hunt",b="Talo, speaking as an old tauren, thanks you and says you have put a troubled mind at peace.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Talo Thornhoof?",a="A seasoned hunter in days past, who feared no creature until harpies ambushed Talo in the forest. Talo was never the same afterward.",al={"talo thornhoof lore","who gives vengeance on the northspring","talo feralas"}},{q="Where are the Northspring harpies located?",a="To the west of Talo Thornhoof.",al={"northspring harpies location","where are northspring harpies","harpy location feralas"}},{q="Why does Talo want revenge against the harpies?",a="Harpies ambushed Talo in the forest, surrounding Talo while honing a weapon after a fight, and Talo barely got away. Talo was never the same, and the hate still boils inside.",al={"why kill northspring harpies","talo thornhoof backstory","why talo hates harpies"}},{q="Which harpies does Talo want killed?",a="Four each of the Northspring Harpies, Northspring Roguefeathers, Northspring Windcallers and Northspring Slayers.",al={"vengeance on the northspring targets","which harpies to kill","northspring harpy types"}},{q="What do the Northspring harpies look like?",a="Talo says their wings are black as night, and warns that they can vanish into the darkness.",al={"harpy appearance","northspring harpy wings"}}},kw={"feralas","harpies","northspring","revenge","roguefeather","slayer","talo thornhoof","windcaller"},rel={"zone:feralas","topic:harpy"},m={start="Talo Thornhoof",["end"]="Talo Thornhoof",level="50",id=3063},src={"Classic quest text: Vengeance on the Northspring"}}
E["quest:3121"] = {t="quest",n="A Strange Request",z="feralas",s="Witch Doctor Uzer'i needs a concoction that Neeru Fireblade in Orgrimmar has mixed up. Uzer'i hands you a shrunken head, promised to Neeru in exchange for the herbs, and sends you to the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar to deliver it.",h="Witch Doctor Uzer'i needs a concoction that Neeru Fireblade in Orgrimmar has mixed up.",sec={{t="A Promised Payment",b="Witch Doctor Uzer'i says Neeru Fireblade in Orgrimmar has what is needed to get started in Feralas: a concoction for something Uzer'i will not yet explain. Uzer'i gives you a shrunken head, promised to Neeru in return for the herbs. It is the head of some poor dwarf Uzer'i came across in the forest. Neeru can be found in the Cleft of Shadow.",sp=0},{t="Neeru's Herbs",b="Neeru Fireblade has been waiting for Uzer'i to make this delivery, and hands over the herb mixture prepared for Uzer'i's experiments.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives A Strange Request?",a="Witch Doctor Uzer'i, who has you take a shrunken head to Orgrimmar.",al={"who gives a strange request","who starts this","strange request quest giver"}},{q="Where is Neeru Fireblade?",a="In the Cleft of Shadow, in Orgrimmar.",al={"where is neeru fireblade","where do i go","shrunken head delivery location"}},{q="Whose head is the shrunken head?",a="Uzer'i calls it the head of some poor dwarf, come across in the forest.",al={"whose head is this","shrunken head identity","who was the dwarf"}},{q="Why does Uzer'i send a shrunken head to Neeru?",a="Uzer'i promised it to Neeru in exchange for the herbs, and needs the concoction Neeru has mixed up.",al={"why does neeru want the head","neeru fireblade trade"}},{q="What follows A Strange Request?",a="The chain goes on with Return to Witch Doctor Uzer'i.",al={"what is next","next quest after strange request"}}},kw={"a strange request","cleft of shadow","feralas","neeru fireblade","orgrimmar","shrunken head","witch doctor uzer'i"},rel={"quest:3122","npc:witch-doctor-uzer-i","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:feralas","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Witch Doctor Uzer'i",["end"]="Neeru Fireblade",level="45",faction="Horde",id=3121},src={"A Strange Request (Feralas)"}}
E["quest:3122"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Witch Doctor Uzer'i",z="feralas",s="With the shrunken head delivered in A Strange Request, Neeru Fireblade hands you the herbs and asks you to carry them to Witch Doctor Uzer'i in Feralas, along with word that Neeru is satisfied with the head.",h="With the shrunken head delivered in A Strange Request, Neeru Fireblade hands you the herbs and asks you to...",sec={{t="The Herbs Go Back",b="After A Strange Request, Neeru Fireblade gives you a pouch of herbs for Witch Doctor Uzer'i. You are also asked to tell Uzer'i that Neeru is satisfied with the shrunken head. The pouch is bound for Uzer'i in Feralas.",sp=0},{t="The Ritual Begins",b="Uzer'i says the herbs are just what is needed to prepare the muisek vessel, and hopes his latest incantations prove as powerful as he had hoped. He asks you to wait a moment while he performs the ritual and applies the herbs.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the herbs to Witch Doctor Uzer'i?",a="Neeru Fireblade, the one you brought the shrunken head to.",al={"where does this quest start","who gave the herbs"}},{q="Where do the herbs go?",a="To Witch Doctor Uzer'i in Feralas.",al={"what herbs are these","where do i take the herb pouch"}},{q="Was Neeru pleased with the shrunken head?",a="Yes. Neeru is satisfied with the head and asks you to say so to Uzer'i.",al={"did neeru like the head","neeru shrunken head trade"}}},kw={"feralas","herb pouch","muisek vessel","shrunken head","witch doctor uzer'i"},rel={"npc:witch-doctor-uzer-i","zone:feralas"},m={start="Neeru Fireblade",["end"]="Witch Doctor Uzer'i",level="45",faction="Horde",id=3122},src={"Return to Witch Doctor Uzer'i"}}
E["quest:3123"] = {t="quest",n="Testing the Vessel",z="feralas",s="Witch Doctor Uzer'i, after Return to Witch Doctor Uzer'i, calls this a test of the ritual Uzer'i performed and of your own abilities. You are given a vessel that can shrink and capture a creature, and sent to the Hinterlands to take ten wildkin with it, then bring them back to Uzer'i in Feralas.",h="Witch Doctor Uzer'i, after Return to Witch Doctor Uzer'i, calls this a test of the ritual Uzer'i performed...",sec={{t="A Vessel for the Hinterlands",b="Witch Doctor Uzer'i calls this a trial, both of the ritual just performed and of your own skills. The vessel you receive can reduce a creature in size and trap it within. You make for the Hinterlands and seek out wildkin, whose kind once belonged to Elune, the night elf goddess, as pets. Uzer'i names the vicious, primitive and savage owlbeasts as your quarry. Ten must fall, each shrunk into the vessel before its spirit slips away. Ten, and the vessel, go back to Uzer'i in Feralas.",sp=0},{t="Afterward",b="When a creature dies violently, Uzer'i explains, its muisek may get free and hunt for revenge. Shrinking the fallen, as you did, keeps the muisek from getting away, and Uzer'i now says it may be used at will.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives Testing the Vessel?",a="Witch Doctor Uzer'i, who hands you the vessel.",al={"quest giver testing the vessel","who gives testing the vessel"}},{q="Where are the wildkin?",a="Uzer'i sends you to the Hinterlands to look for them.",al={"where to find wildkin","wildkin location"}},{q="Which creatures are the targets?",a="The vicious, primitive or savage owlbeasts known as wildkin. Ten are wanted.",al={"which wildkin to kill","testing the vessel targets"}},{q="What is the link between the wildkin and Elune?",a="Uzer'i says wildkin used to be pets of Elune, the night elf goddess.",al={"wildkin elune lore","why wildkin"}},{q="What can the vessel do?",a="It lets you reduce a fallen creature in size and trap it, so its spirit cannot get away.",al={"how does muisek vessel work","vessel power"}},{q="What follows Testing the Vessel?",a="The chain goes on with Hippogryph Muisek.",al={"next quest testing the vessel","what comes after testing the vessel"}}},kw={"elune","feralas","hinterlands","muisek","owlbeast","uzer'i","vessel","wildkin"},rel={"npc:witch-doctor-uzer-i","zone:hinterlands","zone:feralas","topic:elune","quest:3122"},m={start="Witch Doctor Uzer'i",["end"]="Witch Doctor Uzer'i",level="47",faction="Horde",id=3123},src={"Testing the Vessel (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3124"] = {t="quest",n="Hippogryph Muisek",z="feralas",s="After your trials with the muisek vessel, Witch Doctor Uzer'i asks you to deal with a different creature. Frayfeather hippogryphs in the High Wilderness are to be slain and shrunk into the vessel at once, so that their muisek is kept.",h="After your trials with the muisek vessel, Witch Doctor Uzer'i asks you to deal with a different creature.",sec={{t="Loyal Companions",b="Witch Doctor Uzer'i has judged you trustworthy and gifted with the vessel, and now wants the spirit of a different creature. Hippogryphs are old companions of the night elves, and their spirits are loyal and steadfast. Ten Frayfeather hippogryphs of any kind are to be killed, each shrunk and captured quickly with the vessel so that its muisek is preserved. Uzer'i places them in the High Wilderness, southward from the camp.",sp=0},{t="Uzer'i's Warning",b="Uzer'i says that if the muisek of a slain animal is allowed to escape, it could take the shape of a still greater creature, and then no peace would be had from its revenge. Uzer'i calls the job dangerous and says you have again done it well.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to capture hippogryphs?",a="Witch Doctor Uzer'i. You come to this step after Testing the Vessel.",al={"hippogryph muisek quest giver","who gives hippogryph muisek","where to get hippogryph muisek"}},{q="Where are the Frayfeather hippogryphs found?",a="They are in the High Wilderness, which Uzer'i places to the south of the camp.",al={"where are frayfeather hippogryphs","hippogryph location feralas","where to find hippogryphs in feralas"}},{q="Why does Witch Doctor Uzer'i want hippogryph spirits?",a="Uzer'i speaks of hippogryphs as old companions of the night elves, with loyal and steadfast spirits. The aim is for their muisek to be preserved.",al={"why hippogryphs","why capture hippogryph muisek","uzeri hippogryph reasoning"}},{q="How is the muisek captured?",a="Kill a Frayfeather hippogryph, then quickly shrink and capture it with the muisek vessel. Ten are wanted, of any type.",al={"how to use muisek vessel","how to get hippogryph muisek","capturing frayfeather muisek"}},{q="What step comes before this in the chain?",a="Testing the Vessel, where you proved yourself trustworthy and able to use the muisek vessel.",al={"hippogryph muisek prerequisite","previous quest hippogryph muisek","prereq for hippogryph muisek"}}},kw={"feralas","frayfeather","high wilderness","hippogryph muisek","muisek vessel","witch doctor uzer'i"},rel={"npc:witch-doctor-uzer-i","subzone:high-wilderness","zone:feralas","quest:3123"},m={start="Witch Doctor Uzer'i",["end"]="Witch Doctor Uzer'i",level="47",faction="Horde",id=3124},src={"Hippogryph Muisek (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3125"] = {t="quest",n="Faerie Dragon Muisek",z="feralas",s="After the hippogryph spirits, Witch Doctor Uzer'i wants the spirit of a faerie dragon next. You are sent west to hunt sprite darters and sprite dragons and capture what makes them strong.",h="After the hippogryph spirits, Witch Doctor Uzer'i wants the spirit of a faerie dragon next.",sec={{t="Fragile Looks, Strong Spirit",b="Uzer'i points out that faerie dragons seem delicate, yet their spirit is the real prize. They have been allies to the night elves, and Uzer'i wants the Horde to share in that strength. Uzer'i gives you a Muisek Vessel and sends you west to slay eight sprite darters or sprite dragons, then shrink and capture each fallen faerie dragon with it.",sp=0},{t="Back at Uzer'i's Side",b="When you return with the captured spirits, Uzer'i thanks you and says the faerie dragons' spiritual power is now there for the Horde to draw on. Uzer'i also hopes you will agree to one more job.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Witch Doctor Uzer'i want faerie dragon spirits?",a="Uzer'i says faerie dragons look fragile but hold a powerful spirit, and that they have been allies to the night elves. Uzer'i wants the Horde to benefit from that strength as well.",al={"why faerie dragons","faerie dragon muisek purpose","why kill sprite darters"}},{q="Where can the faerie dragons be found?",a="Uzer'i says they lie west of where Uzer'i stands.",al={"where are sprite darters","sprite darter location","faerie dragon location feralas"}},{q="What creatures provide this muisek?",a="Sprite darters and sprite dragons. Eight of them need to be killed and captured.",al={"which mobs for muisek","what do i kill for faerie dragon muisek","faerie dragon muisek targets"}},{q="What must be done to the fallen creatures?",a="The Muisek Vessel is used on each fallen faerie dragon to shrink it and capture its muisek.",al={"how to get faerie dragon muisek","how does muisek vessel work","capturing muisek"}},{q="Where does this step fit among Uzer'i's requests?",a="It comes after Hippogryph Muisek, and Treant Muisek is the step that follows it.",al={"what quest comes before this","muisek chain order","what is next after faerie dragon muisek"}}},kw={"faerie dragon muisek","feralas","hippogryph muisek","horde","muisek vessel","sprite darter","sprite dragon","treant muisek","witch doctor uzer'i"},rel={"npc:witch-doctor-uzer-i","quest:3126","npc:sprite-darter","topic:horde","zone:feralas"},m={start="Witch Doctor Uzer'i",["end"]="Witch Doctor Uzer'i",level="45",id=3125},src={"Classic quest text: Faerie Dragon Muisek"}}
E["quest:3126"] = {t="quest",n="Treant Muisek",z="feralas",s="Witch Doctor Uzer'i's next target is the wandering forest walkers, treants that slowly roam the forest. After the faerie dragons, you are sent to find three of them.",h="Witch Doctor Uzer'i's next target is the wandering forest walkers, treants that slowly roam the forest.",sec={{t="Slow Protectors",b="Uzer'i says the night elves have recruited treants as allies in their fight against the Horde. They move slowly, but Uzer'i calls their role as protectors undeniable, and plans to turn that power to the Horde's own benefit.",sp=0},{t="Three Forest Walkers",b="Uzer'i wants three wandering forest walkers found and killed, then each fallen treant shrunk and captured with the Muisek Vessel.",sp=0},{t="Uzer'i's Verdict",b="On your return Uzer'i thanks you and remarks that the collection of muisek is nearly complete.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends adventurers after the treants?",a="Witch Doctor Uzer'i, who asks for this right after the faerie dragons.",al={"who gives treant muisek","treant muisek quest giver","uzeri treant quest"}},{q="Why does Witch Doctor Uzer'i want treant muisek?",a="Uzer'i says the night elves have recruited treants as allies in their fight against the Horde, and wants to use their protective power for the Horde's own benefit.",al={"why kill forest walkers","why treant muisek","uzeri treant motive"}},{q="What creatures must be found for Treant Muisek?",a="Wandering forest walkers, which roam the forest. Three of them are needed.",al={"which treants to kill","wandering forest walkers","treant muisek targets"}},{q="How are the treants captured?",a="After a wandering forest walker falls, the Muisek Vessel is used to shrink it and capture it.",al={"how to use muisek vessel","capturing forest walkers","shrink treants"}},{q="Where does Treant Muisek fit among Uzer'i's requests?",a="It follows Faerie Dragon Muisek, and Mountain Giant Muisek comes after it.",al={"treant muisek chain","what comes after faerie dragon muisek","next quest after treant muisek"}}},kw={"feralas","muisek vessel","treant muisek","treants","uzer'i","wandering forest walker"},rel={"npc:witch-doctor-uzer-i","quest:3125","quest:3127","zone:feralas","topic:horde"},m={start="Witch Doctor Uzer'i",["end"]="Witch Doctor Uzer'i",level="50",id=3126},src={"Classic quest text: Treant Muisek"}}
E["quest:3127"] = {t="quest",n="Mountain Giant Muisek",z="feralas",s="Witch Doctor Uzer'i calls this the last job and sends you northwest to find the final enemy: mountain giants, whose size and strength Uzer'i is eager to harness.",h="Witch Doctor Uzer'i calls this the last job and sends you northwest to find the final enemy: mountain giants...",sec={{t="Giants of the Rocky Ground",b="In Uzer'i's telling, the mountain giants came down out of the mountains to help the night elves once the Burning Legion arrived in the world. They are easy to know by their sheer size and the tremors underfoot on their rocky ground. Uzer'i is eager to harness power on that scale. Uzer'i wants seven Land Walkers or Cliff Giants brought down, each one shrunk and captured with the Muisek Vessel.",sp=0},{t="Uzer'i's Boast",b="When you return, Uzer'i speaks of the possibilities of what has now been gathered. With the materials you collected along the way, Uzer'i claims to be able to trap the spirits of these creatures permanently into whatever Uzer'i wishes.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who asks for the mountain giants' muisek?",a="Witch Doctor Uzer'i, who calls it the last request of you.",al={"quest giver","who gives mountain giant muisek","uzeri quest"}},{q="Where are the mountain giants located?",a="Uzer'i sends you to travel northwest to find them on rocky terrain.",al={"mountain giant location","where are land walkers","cliff giant location"}},{q="Why are mountain giants here?",a="By Uzer'i's account, they came down from the mountains to help the night elves once the Burning Legion arrived in the world.",al={"why are giants here","mountain giant lore feralas"}},{q="Which creatures provide the required muisek?",a="Land Walkers and Cliff Giants. Seven are needed, and the Muisek Vessel shrinks and captures each fallen one.",al={"what do i kill for muisek","which giants count"}},{q="What comes before this in the sequence?",a="It follows Treant Muisek, and Weapons of Spirit is listed after it.",al={"previous quest","muisek chain order"}}},kw={"burning legion","cliff giant","feralas","land walker","mountain giant muisek","muisek vessel","treant muisek","witch doctor uzer'i"},rel={"npc:witch-doctor-uzer-i","quest:3126","quest:3129","zone:feralas","topic:burning-legion"},m={start="Witch Doctor Uzer'i",["end"]="Witch Doctor Uzer'i",level="50",id=3127},src={"Classic quest text: Mountain Giant Muisek"}}
E["quest:3128"] = {t="quest",n="Natural Materials",z="feralas",s="Witch Doctor Uzer'i in Camp Mojache needs materials to complete an endeavor, to be gathered alongside the other trials: splintered logs, encrusted minerals, resilient sinew and metallic fragments, taken from treants, mountain giants, faerie dragons, owlbeasts and hippogryphs.",h="Witch Doctor Uzer'i in Camp Mojache needs materials to complete an endeavor, to be gathered alongside the...",sec={{t="Gathering for the Witch Doctor",b="After you return to Witch Doctor Uzer'i, a further list of materials awaits, to be collected alongside the other trials. Two splintered logs are needed from a Feralas treant. Six pieces of encrusted minerals are found on mountain giants and faerie dragons, westward. Twenty pieces of resilient sinew come from owlbeasts in the Hinterlands or hippogryphs in Feralas. A large amount of metallic fragments, forty in all, can come from any of these creatures.",sp=0},{t="Uzer'i's Verdict",b="When the materials are brought back, Uzer'i is pleased. Joined with the muisek, they should yield just the results that have been wanted.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who requests these natural materials?",a="Witch Doctor Uzer'i in Camp Mojache.",al={"who gives natural materials","natural materials quest giver","where to start natural materials"}},{q="What creatures hold the splintered logs?",a="A treant of Feralas; two splintered logs are needed.",al={"where to get splintered logs","who drops splintered log","splintered log source"}},{q="Where can encrusted minerals be gathered?",a="Mountain giants and faerie dragons, westward, carry them; six are needed.",al={"how to get encrusted minerals","encrusted minerals source","who drops encrusted minerals"}},{q="Which beasts provide the resilient sinew?",a="The owlbeasts of the Hinterlands, or the hippogryphs of Feralas; twenty pieces are needed.",al={"resilient sinew drop","where to find resilient sinew","who has resilient sinew"}},{q="Where do metallic fragments come from?",a="Forty come from any of the creatures named: treants, mountain giants, faerie dragons, owlbeasts and hippogryphs.",al={"metallic fragments source","how to get metallic fragments","who drops metallic fragments"}},{q="What came before this request?",a="This request follows Return to Witch Doctor Uzer'i.",al={"natural materials prerequisite","previous quest natural materials","what leads to natural materials"}}},kw={"camp mojache","encrusted minerals","feralas","metallic fragments","muisek","natural materials","resilient sinew","splintered log","the hinterlands","witch doctor uzer'i"},rel={"npc:witch-doctor-uzer-i","subzone:camp-mojache","zone:feralas","quest:3122","zone:hinterlands"},m={start="Witch Doctor Uzer'i",["end"]="Witch Doctor Uzer'i",level="50",faction="Horde",id=3128},src={"Natural Materials"}}
E["quest:3129"] = {t="quest",n="Weapons of Spirit",z="feralas",s="Witch Doctor Uzer'i now has everything needed and the spirits you captured. Binding them into weapons is hard work, so Uzer'i asks you to wait a moment while the preparations are made.",h="Witch Doctor Uzer'i now has everything needed and the spirits you captured.",sec={{t="A Moment's Patience",b="Uzer'i admits that imbuing weapons with muisek is hard going. Now holding all the materials needed, along with the spirits you captured, Uzer'i can begin, and asks you to wait while the weapons are prepared.",sp=0},{t="When the Wait Ends",b="Uzer'i returns and lets you choose from the weapons, telling you the spirits of the captured creatures are sealed into them for good. Their energy can now be wielded as your own.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is behind Weapons of Spirit?",a="Witch Doctor Uzer'i, the same one who sent you after the muisek, and it comes after Mountain Giant Muisek.",al={"who gives weapons of spirit","weapons of spirit quest giver","uzeri quest"}},{q="What does Witch Doctor Uzer'i do during this step?",a="Uzer'i works at imbuing the captured muisek into weapons, a process called difficult, and asks you to wait while the preparations are made.",al={"what happens in weapons of spirit","what does uzeri do"}},{q="What is needed before Uzer'i can begin?",a="Uzer'i says the needed materials are gathered and the spirits you captured are in hand, so the work can start.",al={"requirements for weapons of spirit","prerequisites for weapons of spirit"}}},kw={"feralas","muisek","spirit weapons","weapons of spirit","witch doctor uzer'i"},rel={"npc:witch-doctor-uzer-i","quest:3127","zone:feralas"},m={start="Witch Doctor Uzer'i",["end"]="Witch Doctor Uzer'i",level="50",id=3129},src={"Classic quest text: Weapons of Spirit"}}
E["quest:3130"] = {t="quest",n="Against the Hatecrest",z="feralas",s="Having reported back, you are sent on by General Shandris Feathermoon to Latronicus Moonspear, the general's second, in Feathermoon Stronghold. Shandris would like to commit a full force against the naga but will not leave the stronghold open to the Horde, or worse.",h="Having reported back, you are sent on by General Shandris Feathermoon to Latronicus Moonspear, the general's...",sec={{t="Shandris Weighs the Risk",b="General Shandris Feathermoon sends you on to Latronicus Moonspear, the general's second, who has been keeping a close watch on the naga forces so far. Shandris will assess the wider situation with the naga here. Much as a full force against them is wanted, leaving the stronghold open to a direct attack from the Horde, or something worse, seems less than ideal. Latronicus awaits you in Feathermoon Stronghold.",sp=0},{t="What Latronicus Intends",b="Latronicus Moonspear says the General has charged Latronicus with dealing with the naga head-on. The plan has two parts: weaken them in number and in command, and find out what they are doing in the ruins. With your help, their presence can be countered while the stronghold stays secure.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Shandris Feathermoon send you to Latronicus?",a="Shandris will not commit a full force against the naga if that would leave Feathermoon Stronghold exposed to the Horde, or to something worse. Instead the general points you to the second, Latronicus, who has been watching the naga.",al={"why talk to latronicus","why latronicus moonspear","feathermoon referral"}},{q="Where is Latronicus Moonspear located?",a="In Feathermoon Stronghold, where Shandris sends you to report to him.",al={"latronicus location","where is latronicus","find latronicus moonspear"}},{q="What came before this assignment?",a="Return to Feathermoon Stronghold, after which Shandris sends you on to Latronicus.",al={"against the hatecrest prerequisite","previous quest","hatecrest chain start"}}},kw={"against the hatecrest","feathermoon stronghold","feralas","hatecrest","horde","latronicus moonspear","naga","shandris feathermoon"},rel={"npc:shandris-feathermoon","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","quest:2867","quest:2869","topic:naga","topic:horde","zone:feralas"},m={start="Shandris Feathermoon",["end"]="Latronicus Moonspear",level="43",faction="Alliance",id=3130},src={"Against the Hatecrest"}}
E["quest:3445"] = {t="quest",n="The Sunken Temple",z="feralas",s="Angelas Moonbreeze tells of the Sunken Temple, a place buried far underground, put there by powers greater than any Angelas has seen. To learn more, you are pointed to a goblin named Marvon Rivetseeker, last known to be in Tanaris.",h="Angelas Moonbreeze tells of the Sunken Temple, a place buried far underground, put there by powers greater...",sec={{t="A Place Banished Below",b="Angelas Moonbreeze speaks of a place sunk deep below the earth's surface, put there by forces mightier than any Angelas has seen: the Sunken Temple. For more, look for the goblin Marvon Rivetseeker, who, like Angelas and Troyas, has made a study of ancient sites across the world. Marvon left home in Ratchet to look into the troll ruins of Tanaris, and word of him has been missing for some time.",sp=0},{t="What Marvon Says",b="When you find Marvon Rivetseeker, he says he has seen the Sunken Temple with his own eyes and asks whether you would like to hear more. He takes you for the adventurous type and says he knows things that may intrigue you.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who starts the search for the Sunken Temple?",a="Angelas Moonbreeze, who speaks of a place sunk deep below the earth, the Sunken Temple, put there by forces mightier than any Angelas has seen.",al={"sunken temple quest giver","who gives the sunken temple","angelas moonbreeze"}},{q="Who is Marvon Rivetseeker?",a="A goblin who, like Angelas and Troyas, has made a study of ancient sites across the world.",al={"marvon rivetseeker","where is marvon rivetseeker","who is marvon"}},{q="Where did Marvon Rivetseeker go?",a="Last word has him leaving Ratchet, his home, for Tanaris and its troll ruins. Nobody has heard from him in some time.",al={"marvon location","where to find marvon","marvon tanaris"}}},kw={"angelas moonbreeze","feralas","marvon rivetseeker","ratchet","sunken temple","tanaris","troll ruins"},rel={"quest:3444","zone:feralas","zone:tanaris","subzone:ratchet"},m={start="Angelas Moonbreeze",["end"]="Marvon Rivetseeker",level="51",faction="Alliance",id=3445},src={"The Sunken Temple (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:3567"] = {t="quest",n="To the Top",z="feralas",s="Marli Wishrunner can send you up to see the sights from one of the twin colossals of Feralas, with a warning attached: the trip goes only one way.",h="Marli Wishrunner can send you up to see the sights from one of the twin colossals of Feralas, with a warning...",sec={{t="One Way Up",b="Marli Wishrunner asks whether you would like to see the view from the top of one of the twin colossals, and can send you there. Marli adds a word of caution: think about how you will get down, because this is a one-way trip.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who can send you to the top of a colossal?",a="Marli Wishrunner can send you up to a view from one of the twin colossals.",al={"who gives to the top","to the top quest giver","marli wishrunner"}},{q="Where does this journey lead?",a="To the top of one of the twin colossals.",al={"where does marli send you","destination","to the top location"}},{q="Does Marli provide a way back down?",a="No. Marli warns that it is a one-way trip, so you should think about how you will get down.",al={"how do i get down","is there a return trip","way down from twin colossals"}}},kw={"colossals","feralas","marli wishrunner","summit","to the top","twin colossals"},rel={"subzone:twin-colossals","zone:feralas"},m={start="Marli Wishrunner",["end"]="Marli Wishrunner",level="25",id=3567},src={"To the Top"}}
E["quest:3841"] = {t="quest",n="An Orphan Looking For a Home",z="feralas",s="After Doling Justice, Kindal Moonweaver greets you on your return from Darnassus with news: a nest full of eggs was saved, though the mother died. Kindal offers you one of the eggs as a pet and sends you on to Quentin, who waits by the race tracks in the Shimmering Flats of Thousand Needles.",h="After Doling Justice, Kindal Moonweaver greets you on your return from Darnassus with news: a nest full of...",sec={{t="A Nest Without a Mother",b="Kindal Moonweaver is glad to see you back from Darnassus and reports good progress while you were away. A nest full of eggs was saved, though the mother died before help reached her. The eggs look set to hatch soon, so they will need a good keeper, and Kindal offers you one as a pet. If you are truly interested, carry an egg to the race tracks in the Shimmering Flats, where Quentin will tell you more.",sp=0},{t="Quentin at the Flats",b="Quentin is in Thousand Needles, and asks you not to be fooled by the location: the races are not why Quentin is there. Quentin is investigating how salvageable the land is, hoping to replenish it with new, fertile soil and perhaps find a nearby water source. Quentin also finds the change between Feralas and Thousand Needles odd, and says strange magic was afoot when it happened.",sp=0},{t="What Quentin Makes of the Egg",b="Quentin names it a sprite darter egg, near maturation and in remarkably good condition, and is amazed that you found one. Such creatures are rarely seen in Feralas these days; Quentin has heard that poachers were about, hunting them to capture or kill them, for assorted reasons. Quentin thinks it a shame, for they are beautiful when grown, and asks how you came across such a find.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where did the egg come from?",a="Kindal Moonweaver and others saved a nest full of eggs while you were in Darnassus. The mother had died before they reached her.",al={"where did the egg come from","egg origin","sprite darter egg lore"}},{q="Where can Quentin be found?",a="At the race tracks in the Shimmering Flats of Thousand Needles.",al={"quentin location","where is quentin","quentin shimmering flats"}},{q="Why is Quentin at the Shimmering Flats?",a="Not for the races. Quentin is investigating how salvageable the land is, hoping to bring new, fertile soil to the area and perhaps find a water source nearby.",al={"why is quentin at the raceway","what is quentin doing","quentin research"}}},kw={"egg","feralas","kindal moonweaver","quentin","shimmering flats","sprite darter","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:kindal-moonweaver","quest:3842","npc:sprite-darter","subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:feralas","zone:thousandneedles","quest:2972","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Kindal Moonweaver",["end"]="Quentin",level="47",faction="Alliance",id=3841},src={"An Orphan Looking For a Home"}}
E["quest:3842"] = {t="quest",n="A Short Incubation",z="feralas",s="Quentin, waiting in Thousand Needles, hears that the Moonweavers gave you the sprite darter egg. The egg looks almost ready to hatch, so Quentin wants to be sure it is healthy and undamaged, and asks you for two elixirs of fortitude.",h="Quentin, waiting in Thousand Needles, hears that the Moonweavers gave you the sprite darter egg.",sec={{t="Protecting the Egg",b="Quentin finds it intriguing that the Moonweavers looked after the egg and thinks both are quite capable. Since the egg was a gift to you, it is yours to be responsible for as long as you wish. It appears almost ready to hatch, but it should first be checked for health and damage. A small spell to protect it will do the job, and Quentin has every component on hand except two elixirs of fortitude. Quentin admits to growing tempted by the races while waiting, and will return the egg for you to keep once its health is known.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the elixirs?",a="Quentin, who is in Thousand Needles by the Mirage Raceway, asks for two elixirs of fortitude.",al={"who gives this quest","quest giver","quentin location"}},{q="What happened right before this?",a="You brought the egg to Quentin in An Orphan Looking For a Home. It was a gift from the Moonweavers.",al={"previous quest","where did the egg come from","pre-req"}},{q="What is needed to finish the spell?",a="Two elixirs of fortitude. Quentin already has the other components with him.",al={"what do i need to bring","required items","elixirs needed"}},{q="Why does Quentin want the elixirs?",a="The egg is almost ready to hatch, and Quentin wants it to be healthy and undamaged. The elixirs go into a small spell to protect it.",al={"why elixir of fortitude","purpose of the potions"}}},ang={["profession:Alchemy"]="An alchemist can brew the elixirs of fortitude Quentin asks for."},kw={"elixir of fortitude","feralas","mirage raceway","moonweavers","quentin","sprite darter egg","thousand needles"},rel={"quest:3841","quest:3843","npc:sprite-darter","subzone:mirage-raceway","zone:thousandneedles","zone:feralas"},m={start="Quentin",["end"]="Quentin",level="47",faction="Alliance",id=3842},src={"A Short Incubation"}}
E["quest:3843"] = {t="quest",n="The Newest Member of the Family",z="feralas",s="After A Short Incubation, Quentin calls the egg a magnificent specimen and sends you to Aerie Peak in the Hinterlands, to a dwarf named Agnar Beastamer. The egg is fragile and only an hour remains to find Agnar before the hatchling inside dies.",h="After A Short Incubation, Quentin calls the egg a magnificent specimen and sends you to Aerie Peak in the...",sec={{t="Hurry to Aerie Peak",b="Quentin judges the sprite darter egg a magnificent specimen; if it survives, it will make a healthy pet. One last thing is advised: go to Aerie Peak in the Hinterlands and speak to the dwarf Agnar Beastamer, a master animal handler who can guide the final steps of incubation. The egg is fragile and cannot manage long without proper care: the hatchling inside dies if an hour goes by before you find Agnar. Agnar lives in Wildhammer Keep.",sp=0},{t="Agnar's Verdict",b="Agnar has not seen such a creature in ages, and names it a faerie dragon of the sprite darter kind. To let the little one hatch and grow strong, food will be needed, and Agnar is glad you arrived in time.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Agnar Beastamer?",a="Quentin, who follows up A Short Incubation by sending you with the fragile egg to Aerie Peak in the Hinterlands.",al={"quest giver","who starts the newest member of the family","egg quest giver"}},{q="Who must receive the egg?",a="Agnar Beastamer, a dwarf and master animal handler at Aerie Peak in the Hinterlands. Agnar lives in Wildhammer Keep.",al={"where do I take the egg","who is agnar beastamer","who gets the egg"}},{q="How much time is there to deliver the egg?",a="One hour. If the hatchling inside the egg is not brought to Agnar in that time, it dies.",al={"egg time limit","how long do I have","timer on the egg"}},{q="Where does this step fit in the chain?",a="It follows A Short Incubation, and hands the egg over to Agnar Beastamer at Aerie Peak.",al={"quest chain","what comes next","chain progression"}}},kw={"aerie peak","agnar beastamer","feralas","fragile egg","hinterlands","quentin","sprite darter"},rel={"quest:3842","quest:4297","npc:sprite-darter","zone:hinterlands","zone:feralas"},m={start="Quentin",["end"]="Agnar Beastamer",level="47",faction="Alliance",id=3843},src={"The Newest Member of the Family"}}
E["quest:4041"] = {t="quest",n="The Videre Elixir",z="feralas",s="Gregan Brewspewer will make you a Videre Elixir, but only once an Evoroot is brought. Gregan also claims a great many things are known to him about herbs and alchemy.",h="Gregan Brewspewer will make you a Videre Elixir, but only once an Evoroot is brought.",sec={{t="An Evoroot for the Brewer",b="Gregan Brewspewer can make you a Videre Elixir as soon as an Evoroot is put in hand. Meanwhile Gregan boasts of knowing a great many things about herbs and alchemy, and begins a story about turning the cheese meant for lunch into gold, only to ask where you are going when you walk off. Gregan is the one to ask about where an Evoroot can be found.",sp=0},{t="When the Evoroot Arrives",b="When you come back with the Evoroot, Gregan greets you by saying you pulled a fast one on old Miblon.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who brews the Videre Elixir?",a="Gregan Brewspewer, once you bring an Evoroot.",al={"who gives the videre elixir","where do i get videre elixir"}},{q="What ingredient is required to make the elixir?",a="An Evoroot. Gregan can tell you where to find one.",al={"videre elixir ingredients","what does gregan need"}},{q="What does Gregan Brewspewer boast about?",a="Gregan boasts of knowing a great many things about herbs and alchemy, and starts a story about turning a lunchtime cheese into gold.",al={"gregan brewspewer boasts","gregan herbs and alchemy"}}},kw={"alchemy","evoroot","feralas","gregan brewspewer","miblon","videre elixir"},rel={"zone:feralas"},m={start="Gregan Brewspewer",["end"]="Gregan Brewspewer",level="52",id=4041},src={"The Videre Elixir (2)"}}
E["quest:4120"] = {t="quest",n="The Strength of Corruption",z="feralas",s="Talo Thornhoof, a hunter at Camp Mojache in Feralas, believes knowing an enemy well can turn a battle. Talo sends you to Felwood, north of Ashenvale, to face the fel-tainted bears and wolves and learn whether they have truly grown stronger.",h="Talo Thornhoof, a hunter at Camp Mojache in Feralas, believes knowing an enemy well can turn a battle.",sec={{t="Know Your Enemy",b="Talo Thornhoof is a hunter who strives to copy the strengths seen in opponents, and believes simply knowing an enemy well can turn a battle your way. Felwood lies north of Ashenvale, where a substance called fel has tainted the creatures. Talo thinks the bears and wolves there, driven mad by it, have also grown even stronger. Angerclaw grizzlies and Felpaw ravagers are the ones to face, twelve of each. Fel-touched things give off a strange green glow, which Talo senses is evil yet very powerful.",sp=0},{t="What Talo Hears",b="After your account of the beasts, Talo concludes they show a mindless ferocity, and warns you to stay alert and learn more of the corruption, since an enemy should always be known.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Felwood?",a="Talo Thornhoof, a hunter at Camp Mojache in Feralas.",al={"quest giver","who gives the strength of corruption","talo thornhoof location"}},{q="Why does Talo Thornhoof want the beasts of Felwood faced?",a="Talo believes that knowing an enemy well can turn a battle, and wants you to learn for yourself whether the fel-tainted creatures are truly as strong as believed.",al={"why kill the bears and wolves","purpose of the strength of corruption","talo thornhoof motive"}},{q="Which creatures are targeted in Felwood?",a="Angerclaw grizzlies and Felpaw ravagers in Felwood, twelve of each.",al={"which beasts","targets in felwood","what monsters to fight"}},{q="What does Talo say about fel?",a="Everything touched by the fel gives off a strange green glow. Talo senses it is evil but also very powerful.",al={"what is the taint","green glow felwood","what is fel"}}},kw={"angerclaw grizzly","camp mojache","fel corruption","felpaw ravager","felwood","feralas","talo thornhoof"},rel={"subzone:camp-mojache","zone:feralas","zone:felwood","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Talo Thornhoof",["end"]="Talo Thornhoof",level="52",faction="Horde",id=4120},src={"The Strength of Corruption"}}
E["quest:4124"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Courier",z="feralas",s="Latronicus Moonspear in Feathermoon Stronghold says a courier and the parcels he carried went missing about a week ago. The stronghold's own searches found nothing, so the courier is declared missing in action, and you are sent to Ginro Hearthkindle, who is seeking help.",h="Latronicus Moonspear in Feathermoon Stronghold says a courier and the parcels he carried went missing about a...",sec={{t="A Courier Gone Missing",b="Latronicus Moonspear has reached an impasse. A courier has been missing for about a week along with the parcels he was carrying, and the stronghold's own searches have been fruitless, so Latronicus has declared him missing in action. An associate, Ginro Hearthkindle, is looking for help with the matter and should be in Feathermoon Stronghold, perhaps in his quarters. Latronicus asks that you speak with Ginro, if you have time and means to spare.",sp=0},{t="Ginro's Weary Search",b="Ginro knows that Latronicus, whom Ginro calls Latro, sent you. Ginro thinks it a lost cause, yet takes whatever help is offered, and longs to put the matter to rest. Each day Ginro heads out into Feralas to look for signs of Raschal, and each night comes back with only gnoll teeth and disappointment.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who has gone missing?",a="A courier who vanished about a week ago along with the parcels he carried. The stronghold's searches found nothing, and he has been declared missing in action.",al={"who is the courier","who went missing","missing courier name"}},{q="Where can Ginro Hearthkindle be found?",a="In Feathermoon Stronghold, perhaps in his quarters.",al={"ginro hearthkindle location","where is ginro","find ginro"}},{q="Who starts the search for the courier?",a="Latronicus Moonspear, in Feathermoon Stronghold, sends you to Ginro Hearthkindle to help.",al={"who gives the missing courier","latronicus moonspear quest","who starts missing courier"}}},kw={"courier","feathermoon stronghold","feralas","ginro hearthkindle","gnolls","latronicus moonspear","parcels","raschal"},rel={"subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","zone:feralas","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Latronicus Moonspear",["end"]="Ginro Hearthkindle",level="43",faction="Alliance",id=4124},src={"The Missing Courier"}}
E["quest:4125"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Courier",z="feralas",s="Ginro Hearthkindle tells you the courier, Raschal, set out for Thalanaar about a week ago, planning to row down the coast. Ginro could not find the boat and asks you to look for it along the coast of Feralas, in case it holds a clue to where Raschal is.",h="Ginro Hearthkindle tells you the courier, Raschal, set out for Thalanaar about a week ago, planning to row...",sec={{t="A Route Down the Coast",b="About a week ago Raschal set out for Thalanaar. Raschal knows Feralas well and has been with the expeditionary forces since General Feathermoon led them here. Ginro's understanding is that Raschal meant to go by row boat down the coast and cross southern Feralas, avoiding the Horde camp. Ginro could not find the boat, which may be hidden or sunk, and asks you to look for it along the coast of Feralas, since it might hold a clue to where Raschal is. On the mainland, the Forgotten Coast stretches south from the jetty.",sp=0},{t="At the Shore",b="Through slightly muddy water you spot a wrecked row boat, riddled with gaping holes along one side and shredded nearly down to its wooden frame. Whatever broke it probably tried to split it in half. A small crest of Feathermoon Stronghold is painted on the other side, and in the mud at the boat's base something metallic glints.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Raschal?",a="The courier who went missing. Raschal knows Feralas well and has been with the expeditionary forces since General Feathermoon led them here.",al={"who is raschal","missing courier identity","who went missing"}},{q="Where was Raschal heading?",a="To Thalanaar. Raschal planned to go by boat down the coast, then over southern Feralas, to steer clear of the Horde camp.",al={"raschal destination","where was he going","courier route"}},{q="How long has Raschal been missing?",a="About a week, since setting out for Thalanaar.",al={"when did raschal leave","how long gone"}},{q="Where did this search begin?",a="This step follows the earlier The Missing Courier, in which you spoke with Ginro Hearthkindle.",al={"previous step","how did this quest start"}}},kw={"feathermoon stronghold","feralas","forgotten coast","ginro hearthkindle","raschal","rowboat","thalanaar"},rel={"quest:4124","quest:4127","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","subzone:forgotten-coast","subzone:thalanaar","zone:feralas","topic:horde"},m={start="Ginro Hearthkindle",["end"]="Wrecked Row Boat",level="43",faction="Alliance",id=4125},src={"The Missing Courier (2)"}}
E["quest:4127"] = {t="quest",n="Boat Wreckage",z="feralas",s="Beside a wrecked row boat in the water you find a well-cared-for knife in the mud. Ginro Hearthkindle in Feathermoon Stronghold wants any clue you find brought back, and a feeling creeps over you that something else shares the water.",h="Beside a wrecked row boat in the water you find a well-cared-for knife in the mud.",sec={{t="A Knife in the Mud",b="Feeling along the mud near the wrecked boat, your fingertips brush the grip of a knife that looks well cared for. Whoever was on the boat may have lost it, and the large chunk missing from the boat might have a part in the loss. You take the knife, recalling that Ginro Hearthkindle in Feathermoon Stronghold asked you to bring any clue you found back to him, yet the feeling creeps over you that something else shares the water.",sp=0},{t="A Question for You",b="Ginro believes the knife is Raschal's and asks whether you really found it on the bottom with his boat. The knife alone may not be enough to connect the boat to Raschal's disappearance, but there is an unconventional option for learning more, and Ginro asks whether you have ever heard of psychometry.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the knife discovered?",a="In the mud beside the wrecked row boat in the water off the coast.",al={"knife location","where is discarded knife","where do i find the knife"}},{q="Who wants the clue brought back?",a="Ginro Hearthkindle in Feathermoon Stronghold, who wanted you to return with any clue you found.",al={"who sent me to boat","who wants the knife","boat wreckage turn in"}},{q="What sort of knife is it?",a="A well-cared-for one, in the mud by the wrecked boat. Whoever was on the boat may have lost it.",al={"who owns the knife","whose blade is it"}},{q="What comes directly before investigating the wreckage?",a="It follows the second part of The Missing Courier, in which you were asked to find the courier's boat.",al={"previous quest","what led to boat wreckage"}}},kw={"boat wreckage","discarded knife","feathermoon stronghold","feralas","ginro hearthkindle","missing courier","raschal","row boat"},rel={"quest:4125","quest:4129","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","zone:feralas"},m={start="Wrecked Row Boat",["end"]="Ginro Hearthkindle",level="44",faction="Alliance",id=4127},src={"Boat Wreckage"}}
E["quest:4129"] = {t="quest",n="The Knife Revealed",z="feralas",s="Ginro Hearthkindle sends you with the knife to Quintis Jonespyre, the Stronghold's resident druid, who can learn an object's past by touching it. Ginro says Quintis owes a Kalimdor Hold 'Em debt that this will clear.",h="Ginro Hearthkindle sends you with the knife to Quintis Jonespyre, the Stronghold's resident druid, who can...",sec={{t="A Druid's Debt",b="After Boat Wreckage, Ginro Hearthkindle sends you with the knife to Quintis Jonespyre, the resident druid of Feathermoon Stronghold, who has unusual skills. One is psychometry, learning an object's past just by touching it. Ginro will not say how it works, calling it magic Ginro does not and chooses not to understand, only that Ginro has seen it work. Quintis owes Ginro a Kalimdor Hold 'Em debt, which will be paid if Quintis works some magic on the knife. Quintis lives in a little tree-house in the Stronghold.",sp=0},{t="King of the Bad Beats",b="Quintis says the psychometric readings drain the psyche, much as the losses at Kalimdor Hold 'Em do, and the Stronghold calls Quintis the King of the Bad Beats: unlucky at cards, lucky at the secrets of nature. Quintis agrees to do it, hoping the knife brings the breakthrough needed to uncover Raschal's fate.",sp=0},{t="Before the Reading",b="Quintis thanks you, noting that psychometry is no exact art, but he has used it before to shed light on situations that others wrote off as lost causes. He expects the knife to give a glimpse of what happened to Raschal. It takes only a moment, though it is hard going for a caster, and Quintis asks you to bear with it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Quintis Jonespyre?",a="The Stronghold's resident druid, who lives in a little tree-house in Feathermoon Stronghold and has an unusual skill: psychometry.",al={"quintis","who is quint","druid in feathermoon"}},{q="What is psychometry?",a="Learning an object's past by touching it. Quintis says such readings take a toll on the mind.",al={"how does psychometry work","reading the knife","quintis psychometry"}},{q="Why does Quintis help with the knife?",a="Quintis owes Ginro Hearthkindle a Kalimdor Hold 'Em debt, which Ginro says will be paid if the knife is read. Quintis is also eager to find out Raschal's fate.",al={"why help quintis","ginro debt","kalimdor hold em"}},{q="Where does this happen in the investigation?",a="It follows Boat Wreckage, in which the knife was found.",al={"what quest is before this","what quest comes next","knife revealed chain"}}},kw={"discarded knife","feathermoon stronghold","ginro hearthkindle","kalimdor hold em","psychometry","quintis jonespyre","raschal"},rel={"quest:4127","quest:4130","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","zone:feralas"},m={start="Ginro Hearthkindle",["end"]="Quintis Jonespyre",level="44",faction="Alliance",id=4129},src={"The Knife Revealed"}}
E["quest:4130"] = {t="quest",n="Psychometric Reading",z="feralas",s="Quintis Jonespyre, still wobbly after reading the knife, passes on visions of Raschal and the Woodpaw gnolls and asks you to take them to Ginro Hearthkindle in Feathermoon Stronghold.",h="Quintis Jonespyre, still wobbly after reading the knife, passes on visions of Raschal and the Woodpaw gnolls...",sec={{t="What Quintis Saw",b="Quintis Jonespyre is still unsteady but has seen something useful. In the vision Raschal pulls two big leather backpacks off the boat, heads inland, and then goes back to the boat. Gnoll scalps appear, and Quintis thinks Raschal met Woodpaw gnolls. Raschal is very worried, almost terrified, and does not notice water elementals forming behind. There the images stop. Quintis must rest and asks you to tell Ginro, who needs to know.",sp=0},{t="Ginro's Answer",b="Ginro thanks you for carrying Quintis's visions. Raschal can handle a fight, and gnolls would not worry Raschal, let alone terrify. Even so, Ginro hopes you and your companions can act on this and make the breakthrough that is badly needed.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who has the vision to share?",a="Quintis Jonespyre, who is still wobbly after reading the knife and asks you to carry word of it to Ginro.",al={"who gives psychometric reading","quest giver psychometric reading"}},{q="What did Quintis see in his vision?",a="Raschal took two large leather backpacks from the boat inland and then returned to it. Quintis also saw gnoll scalps, took the gnolls to be Woodpaw, saw Raschal very worried, almost terrified, and saw water elementals forming behind him.",al={"what was quintis's vision","what happened to raschal vision"}},{q="Where does this report need to go?",a="To Ginro Hearthkindle in Feathermoon Stronghold.",al={"where do i deliver the vision","who do i talk to psychometric reading"}}},kw={"feathermoon stronghold","ginro hearthkindle","psychometric reading","quintis jonespyre","raschal","water elementals","woodpaw"},rel={"quest:4129","quest:4131","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","topic:gnoll","zone:feralas"},m={start="Quintis Jonespyre",["end"]="Ginro Hearthkindle",level="44",faction="Alliance",id=4130},src={"Psychometric Reading"}}
E["quest:4131"] = {t="quest",n="The Woodpaw Gnolls",z="feralas",s="After Quintis's vision, Ginro Hearthkindle sends you to search the camps of the Woodpaw gnolls in southern Feralas for evidence of the courier or the courier's belongings. Ginro doubts the gnolls were Raschal's undoing, but they are the best place to start.",h="After Quintis's vision, Ginro Hearthkindle sends you to search the camps of the Woodpaw gnolls in southern...",sec={{t="Where to Start Looking",b="Ginro Hearthkindle allows that the Woodpaw, whom Ginro puts in quotation marks as friends, may have done for Raschal in the end, though something tells Ginro otherwise. Still, they are the best place to start. Ginro has no clearer plan than searching their camps, and knows gnolls keep what they scavenge and fight over it, so they may have come across the backpacks Quintis mentioned. In past searches Ginro steered clear of open fighting, but with the vision to go on now says to rip into them. The camps lie in southern Feralas.",sp=0},{t="At the Camps",b="Two large leather backpacks are tacked to a nearby tree, and each carries a small insignia of Feathermoon Stronghold on its front. They are in the Lower Wilds.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is being searched for?",a="Raschal, the courier. Ginro Hearthkindle wants evidence of the courier or the courier's belongings.",al={"who is missing","woodpaw gnolls search target","who is raschal"}},{q="Why search the Woodpaw gnoll camps?",a="Ginro says they are the best place to start. Gnolls keep what they scavenge and fight over it, so they may have come across the backpacks Quintis mentioned.",al={"why woodpaw gnolls","why kill gnolls","why search gnoll camps"}},{q="Where did the clue about the backpacks come from?",a="Quintis Jonespyre mentioned them in the vision of Raschal taking two large leather backpacks from the boat.",al={"who mentioned backpacks","quint vision backpacks","how does ginro know about backpacks"}},{q="Where are the Woodpaw camps?",a="In southern Feralas.",al={"woodpaw gnoll location","where are gnoll camps feralas","woodpaw camps map"}}},kw={"feathermoon stronghold","feralas","ginro hearthkindle","leather backpacks","lower wilds","quintis jonespyre","raschal","woodpaw gnolls"},rel={"quest:4130","zone:feralas","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","subzone:lower-wilds","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Ginro Hearthkindle",["end"]="Large Leather Backpacks",level="44",faction="Alliance",id=4131},src={"The Woodpaw Gnolls"}}
E["quest:4135"] = {t="quest",n="The Writhing Deep",z="feralas",s="Among the backpacks lies a hurried note signed by Raschal of Feathermoon. He writes of bug-like creatures he came across, and of his decision to look into them himself. Your search for him now leads there.",h="Among the backpacks lies a hurried note signed by Raschal of Feathermoon.",sec={{t="The Note in the Packs",b="The backpacks hold a parcel meant for Thalanaar, and a note scribbled in a hurry to no one in particular. Its author, Raschal of Feathermoon, describes insidious bug-like creatures he discovered in the Writhing Deep, south of the gnoll camps. He felt he had to see them with his own eyes, for they seemed a grave danger to all of Feralas. The note shows where he went.",sp=0},{t="What Waits Below",b="In the Writhing Deep you come upon a large pod of an alien kind. Its surface looks mucous, with hardened growths jutting from it here and there. It is tall and broad enough to hold a person, and through its skin you can make out the faint shape of a humanoid, which you take to be what it holds.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Raschal?",a="Raschal of Feathermoon wrote the note found in the backpacks. He went to look into bug-like creatures he had discovered, and your search for him continues.",al={"raschal lore","who is raschal","raschal feathermoon"}},{q="Where is the Writhing Deep located?",a="Raschal's note puts the Writhing Deep south of the Woodpaw gnoll camps.",al={"writhing deep location","where is writhing deep","how to find writhing deep"}},{q="Why did Raschal go to the Writhing Deep?",a="His note says he found insidious bug-like creatures there and felt the need to investigate personally, since they looked like a grave danger to Feralas as a whole.",al={"why raschal went to the hive","raschal motives","why the writhing deep"}},{q="What comes before this search?",a="It follows The Woodpaw Gnolls, the step before it.",al={"writhing deep prerequisite","what quest comes first"}}},kw={"feathermoon","feralas","pod","raschal","thalanaar","woodpaw","writhing deep","zukk'ash"},rel={"quest:4131","quest:4265","subzone:writhing-deep","zone:feralas","subzone:thalanaar","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Large Leather Backpacks",["end"]="Zukk'ash Pod",level="46",faction="Alliance",id=4135},src={"The Writhing Deep (quest)"}}
E["quest:4265"] = {t="quest",n="Freed from the Hive",z="feralas",s="The pod you found in the Writhing Deep splits open at your touch, and inside is a night elf, alive though deeply stunned. He is Raschal, the missing courier. With him freed from the Zukk'ash hive, word must reach Ginro Hearthkindle in Feathermoon Stronghold that Raschal is alive and well.",h="The pod you found in the Writhing Deep splits open at your touch, and inside is a night elf, alive though...",sec={{t="Out of the Pod",b="As you help the night elf down from the pod, he stirs. He gives his name as Raschal and says he woke paralyzed inside it after the bugs overwhelmed him. He looks healthy, but is deeply stunned. He asks whether you were sent by the Stronghold.",sp=0},{t="Word for Feathermoon Stronghold",b="Ginro Hearthkindle waits in Feathermoon Stronghold, and he is the one to be told that Raschal lives and is well.",sp=0},{t="Back at the Stronghold",b="Raschal has already reached the Stronghold and told Ginro what happened. Ginro says the whole Stronghold cannot begin to thank you, that Raschal would have died without you arriving in time, and that you asked for no mercenary's fee. You are named a true hero, and a friend to Ginro for good.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is trapped inside the Zukk'ash pod?",a="A night elf named Raschal, the missing courier, who woke paralyzed inside it after the bugs overwhelmed him.",al={"who is in the pod","who is raschal","freed from the hive trapped elf"}},{q="Who do I tell once Raschal is free?",a="Ginro Hearthkindle, in Feathermoon Stronghold, should hear that Raschal is alive and well.",al={"where to turn in freed from the hive","who do i talk to after freeing raschal","ginro hearthkindle location"}},{q="What came before this in the search?",a="It follows The Writhing Deep, where you found the pod.",al={"what quest comes before freed from the hive","freed from the hive prerequisites","previous quest"}}},kw={"courier","feathermoon stronghold","feralas","ginro hearthkindle","pod","raschal","writhing deep","zukk'ash"},rel={"quest:4135","quest:4266","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","zone:feralas","quest:4124"},m={start="Zukk'ash Pod",["end"]="Ginro Hearthkindle",level="46",faction="Alliance",id=4265},src={"Freed from the Hive"}}
E["quest:4266"] = {t="quest",n="A Hero's Welcome",z="feralas",s="Ginro Hearthkindle tells you that General Shandris Feathermoon wants a word with you in person. Gratitude for what you have done for the Stronghold is surely part of it, but she also means to discuss the insect creatures you and Raschal met in the south of Feralas.",h="Ginro Hearthkindle tells you that General Shandris Feathermoon wants a word with you in person.",sec={{t="A Summons",b="Ginro Hearthkindle passes the word: General Shandris Feathermoon wants to see you personally, and she is waiting in the main compound of Feathermoon Stronghold. Ginro admits the reports about the Zukk'ash insects are frightening.",sp=0},{t="At the General's Side",b="The General gives her warmest thanks and a gift on behalf of the whole Stronghold, though she says your bravery against overwhelming odds deserves something a thousand times greater. She then asks for your help once more. With the Zukk'ash hive found here in Feralas, she thinks you are the best choice.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does General Feathermoon want to see me?",a="Ginro expects she means to thank you for your help, and she also wants to talk about the Zukk'ash insects that you and Raschal met in the south of Feralas.",al={"why see shandris","shandris summons","a hero's welcome why"}},{q="Who sends you to speak with Shandris Feathermoon?",a="Ginro Hearthkindle, who says the General wants to see you in person.",al={"who starts a hero's welcome","quest giver hero's welcome","ginro hearthkindle quest"}},{q="Where is General Shandris Feathermoon located?",a="General Feathermoon is waiting in the main compound of Feathermoon Stronghold.",al={"where is shandris","feathermoon stronghold general location","find shandris feathermoon"}},{q="What is the concern about the Zukk'ash insects?",a="Ginro finds the reports of the Zukk'ash insects frightening, and the General wants to talk with you about them.",al={"what are zukk'ash","why are zukk'ash dangerous","insect hive feralas"}}},kw={"a hero's welcome","feathermoon stronghold","feralas","ginro hearthkindle","hive","raschal","shandris feathermoon","zukk'ash"},rel={"npc:shandris-feathermoon","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","quest:4265","zone:feralas"},m={start="Ginro Hearthkindle",["end"]="Shandris Feathermoon",level="46",faction="Alliance",id=4266},src={"A Hero's Welcome (Classic)"}}
E["quest:4267"] = {t="quest",n="Rise of the Silithid",z="feralas",s="General Shandris Feathermoon hands you a copy of Raschal's account of the infestation in southeastern Feralas. Darnassus is where the main report is filed, and she wants this copy to reach Gracina Spiritmight, a priestess of the Temple of the Moon who knows a great deal about such creatures.",h="General Shandris Feathermoon hands you a copy of Raschal's account of the infestation in southeastern Feralas.",sec={{t="A Copy for the Protectorate",b="While the main report is filed in Darnassus, Shandris Feathermoon entrusts this copy to you. It is meant for Gracina Spiritmight, an associate of the Protectorate. She is a priestess, and her home is the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, and the General says her broad knowledge of such creatures, and her receiving the report, would benefit everyone. She dismisses you with good wishes and a prayer that Elune watch over all.",sp=0},{t="What the Priestess Knows",b="Gracina welcomes you to the blessed temple, and tells you the night elves already know the terror outlined in the report. These creatures, she says, will consume Feralas rapidly, and they are among the greatest menaces anyone will face. They are known as the silithid, and they serve as mere tools of one of the gravest threats the Horde and the Alliance will ever face. She prays that resolve will be found to defeat them before they can destroy us.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Darnassus with this report?",a="General Shandris Feathermoon gives you a copy of Raschal's report to carry to Darnassus.",al={"who starts rise of the silithid","quest giver rise of the silithid","who gives rise of the silithid"}},{q="Who is Gracina Spiritmight?",a="Gracina Spiritmight is a priestess of Darnassus, found in the Temple of the Moon. Shandris Feathermoon calls her an associate of the Protectorate with broad knowledge of the creatures in the report.",al={"who is gracina","gracina spiritmight lore","where is gracina spiritmight"}},{q="What is Raschal's report about?",a="It is Raschal's own account of the infestation in southeastern Feralas.",al={"what is raschals report","what did raschal find","contents of raschal report"}},{q="What came before this delivery?",a="It follows A Hero's Welcome, your meeting with General Feathermoon at the Stronghold.",al={"rise of the silithid prerequisite","what quest comes before rise of the silithid"}}},kw={"darnassus","feathermoon stronghold","feralas","gracina spiritmight","raschal","shandris feathermoon","silithid","temple of the moon"},rel={"subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","npc:shandris-feathermoon","zone:feralas","zone:darnassus","topic:elune","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},m={start="Shandris Feathermoon",["end"]="Gracina Spiritmight",level="46",faction="Alliance",id=4267},src={"Rise of the Silithid (Feralas)"}}
E["quest:4281"] = {t="quest",n="Thalanaar Delivery",z="feralas",s="You picked up a parcel of goods in the Woodpaw gnoll camps, though it was meant for Thalanaar, a small way-station in the southeast of Feralas. Whatever became of the courier, the delivery remains unfinished, and a hand-written name on the packaging, Falfindel Waywarder, may point to the one it was meant for.",h="You picked up a parcel of goods in the Woodpaw gnoll camps, though it was meant for Thalanaar, a small...",sec={{t="A Parcel Gone Astray",b="The goods were supposed to reach Thalanaar, a small way-station in southeastern Feralas, but you found them in the Woodpaw gnoll camps instead. Closer inspection shows a name written by hand on the outside: Falfindel Waywarder. It is a fair guess that this is who the parcel was meant for, and Thalanaar is where to look.",sp=0},{t="Word at the Way-station",b="Falfindel praises Elune: the shipment from Feathermoon Stronghold has at last arrived. Seeing you with it, Falfindel fears some ill fate has befallen Raschal, the usual courier. The Woodpaw have lately grown highly agitated over something to their south, and Falfindel suspects Raschal fell to the wilds there. You are told to be careful.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Falfindel Waywarder?",a="Falfindel Waywarder is the name written by hand on the parcel's packaging, and the one you are to find in Thalanaar.",al={"falfindel","who is falfindel","falfindel waywarder thalanaar"}},{q="Where is Thalanaar?",a="Thalanaar is a small way-station in southeastern Feralas, where the parcel was supposed to be delivered.",al={"thalanaar location","where is thalanaar"}},{q="Where was the parcel found?",a="You found it in the Woodpaw gnoll camps.",al={"where did the parcel come from","package origin","undelivered parcel origin"}},{q="What happened to the courier?",a="The courier's fate is unknown. Still, the delivery remains unfinished, so the parcel needs to be brought to Thalanaar.",al={"who was the courier","missing courier name","who carried the parcel"}}},kw={"falfindel waywarder","feathermoon stronghold","feralas","raschal","thalanaar","undelivered parcel","woodpaw"},rel={"subzone:thalanaar","npc:falfindel-waywarder","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","zone:feralas","topic:gnoll","quest:4124"},m={start="Undelivered Parcel",["end"]="Falfindel Waywarder",level="44",faction="Alliance",id=4281},src={"Thalanaar Delivery"}}
E["quest:4297"] = {t="quest",n="Food for Baby",z="feralas",s="Agnar Beastamer will look after your egg for now, so that it is ready for the day it hatches. Sprite darters eat both meat and vegetation, and the young ones like flanks of meat, raw and juicy. Agnar wants Silvermane stalker flanks to feed the hatchling its first meal.",h="Agnar Beastamer will look after your egg for now, so that it is ready for the day it hatches.",sec={{t="A Hatchling's First Meal",b="Agnar Beastamer says sprite darters are omnivores, so a hatchling will need something good to eat once it is out of its shell. Raw, juicy flanks of meat are good eating for the little ones. Agnar will care for the egg meanwhile and wants Silvermane stalker flanks to feed it. Without a good first meal, the newborn might not make it past its first week.",sp=0},{t="Elune's Plan",b="Agnar never learned why sprite darters take to meat. All Agnar knows is that it is tied to Elune's plan for the elves, and wonders whether they were meant to be protectors, but cannot say for sure. Agnar also admits to being jealous that you were the one to get the egg.",sp=0},{t="Back with the Flanks",b="When you return with the flanks, Agnar judges them good enough and says the egg looks just about ready to hatch. Agnar teases you about being a mother or father soon, since you did not expect that kind of responsibility.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does a sprite darter eat?",a="Sprite darters are omnivores, eating both meat and vegetation. Agnar Beastamer says flanks of raw, juicy meat are good eating for the young ones.",al={"sprite darter diet","what do sprite darters eat","sprite dragon food"}},{q="Where is Agnar Beastamer caring for the egg?",a="Agnar looks after the egg in the Hinterlands, and that is where the meat is brought.",al={"agnar beastamer location","where is agnar"}},{q="What meat does Agnar want?",a="Agnar wants five Silvermane stalker flanks, to feed the hatchling once it is out of its shell.",al={"what meat to get","food for baby meat","stalker flanks"}},{q="How does Elune connect to sprite darters?",a="Agnar never found out why darters take to meat, only that it is tied to Elune's plan for the elves, and wonders whether they were meant to be protectors.",al={"elune sprite darter","why meat elune"}},{q="What happens if the hatchling has no good first meal?",a="Agnar warns that without a good first meal it might not make it past its first week.",al={"hatchling no food","will the baby survive"}}},kw={"agnar beastamer","egg","elune","flanks","hinterlands","omnivore","silvermane stalker","sprite darter"},rel={"quest:3843","quest:4298","quest:2969","npc:sprite-darter","topic:elune","zone:feralas"},m={start="Agnar Beastamer",["end"]="Agnar Beastamer",level="47",faction="Alliance",id=4297},src={"Food for Baby"}}
E["quest:4298"] = {t="quest",n="Becoming a Parent",z="feralas",s="Agnar Beastamer in the Hinterlands has found the egg much further along than expected, and wants a word with you about it.",h="Agnar Beastamer in the Hinterlands has found the egg much further along than expected, and wants a word with...",sec={{t="Sooner Than Expected",b="Agnar Beastamer was not prepared for how ready the egg turned out to be. Speak with Agnar in the Hinterlands, where you have been bringing food for the hatchling.",sp=0},{t="A Parent, of a Sort",b="Agnar hands the egg over, so that it will bond to you and look to you as its parent. Agnar congratulates you on becoming a parent, of a sort.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who has news about the egg?",a="Agnar Beastamer, who has been looking after the egg in the Hinterlands.",al={"who starts becoming a parent","becoming a parent quest giver","agnar beastamer quest"}},{q="Where do I find Agnar Beastamer?",a="Agnar is in the Hinterlands.",al={"becoming a parent location","where is agnar beastamer"}},{q="What came before this step?",a="It follows Food for Baby, in which you gathered meat for the hatchling.",al={"becoming a parent prerequisite","previous quest becoming a parent"}}},kw={"agnar beastamer","becoming a parent","egg","food for baby","freedom for all creatures","hinterlands","pet"},rel={"quest:4297","quest:2969","zone:hinterlands","zone:feralas"},m={start="Agnar Beastamer",["end"]="Agnar Beastamer",level="48",faction="Alliance",id=4298},src={"Becoming a Parent"}}
E["quest:7003"] = {t="quest",n="Zapped Giants",z="feralas",s="On the Forgotten Coast of Feralas, near the docks, Zorbin Fandazzle says the giants are bad for business. Zorbin has built a shrinking ray from a gnomish design, improved with goblin know-how, and hands you the Ultra-Shrinker to try on the giants of Feralas.",h="On the Forgotten Coast of Feralas, near the docks, Zorbin Fandazzle says the giants are bad for business.",sec={{t="A Shrinking Ray for the Giants",b="Zorbin Fandazzle has to do something about the giants of Feralas, which are certainly no good for business if Zorbin is to remain out here. The remedy is a variant on a gnomish shrinking ray, built with what Zorbin proudly calls superior goblin advances. To avoid such inconveniences as death, Zorbin would rather you test it. You are to use the Ultra-Shrinker on giants such as Cliff Giants, Deep Striders, Wave Striders, Shore Striders or Land Walkers, and gather the miniaturization residue left on them once shrunk, to bring back to the docks.",sp=0},{t="Why Zorbin Wants the Residue",b="Zorbin calls miniaturization residue a valuable commodity in engineering, because it helps make sure the zapper will not do something as disappointing as exploding on the user. Zorbin then adds that this applies only to other zappers, not the one in your hands.",sp=0},{t="Back at the Docks",b="On your return Zorbin is delighted to see the residue and that you still have all your major appendages. Zorbin then insists the Ultra-Shrinker was never risky at all, and calls you a friend to goblins everywhere.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is behind the Ultra-Shrinker?",a="Zorbin Fandazzle, found by the docks on the Forgotten Coast in Feralas.",al={"who gives zapped giants","zorbin fandazzle quest giver","where to start zapped giants"}},{q="Why does Zorbin want the giants shrunk?",a="Zorbin says the giants are certainly not good for business if Zorbin stays out here, and a shrunken giant is far more manageable.",al={"why zap giants","why shrink giants feralas","zorbin fandazzle motivation"}},{q="Which giants can be shrunk?",a="Any kind of giant in Feralas will do. Along the Forgotten Coast these include Cliff Giants, Deep Striders, Wave Striders, Shore Striders and Land Walkers.",al={"what giants can i zap","which giants count","zapped giants targets"}},{q="What is miniaturization residue?",a="It is found on a giant after it has been shrunk. Zorbin calls it a valuable commodity in engineering, and says it helps make sure the zapper will not explode on the user.",al={"why miniaturization residue","what does residue do","zorbin residue purpose"}}},kw={"cliff giant","feralas","forgotten coast","land walker","miniaturization residue","ultra-shrinker","zapped giants","zorbin fandazzle"},rel={"quest:7725","zone:feralas","subzone:forgotten-coast","topic:goblin"},m={start="Zorbin Fandazzle",["end"]="Zorbin Fandazzle",level="48",id=7003},src={"Zapped Giants"}}
E["quest:7721"] = {t="quest",n="Fuel for the Zapping",z="feralas",s="On the Forgotten Coast of Feralas, Zorbin Fandazzle has opened an engineering shop against better judgment, and the local elementals are a pest. They are also an ideal supply of raw power for refining the Ultra-Shrinker, and the water elemental cores are what Zorbin wants.",h="On the Forgotten Coast of Feralas, Zorbin Fandazzle has opened an engineering shop against better judgment...",sec={{t="Power from the Surf",b="Zorbin Fandazzle curses the unchecked powers of elementalism, and calls the elementals of the coast pests. Yet Zorbin also reckons them an ideal supply of raw power when refining the Ultra-Shrinker. Zorbin wants you to give the Sea Elementals and Sea Sprays of the coast what for, keep their water elemental cores, and bring them to Zorbin by the dock.",sp=0},{t="Zorbin's Thanks",b="Zorbin is delighted: the cores will keep the work going for some time, and there are now fewer elementals along the coast. Zorbin adds that setting up the shop in what may be the worst place imaginable had been a reason to cry at night. Zorbin shows gratitude with payment, though it strains Zorbin's finances.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the elemental cores?",a="Zorbin Fandazzle, who keeps an engineering shop on the Forgotten Coast of Feralas, near the dock there.",al={"who gives fuel for the zapping","zorbin fandazzle quest giver","who starts fuel for the zapping"}},{q="Why does Zorbin Fandazzle need water elemental cores?",a="Zorbin considers the local elementals an ideal supply of raw power for refining the Ultra-Shrinker, and it is the water elemental cores that Zorbin wants.",al={"why water elemental cores","what are cores used for","ultra-shrinker fuel"}},{q="Where are the elemental cores gathered?",a="Zorbin wants them taken from the Sea Elementals and the Sea Sprays that roam the Forgotten Coast of Feralas.",al={"where to find cores","sea elemental location","where are sea sprays"}}},kw={"feralas","forgotten coast","sea elemental","sea spray","ultra-shrinker","water elemental core","zorbin fandazzle"},rel={"zone:feralas","subzone:forgotten-coast","quest:7726"},m={start="Zorbin Fandazzle",["end"]="Zorbin Fandazzle",level="48",id=7721},src={"Fuel for the Zapping"}}
E["quest:7725"] = {t="quest",n="Again With the Zapped Giants",z="feralas",s="Zorbin Fandazzle knows you have already gathered residue, but can always use more. The Ultra-Shrinker is yours to use once more on the giants of Feralas, and Zorbin waits by the Forgotten Coast docks. Zorbin cannot pay nearly as much this time, but promises to spread word of your service.",h="Zorbin Fandazzle knows you have already gathered residue, but can always use more.",sec={{t="An Encore for the Ultra-Shrinker",b="Zorbin Fandazzle admits you have gathered residue already, yet calls this an encore performance and says there is always room for more. Zorbin asks you to zap giants in Feralas once more with the Ultra-Shrinker and bring ten miniaturization residues from the shrunken giants to the docks of the Forgotten Coast. Since Zorbin cannot offer nearly as much in return, the offer is to praise your service among goblin friends, who have quite large ears.",sp=0},{t="Zorbin's Thanks",b="Zorbin is overjoyed that you have come through again, even though the coin is less than you are used to. Zorbin insists that word of your great deeds for goblindom is already ringing through the Steamwheedle Cartel's seats of power.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who asks for more residue?",a="Zorbin Fandazzle, who waits by the Forgotten Coast docks in Feralas.",al={"quest giver","zorbin location","who gives again with the zapped giants"}},{q="What came before this?",a="It follows Zapped Giants, your first round of residue gathering for Zorbin Fandazzle.",al={"prerequisite","previous quest","what do i do first"}},{q="How is the residue gathered?",a="Zorbin's Ultra-Shrinker is turned on any kind of giant in Feralas to shrink it, and the residue is found on the shrunken giants.",al={"how to get residue","miniaturization residue","how to shrink giants"}},{q="Where are the giants found?",a="The giants are found along the western coast of Feralas.",al={"giant location","where are feralas giants","forgotten coast giants"}},{q="Will Zorbin take more residue another time?",a="Zorbin says more residue can always be used, so you are welcome to come back with another batch of ten.",al={"is this repeatable","can i repeat again with the zapped giants","repeatable giant quest"}}},kw={"feralas","forgotten coast","giants","miniaturization residue","steamwheedle cartel","ultra-shrinker","zorbin fandazzle"},rel={"quest:7003","subzone:forgotten-coast","zone:feralas","topic:steamwheedle-cartel","topic:goblin"},m={start="Zorbin Fandazzle",["end"]="Zorbin Fandazzle",level="55",id=7725},src={"Again With the Zapped Giants"}}
E["quest:7726"] = {t="quest",n="Refuel for the Zapping",z="feralas",s="Zorbin Fandazzle needs more water elemental cores. Setting up shop on the Forgotten Coast is a struggle, so the pay will be smaller, but Zorbin promises to tell everyone in earshot of your help and says there are friends in the Cartel.",h="Zorbin Fandazzle needs more water elemental cores.",sec={{t="More of the Same",b="Zorbin Fandazzle jokes about the heroic deed of collecting goo from inside elemental beings, wondering whether you will want more of the same. Melodrama aside, Zorbin does need more water elemental cores. Establishing the shop here is a desperate business, so there is little to give in return, but Zorbin promises to tell everyone in earshot how you helped, and says to trust this because Zorbin knows people in the Cartel. Six cores are wanted, taken from Sea Elementals and Sea Sprays on the Forgotten Coast, and brought to Zorbin near the dock.",sp=0},{t="Zorbin's Thanks",b="Zorbin is pleased and admits the coin may not be the most you will ever receive for such work. The Steamwheedle Cartel comrades of Zorbin will be told of your efforts, and if you want more to do, Zorbin has an ongoing need for further cores and similar things.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is requesting the water elemental cores?",a="Zorbin Fandazzle, found by the dock on the Forgotten Coast of Feralas.",al={"who gives this quest","who is zorbin fandazzle","where is zorbin"}},{q="Where do the water elemental cores come from?",a="They are taken from Sea Elementals and Sea Sprays on the Forgotten Coast of Feralas.",al={"where do cores drop","water elemental core location","which enemies drop cores"}},{q="Why does Zorbin Fandazzle need more cores?",a="Zorbin says only that more water elemental cores are needed, while struggling to get a shop established on the coast.",al={"why does zorbin want cores","zorbin fandazzle motive","what are the cores for"}},{q="What came before this?",a="It follows Fuel for the Zapping, when you first gathered elemental cores for Zorbin.",al={"previous quest","prerequisite quest","what quest comes first"}}},kw={"feralas","forgotten coast","sea elemental","sea spray","steamwheedle cartel","water elemental core","zorbin fandazzle"},rel={"quest:7721","subzone:forgotten-coast","zone:feralas","topic:steamwheedle-cartel"},m={start="Zorbin Fandazzle",["end"]="Zorbin Fandazzle",level="55",id=7726},src={"Refuel for the Zapping"}}
E["quest:7730"] = {t="quest",n="Zukk'ash Infestation",z="feralas",s="At Camp Mojache, Hadoken Swiftstrider has word of insect-like creatures, the Zukk'ash, south of the gnolls. If they are whipping the gnolls into a frenzy, they are as great a threat as the gnolls, perhaps greater. You are sent into their home, the Writhing Deep, to thin their numbers and bring back twenty carapaces.",h="At Camp Mojache, Hadoken Swiftstrider has word of insect-like creatures, the Zukk'ash, south of the gnolls.",sec={{t="The Foe South of the Gnolls",b="Hadoken Swiftstrider believes that the enemy to the south of the gnolls is a race of insect-like creatures. Whether they can think hardly matters to Hadoken. If they are driving the gnolls into a frenzy against Camp Mojache, they are as big a danger as the gnolls themselves, or bigger. You are to go deep into where they dwell, known as the Writhing Deep, and thin their numbers. The carapaces of twenty Zukk'ash will be your proof, and Hadoken wants to hear what you find.",sp=0},{t="Hadoken's Verdict",b="When you return, Hadoken is pleased. Nothing short of a full-scale invasion will end the Zukk'ash presence, but you have bought the camp time to devise a proper strategy. The carapaces will be analyzed, since the camp must learn everything about these creatures. This has unfortunately turned into a far bigger problem than anyone had anticipated.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you after the Zukk'ash?",a="Hadoken Swiftstrider, at Camp Mojache in Feralas.",al={"quest giver","hadoken swiftstrider","who starts zukkash infestation"}},{q="What are the Zukk'ash?",a="Hadoken believes they are a race of insect-like creatures south of the gnolls. Whether they can think does not matter to Hadoken, only that they may be driving the gnolls into a frenzy.",al={"what are zukkash","zukkash insects","writhing deep bugs"}},{q="Where is the Writhing Deep?",a="It is where the Zukk'ash insects dwell, south of the gnolls.",al={"writhing deep location","where is writhing deep","where are the insects"}},{q="Why does Hadoken want Zukk'ash carapaces?",a="Hadoken wants the carapaces as evidence of your handiwork against the Zukk'ash.",al={"why carapaces","zukkash carapace use","purpose of carapaces"}}},kw={"camp mojache","carapace","feralas","gnolls","hadoken swiftstrider","insects","writhing deep","zukk'ash"},rel={"quest:7732","subzone:writhing-deep","subzone:camp-mojache","zone:feralas","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Hadoken Swiftstrider",["end"]="Hadoken Swiftstrider",level="45",faction="Horde",id=7730},src={"Zukk'ash Infestation (Classic)"}}
E["quest:7731"] = {t="quest",n="Stinglasher",z="feralas",s="While surveying the Writhing Deep, one of Hadoken Swiftstrider's scouts spotted a giant insect, far larger than the others, wandering the twisted terrain. It has been named Stinglasher, and Hadoken wants it brought down and its secretion glands brought back to Camp Mojache.",h="While surveying the Writhing Deep, one of Hadoken Swiftstrider's scouts spotted a giant insect, far larger...",sec={{t="A Giant Among the Insects",b="One scout in the Writhing Deep saw an insect much bigger than the others, wandering about the twisted terrain. It also seems to give off an aura that sets it apart from the rest. It has been given the name Stinglasher. Its innards would be invaluable to study while Hadoken works out how to deal with this new threat, so Hadoken wants its secretion glands cut out and brought straight to Camp Mojache.",sp=0},{t="Hadoken's Thanks",b="Hadoken is most impressed. If Stinglasher is indeed one of the strongest of the insects, studying the beast will prove valuable in time, and Hadoken's charge is to make sure the camp defends itself long enough to benefit. A coin bounty is given, with thanks from the whole camp.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you after Stinglasher?",a="Hadoken Swiftstrider, at Camp Mojache in Feralas.",al={"quest giver","who gives stinglasher","hadoken swiftstrider"}},{q="Where is Stinglasher found?",a="Stinglasher wanders around the twisted terrain of the Writhing Deep.",al={"stinglasher location","where is stinglasher","writhing deep location"}},{q="What makes Stinglasher different from the other insects?",a="A scout reported an insect of giant size, and it seems to give off an aura the rest lack.",al={"why stinglasher","what is stinglasher","stinglasher aura"}},{q="Why does Hadoken want Stinglasher's glands?",a="Hadoken says studying its innards would be invaluable while a plan against this new threat is worked out.",al={"why collect glands","stinglasher glands purpose"}}},kw={"camp mojache","feralas","glands","hadoken swiftstrider","insect","stinglasher","writhing deep","zukk'ash"},rel={"quest:7730","quest:7732","subzone:camp-mojache","subzone:writhing-deep","zone:feralas"},m={start="Hadoken Swiftstrider",["end"]="Hadoken Swiftstrider",level="47",faction="Horde",id=7731},src={"Stinglasher (Classic)"}}
E["quest:7732"] = {t="quest",n="Zukk'ash Report",z="feralas",s="Hadoken Swiftstrider says you have done doubly well against the Zukk'ash insects menacing Camp Mojache, but the danger is far from over. One last favor for the Horde: carry a document recording everything learned about the Zukk'ash to Orgrimmar, to Zilzibin Drumlore.",h="Hadoken Swiftstrider says you have done doubly well against the Zukk'ash insects menacing Camp Mojache, but...",sec={{t="A Document for the Drag",b="Hadoken Swiftstrider holds a document that sets down all the camp has learned about the Zukk'ash insects. The danger they pose is far from over, and Hadoken asks you to take it to Orgrimmar. There, in the Drag, lives Zilzibin Drumlore, an expert on alien creatures such as these, and Hadoken hopes the lore gathered so far will be put to some use.",sp=0},{t="The Expert's Verdict",b="Zilzibin has been expecting the report. He calls the creatures you faced an ancient threat that the Horde keeps choosing to ignore, and says Hadoken was wise to send both the report and you. The Zukk'ash are nothing but creatures called the silithid. Some think them a mindless nuisance, but Zilzibin assures you they are a much worse threat than any the Alliance could muster.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends the report to Orgrimmar?",a="Hadoken Swiftstrider at Camp Mojache in Feralas hands you the document.",al={"who gives zukkash report","who starts zukkash report","quest giver"}},{q="To whom is the report delivered?",a="To Zilzibin Drumlore, who resides in the Drag of Orgrimmar.",al={"where does the report go","who gets zukkash report","drumlore location"}},{q="Why is the document taken to Orgrimmar?",a="Zilzibin Drumlore is an expert on alien creatures like the Zukk'ash, and Hadoken hopes the lore the camp has gathered will be put to some use.",al={"why send to orgrimmar","purpose of report"}},{q="What came before this delivery?",a="It follows your efforts against the Zukk'ash insects, in Zukk'ash Infestation and Stinglasher.",al={"previous quests","prerequisites"}}},kw={"camp mojache","drag","feralas","hadoken swiftstrider","orgrimmar","silithid","zilzibin drumlore","zukk'ash report"},rel={"subzone:camp-mojache","zone:feralas","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:drag","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},m={start="Hadoken Swiftstrider",["end"]="Zilzibin Drumlore",level="48",faction="Horde",id=7732},src={"Zukk'ash Report"}}
E["quest:7733"] = {t="quest",n="Improved Quality",z="feralas",s="Pratt McGrubben has heard of hides better still than the last. Up in the north of Feralas, inside Rage Scar Hold, roams another throng of yetis, tougher than those you faced before. Ten of their hides are wanted at Feathermoon Stronghold.",h="Pratt McGrubben has heard of hides better still than the last.",sec={{t="A Tougher Throng of Yetis",b="After The Mark of Quality, Pratt McGrubben has found a lead on a still finer supply of hides. Up in the north of Feralas, inside Rage Scar Hold, another throng of yetis lives, tougher than the ones you faced earlier. Pratt McGrubben will pay handsomely for ten of their hides, brought back to Feathermoon Stronghold to settle the matter. If they match the quality of the Feral Scar hides, they could prove as resilient as thorium.",sp=0},{t="Pratt's Thanks",b="The hides are even better than hoped. Pratt McGrubben can already tell they will turn much harder once properly cured, and hands you one of the latest creations as thanks.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who asks for the Rage Scar yeti hides?",a="Pratt McGrubben, at Feathermoon Stronghold in Feralas.",al={"who gives improved quality","improved quality questgiver","pratt mcgrubben"}},{q="Where do the Rage Scar yetis live?",a="Inside Rage Scar Hold, in the north of Feralas.",al={"rage scar yeti location","where is rage scar hold","where to get rage scar hides"}},{q="How many hides are wanted?",a="Pratt McGrubben wants ten Rage Scar yeti hides.",al={"how many yeti hides","improved quality items needed"}},{q="What came before this?",a="It follows The Mark of Quality, when you dealt with the first throng of yetis.",al={"prerequisite quest","what quest leads to improved quality","previous quest"}}},kw={"feathermoon stronghold","feralas","improved quality","pratt mcgrubben","rage scar hold","thorium","yeti hide","yetis"},rel={"subzone:rage-scar-hold","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","zone:feralas"},m={start="Pratt McGrubben",["end"]="Pratt McGrubben",level="48",faction="Alliance",id=7733},src={"Improved Quality (Classic Alliance)"}}
E["quest:7734"] = {t="quest",n="Improved Quality",z="feralas",s="Jangdor Swiftstrider has heard of hides better still than the last. Up in the north of Feralas, inside Rage Scar Hold, roams another throng of yetis, tougher than those you faced before. Ten of their hides are wanted at Camp Mojache.",h="Jangdor Swiftstrider has heard of hides better still than the last.",sec={{t="A Tougher Throng of Yetis",b="After The Mark of Quality, Jangdor Swiftstrider has found a lead on a still finer supply of hides. Up in the north of Feralas, inside Rage Scar Hold, another throng of yetis lives, tougher than the ones you faced earlier. Jangdor Swiftstrider will pay handsomely for ten of their hides, brought back to Camp Mojache to settle the matter. If they match the quality of the Feral Scar hides, they could prove as resilient as thorium.",sp=0},{t="Jangdor's Thanks",b="The hides are even better than hoped. Jangdor Swiftstrider can already tell they will turn much harder once properly cured, and hands you one of the latest creations as thanks.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who asks for the Rage Scar yeti hides?",a="Jangdor Swiftstrider, at Camp Mojache in Feralas.",al={"who gives improved quality","improved quality questgiver","jangdor swiftstrider"}},{q="Where do the Rage Scar yetis live?",a="Inside Rage Scar Hold, in the north of Feralas.",al={"rage scar yeti location","where is rage scar hold","where to get rage scar hides"}},{q="How many hides are wanted?",a="Jangdor Swiftstrider wants ten Rage Scar yeti hides.",al={"how many yeti hides","improved quality items needed"}},{q="What came before this?",a="It follows The Mark of Quality, when you dealt with the first throng of yetis.",al={"prerequisite quest","what quest leads to improved quality","previous quest"}}},kw={"camp mojache","feralas","improved quality","jangdor swiftstrider","rage scar hold","rage scar yeti","yeti hides"},rel={"subzone:camp-mojache","subzone:rage-scar-hold","zone:feralas"},m={start="Jangdor Swiftstrider",["end"]="Jangdor Swiftstrider",level="48",faction="Horde",id=7734},src={"Improved Quality (Classic Horde)"}}
E["quest:7735"] = {t="quest",n="Pristine Yeti Hide",z="feralas",s="You have come into a yeti hide that is unusually thick and tough, tougher even than any you have seen from the yetis of Rage Scar. Pratt McGrubben at Feathermoon Stronghold is looking for yeti hides, and this one may interest him.",h="You have come into a yeti hide that is unusually thick and tough, tougher even than any you have seen from...",sec={{t="A Hide Out of the Ordinary",b="This hide is pristine, and clearly thicker and sturdier than the hides taken from the yetis of Rage Scar. Pratt McGrubben, at Feathermoon Stronghold in Feralas, wants to buy yeti hides, so this one is worth carrying to him.",sp=0},{t="Pratt's Reaction",b="Pratt is amazed and wonders aloud if this is the greatest yeti hide there could be. Pratt will pay you for it, more than a single hide usually fetches, and thinks something special can be made from it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who wants the Pristine Yeti Hide?",a="Pratt McGrubben at Feathermoon Stronghold in Feralas, who is looking to buy yeti hides.",al={"who takes pristine yeti hide","where do i bring the yeti hide","pratt mcgrubben yeti hide"}},{q="What makes this hide special?",a="It is unusually thick and tough, beating even the hides that come from Rage Scar's yetis.",al={"pristine yeti hide source","what makes the hide special","feralas yeti hide"}},{q="Where is Pratt McGrubben?",a="At Feathermoon Stronghold in Feralas.",al={"where is pratt mcgrubben","where to bring pristine yeti hide"}}},kw={"feathermoon stronghold","feralas","pratt mcgrubben","pristine yeti hide","rage scar","yeti pelt"},rel={"subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","zone:feralas"},m={start="Pristine Yeti Hide",["end"]="Pratt McGrubben",level="48",id=7735},src={"Classic quest text: Pristine Yeti Hide"}}
E["quest:7738"] = {t="quest",n="Perfect Yeti Hide",z="feralas",s="You have found a yeti hide that may well be perfect: remarkably thick and tough, beyond what the yetis of Rage Scar yield. At Camp Mojache, Jangdor Swiftstrider is looking for yeti hides.",h="You have found a yeti hide that may well be perfect: remarkably thick and tough, beyond what the yetis of...",sec={{t="A Hide Worth Showing",b="The hide is plainly thicker and sturdier than the ones from the yetis of Rage Scar. At Camp Mojache in Feralas, Jangdor Swiftstrider wants to buy yeti hides, so this one is worth bringing there.",sp=0},{t="Jangdor's Verdict",b="Jangdor is delighted, calling it the finest yeti hide he has ever seen. A fitting bounty is in order, more than he usually pays for a single hide, and he is confident something special can be made from it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is interested in the Perfect Yeti Hide?",a="Jangdor Swiftstrider, at Camp Mojache in Feralas, who wants to buy yeti hides.",al={"who wants the hide","who turns in perfect yeti hide","jangdor yeti pelt"}},{q="Why is this hide considered special?",a="It is unusually thick and tough, and may well be perfect, better than the hides from Rage Scar's yetis.",al={"why is it perfect","what makes the hide special"}},{q="Where is Jangdor Swiftstrider?",a="At Camp Mojache in Feralas.",al={"where is jangdor swiftstrider","where to bring perfect yeti hide"}}},kw={"camp mojache","feralas","jangdor swiftstrider","perfect yeti hide","rage scar","yeti pelt"},rel={"subzone:camp-mojache","zone:feralas"},m={start="Perfect Yeti Hide",["end"]="Jangdor Swiftstrider",level="48",id=7738},src={"Classic quest text: Perfect Yeti Hide"}}
E["subzone:camp-mojache"] = {t="subzone",n="Camp Mojache",z="feralas",s="Camp Mojache is the primary Horde outpost in Feralas, established as a fortified tauren settlement along the waters feeding Wildwind Lake. It provides shelter, provisions, and flight connections to travelers contending with the untamed wilderness, aggressive wildlife, and ancient ruins of the deep forest.",h="Camp Mojache is the primary Horde outpost in Feralas, established as a fortified tauren settlement along the...",sec={{t="A Tauren Bastion in the Rainforest",b="Situated in eastern Feralas along a swift-flowing stream that feeds Wildwind Lake, Camp Mojache is a tauren settlement built to secure a foothold in the wild southern forest. While the dense jungle holds perilous threats—from savage wildlife to Gordunni ogres and aggressive Woodpaw gnolls—the camp stands as an island of safety. Equipped with lodging, trade masters, and a wind rider roost, it serves as the vital logistical hub for Horde champions operating in the region.",sp=0},{t="Frontier Outpost",b="The camp's hunters and braves are renowned for their courage and thick hides, maintaining constant vigilance against raids from the surrounding wilderness. For the Horde, holding Mojache is essential for projecting influence across Feralas, checking the presence of both the Night Elves from the coast and the dark forces lurking within Dire Maul.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camp Mojache?",a="Camp Mojache is the main Horde base of operations in Feralas. Built and maintained predominantly by the tauren, it straddles a stream emptying into Wildwind Lake and offers resting facilities, trade supplies, and flight transport.",al={"camp mojache purpose","what is this camp","tauren town feralas"}},{q="Who leads or defends the camp?",a="The settlement is protected by seasoned tauren braves who guard against incursions from local beast packs, Gordunni ogres, and aggressive Woodpaw gnolls that prowl the hills just to the south.",al={"camp mojache guards","who defends mojache","who is in charge of camp mojache"}},{q="Where does the local flight master travel?",a="From the camp's wind rider perch, travelers can reach central hubs such as Thunder Bluff, the Crossroads in the Barrens, Shadowprey Village in Desolace, and neighboring outposts like Gadgetzan in Tanaris.",al={"camp mojache flight paths","where can i fly from camp mojache"}},{q="What major threats surround Camp Mojache?",a="The surrounding woods are home to the Woodpaw gnoll clan to the south, territorial Gordunni ogres to the north and south, and Alliance forces operating out of the distant western coast at Feathermoon Stronghold.",al={"feralas danger camp mojache","threats near camp mojache","enemies near mojache"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Camp Mojache represents the farthest southern reach of your people's traditional craftsmanship and settlements in Kalimdor, carving out harmony within the deep rainforest.",["faction:Horde"]="As the Horde's sole fortified hub in Feralas, Mojache is your only refuge for resting, restocking provisions, and securing swift transport across the deep forest."},kw={"braves","camp mojache","feralas","flight master","gordunni","tauren","wildwind lake","woodpaw"},rel={"zone:feralas","topic:tauren","topic:horde","zone:thunderbluff","subzone:crossroads","subzone:shadowprey-village","subzone:gadgetzan","topic:gnoll"},src={"Camp Mojache"}}
E["subzone:capital-gardens"] = {t="subzone",n="Capital Gardens",z="feralas",s="The Capital Gardens form the western wing of the ancient elven ruins of Dire Maul in Feralas. Once a serene, manicured park for the Kaldorei nobility, it has withered into a blighted woodland stalked by corrupted ancients, ghosts, and remnants of the Shen'dralar.",h="The Capital Gardens form the western wing of the ancient elven ruins of Dire Maul in Feralas.",sec={{t="A Decayed Sanctuary",b="Ten millennia ago, Eldre'Thalas stood as one of the shining jewels of the Kaldorei empire. The Capital Gardens served as its outdoor district, lush with enchanted flora and grand marble terraces where Highborne sorcerers debated and relaxed. Following the Great Sundering, the enclave fell on desperate times. Deprived of the Well of Eternity, the resident Shen'dralar turned to dark magic to sustain their immortality, letting the gardens wither away. Today, gray, twisted boughs and corrupted treants fill the broken courtyards, while residual magical corruption prevents the forest from ever truly healing.",sp=0},{t="The Athenaeum and the Prison",b="Beyond the overgrown alleys and hostile ancients, the Capital Gardens connect deeper into the heart of the Shen'dralar redoubt. The paths lead directly to the Court of the Highborne and the Athenaeum—the preserved library holding centuries of arcane lore and forgotten treatises. Deeper still lies the Prison of Immol'thar, where the surviving elves bound a demon to siphon its power, an act of desperation that warped the surrounding gardens into the nightmare seen today.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Capital Gardens?",a="The Capital Gardens is the western wing of Dire Maul, located within the ruins of Eldre'Thalas in central Feralas. It was once a pristine public park and residence for the city's Highborne elite.",al={"what is capital gardens","dire maul west gardens","eldre'thalas park"}},{q="Why are the trees and ancients corrupted here?",a="After the Well of Eternity was destroyed, the surviving Shen'dralar sustained themselves by siphoning dark fel energies from a summoned demon, Immol'thar. The resulting leak of volatile magic slowly warped the local plant life and drove the resident ancients into violent madness.",al={"why are ancients evil here","what happened to the trees","why is it blighted"}},{q="Where does this area lead?",a="The gardens lead deeper into the western complex of Dire Maul, opening into the Court of the Highborne, the scholarly Athenaeum, and the inner sanctuary holding the demon Immol'thar.",al={"what connects to capital gardens","where does it go"}},{q="Are there any friendly elves left in the gardens?",a="Most of the Highborne roaming the pathways are hostile spirits or maddened defenders. However, within the nearby Athenaeum, some Shen'dralar scholars still endure, willing to barter ancient knowledge or trade for lost elven librams.",al={"any allies inside","who lives in capital gardens"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves, walking the blighted paving of the Capital Gardens is a harrowing reminder of Highborne hubris and the catastrophic costs of arcane addiction.",["class:Mage"]="Despite the decay, the gardens house pathways toward the Athenaeum, one of the greatest repositories of pre-Sundering magical theory still standing in Kalimdor."},kw={"athenaeum","capital gardens","dire maul west","eldre'thalas","feralas","immol'thar","shen'dralar"},rel={"subzone:dire-maul","zone:feralas","topic:highborne","subzone:gordok-commons"},src={"Capital Gardens"}}
E["subzone:dire-maul"] = {t="subzone",n="Dire Maul",z="feralas",s="Dire Maul is the ruined expanse of Eldre'Thalas, an ancient Highborne city hidden deep in the wilderness of Feralas. Once built to safeguard Queen Azshara's arcane secrets, its crumbling plazas and towering coliseums are now divided between occupying Gordok ogres, invading satyrs, and the withered remnants of its original elven caretakers.",h="Dire Maul is the ruined expanse of Eldre'Thalas, an ancient Highborne city hidden deep in the wilderness of...",sec={{t="Eldre'Thalas and the Great Sundering",b="Twelve thousand years ago, Eldre'Thalas served as a wondrous bastion for Queen Azshara's favored sorcerers, the Shen'dralar. When the Well of Eternity collapsed during the Great Sundering, Prince Tortheldrin wove a magical barrier that shielded the city from ruin. Severed from their source of magic, the surviving Highborne trapped a colossal demon named Immol'thar beneath their sanctum, siphoning its fel essence to sustain their immortality and arcane powers for millennia.",sp=0},{t="A Divided Ruin",b="Centuries of isolation and dwindling power drove Prince Tortheldrin to madness, leading him to purge most of his own citizens so a small cabal could monopolize the demon's remaining energy. Today, the outer districts of the sprawling complex lie abandoned to other threats. Gordunni ogres claim the Gordok Commons and run brutal gladiatorial games in the arena, while Alzzin the Wildshaper and his corrupt satyrs rot the Warpwood Quarter from within.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What was Dire Maul originally called?",a="Dire Maul was originally Eldre'Thalas, an opulent night elf city constructed twelve thousand years ago by the Shen'dralar sect to protect Queen Azshara's most precious arcane lore.",al={"dire maul original name","eldre'thalas history","who built dire maul"}},{q="Who lives in Dire Maul now?",a="The complex is splintered into several hostile zones. The Gordunni ogres control the northern commons under King Gordok, satyrs and corrupted treants infest the eastern gardens, and a reclusive remnant of Highborne sorcerers clings to survival in the western sanctuaries.",al={"who is in dire maul","dire maul occupants","what monsters are in dire maul"}},{q="How did the city survive the Sundering?",a="When the continent tore apart during the Great Sundering, Prince Tortheldrin and his arcanists cast a massive protective spell that shielded Eldre'Thalas from the devastation that submerged the surrounding empire.",al={"how did eldre'thalas survive","sundering shield dire maul","why wasn't it destroyed"}},{q="Why are the Highborne here using demonic energy?",a="When the Well of Eternity was destroyed, the Shen'dralar suffered severe arcane withdrawal. To preserve their power and immortality, they bound the demon Immol'thar and siphoned its essence to survive.",al={"immol'thar dire maul","why do shen'dralar drain a demon","demon in dire maul"}},{q="What happens in the arena at Dire Maul?",a="Known as the Maul, the open coliseum in the city center is used by the ogres and slavemasters as a fighting pit for gladiatorial tournaments, blood sports, and challenges to the Gordok throne.",al={"dire maul coliseum","the maul pvp","gladiators dire maul"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Eldre'Thalas stands as a tragic monument to the unchecked arcane hubris and demonic compromises that broke the ancient Kaldorei Empire.",["class:Mage"]="Within the ruined libraries of the Shen'dralar lie arcane treatises and secrets preserved from before the Great Sundering, guarded by the ghosts of master sorcerers."},kw={"dire maul","eldre'thalas","feralas","gordok","gordunni","immol'thar","shen'dralar","tortheldrin"},rel={"zone:feralas","topic:highborne","subzone:gordok-commons","subzone:capital-gardens","subzone:warpwood-quarter","subzone:maul-subzone","topic:satyr","topic:war-of-the-ancients"},src={"Dire Maul"}}
E["subzone:dream-bough"] = {t="subzone",n="Dream Bough",z="feralas",s="Dream Bough is a colossal Great Tree nestled on an island in the center of Jademir Lake in northern Feralas. The ancient tree shelters a mysterious gateway connecting Azeroth directly to the Emerald Dream. Green dragons loyally watch over the sanctuary, keeping unwanted intruders away from its verdant boughs.",h="Dream Bough is a colossal Great Tree nestled on an island in the center of Jademir Lake in northern Feralas.",sec={{t="The Great Tree of Jademir",b="Rising high above the canopy of northern Feralas, the Dream Bough stands as the largest tree in the region. Situated in the tranquil waters of Jademir Lake, the towering sentinel houses a natural portal carved into its trunk, providing a direct threshold into the untamed Emerald Dream.",sp=0},{t="The Emerald Watchers",b="Because of its connection to the Emerald Dream, the tree is under the vigilant protection of the Green Dragonflight. Dragonkin and drakes patrol the banks of Jademir Lake and the approaches to the great trunk. While primarily a place of contemplation and slumber for druids wandering between realms, travelers should approach with care, as the green dragons tolerate few uninvited visitors near such an important threshold.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Dream Bough?",a="Dream Bough is a massive Great Tree located on an island in Jademir Lake, within northern Feralas. It serves as a sanctum housing an active gateway into the Emerald Dream.",al={"dream bough tree","what is dream bough","jademir lake tree"}},{q="Who planted the Dream Bough?",a="No account from this age records who planted the Dream Bough. It is known as one of the Great Trees that shelter gateways into the Emerald Dream, watched over by the green dragonflight.",al={"who grew dream bough","origin of dream bough","staghelm tree"}},{q="Why are there green dragons here?",a="The Green Dragonflight acts as the eternal wardens of the Emerald Dream. Because a direct gateway to the Dream rests within the tree's trunk, dragons and their kin maintain a constant guard to protect the portal from intruders.",al={"green dragonflight dream bough","dragons at jademir lake"}},{q="Can players enter the portal into the Emerald Dream?",a="The swirling portal set into the trunk connects directly into the Emerald Dream, but it remains impassable to mortal adventurers waking in the physical realm. Only powerful sleeping druids and the Green Dragonflight freely cross its boundary.",al={"can i use dream bough portal","enter emerald dream feralas"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Dream Bough is sacred ground, embodying the vital bridge between Azeroth's wilderness and the pristine Emerald Dream tended by your order.",["race:NightElf"]="Guarding a gateway into the Emerald Dream, this great tree represents your people's ancient duty to nurture and defend the natural world."},kw={"dream bough","emerald dream","feralas","great tree","green dragonflight","jademir lake"},rel={"zone:feralas","topic:emerald-dream","topic:druid"},src={"Dream Bough"}}
E["subzone:eldreth-row"] = {t="subzone",n="Eldreth Row",z="feralas",s="Eldreth Row comprises the soaring, ruined outer halls forming the western entrance to Dire Maul in Feralas. Once a grand threshold of ancient Eldre'Thalas, the area is now choked with overgrowth and fiercely patrolled by Gordunni ogres.",h="Eldreth Row comprises the soaring, ruined outer halls forming the western entrance to Dire Maul in Feralas.",sec={{t="The Threshold of Eldre'Thalas",b="Standing as the outermost perimeter of ancient Eldre'Thalas, Eldreth Row is an imposing avenue of high-arched elven architecture that sits just outside the deeper quarters and the Broken Commons. Centuries of neglect have cracked its stonework, allowing the creeping flora of Feralas to reclaim its colonnades. Today, the pristine majesty of the Highborne has been replaced by the crude dominance of the Gordunni ogres, who use the halls as an outer staging ground, guarding the paths leading east toward the Warpwood Quarter and west past the Dire Pool.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Eldreth Row?",a="Eldreth Row is the exterior entrance hall and perimeter of Dire Maul in Feralas, situated before the Broken Commons and the inner instance gateways.",al={"eldreth row","what is this place","dire maul entrance"}},{q="Who controls Eldreth Row right now?",a="The area is occupied and patrolled by the Gordunni clan of ogres, who have fortified Dire Maul's ruins and wander its broken avenues.",al={"who lives here","who controls eldreth row","eldreth row monsters"}},{q="Where does Eldreth Row lead?",a="The avenue leads inward toward the Broken Commons and the main complexes of Dire Maul, with an entrance to the Warpwood Quarter on its far eastern flank and the Dire Pool located to the west.",al={"where does this hall go","eldreth row exits","dire maul paths"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Seeing the majestic masonry of ancient Eldre'Thalas desecrated by brutish ogres serves as a bitter reminder of the fall of the Highborne and the Sundering."},kw={"broken commons","dire maul","dire pool","eldre'thalas","eldreth row","feralas","gordunni","warpwood quarter"},rel={"subzone:dire-maul","subzone:commons","subzone:warpwood-quarter","zone:feralas"},src={"Eldreth Row"}}
E["subzone:feathermoon-stronghold"] = {t="subzone",n="Feathermoon Stronghold",z="feralas",s="Feathermoon Stronghold is the premier night elf military base in southern Kalimdor, situated securely on Sardor Isle off the Forgotten Coast of Feralas. Commanded by General Shandris Feathermoon, this fortified outpost projects Sentinel strength across the wild forest and keeps watch over regional threats.",h="Feathermoon Stronghold is the premier night elf military base in southern Kalimdor, situated securely on...",sec={{t="Sentinel Bastion of the South",b="Perched on Sardor Isle across the channel from Feralas's mainland, Feathermoon Stronghold serves as the primary strategic base for the Sentinels in southern Kalimdor. Built among ancient elven groves and supplied with a sacred moonwell, the fortress houses archers, huntresses, and support staff under the direct supervision of General Shandris Feathermoon. From this insular sanctuary, the night elves project their influence over the verdant interior of Feralas, guarding against demonic corruption, hostile wildlife, and encroaching Horde expeditions.",sp=0},{t="A Safe Haven in the Wilds",b="Because the mainland of Feralas is thick with savage beasts, Gordunni ogres, and the tainted shadows of Dire Maul, Sardor Isle provides an essential defensive buffer. Alliance travelers rely on the ferry crossing from the Forgotten Coast to reach its fortified docks, repair their gear, and gather intelligence. The presence of Shandris Feathermoon—General of the Sentinels and High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind's trusted right hand—ensures that the stronghold remains an unassailable redoubt against all enemies of the kaldorei.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Feathermoon Stronghold located?",a="Feathermoon Stronghold sits on Sardor Isle, an island positioned off the Forgotten Coast on the western edge of Feralas. Travelers must journey west across the forest to the coast and take a boat across the water to reach the island fortress.",al={"feathermoon location","where is feathermoon","how to get to feathermoon stronghold"}},{q="Who commands Feathermoon Stronghold?",a="The stronghold is commanded by General Shandris Feathermoon, supreme commander of the Sentinel army and right hand of High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind. She oversees all kaldorei military efforts throughout southern Kalimdor from this outpost.",al={"who leads feathermoon","feathermoon leader","shandris feathermoon base"}},{q="Why is the stronghold located on an island instead of the mainland?",a="Sardor Isle offers natural oceanic defenses against the many dangers of mainland Feralas, which is overrun by savage beasts, Gordunni ogres, and lingering arcane and demonic perils. Positioning the fortress on an island provides a secure port that controls coastal waters while keeping mainland threats at bay.",al={"why sardor isle","why is feathermoon on an island"}},{q="Does Feathermoon Stronghold have a moonwell?",a="Yes, Feathermoon Stronghold maintains a sacred moonwell within its grounds. It provides spiritual focus, sustenance, and a source of holy water for the night elf garrison stationed far from their homeland in the north.",al={"feathermoon moonwell","is there a moonwell at feathermoon"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions braving southern Kalimdor, Feathermoon Stronghold provides vital supplies, flight paths, and quest headquarters amidst the hostile wilderness of Feralas.",["race:NightElf"]="As the main Sentinel encampment south of Ashenvale, this fortress represents the resolve of the kaldorei to safeguard Kalimdor under the leadership of General Shandris Feathermoon."},kw={"feathermoon","feathermoon stronghold","feralas","forgotten coast","kaldorei","moonwell","sardor isle","sentinels","shandris feathermoon"},rel={"npc:shandris-feathermoon","zone:feralas","subzone:sardor-isle","subzone:forgotten-coast","topic:alliance"},src={"Feathermoon Stronghold (Classic)"}}
E["subzone:feathermoon-stronghold-classic"] = {t="subzone",n="Feathermoon Stronghold (Classic)",z="feralas",s="Feathermoon Stronghold is a fortified night elf bastion situated on Sardor Isle off the western shores of Feralas. Established by General Shandris Feathermoon, it serves as the Alliance's primary staging ground and military anchor in southern Kalimdor.",h="Feathermoon Stronghold is a fortified night elf bastion situated on Sardor Isle off the western shores of...",sec={{t="Sentinel Bastion of the South",b="Perched on Sardor Isle just off the Forgotten Coast, Feathermoon Stronghold stands as a crucial bulwark for the Night Elves and the broader Alliance. Built under the direction of General Shandris Feathermoon—Tyrande Whisperwind's trusted lieutenant for ten millennia—the fortress projects Sentinel power deep into southern Kalimdor. Its isolated island geography shields it from the beasts, ogres, and Horde interlopers prowling the primeval jungles of mainland Feralas.",sp=0},{t="Lifeline Across the Waves",b="Given its insular position, Feathermoon relies heavily on sea and air links to maintain logistics. A small passenger boat regularly shuttles travellers across the channel between Sardor Isle and the Forgotten Coast dock. For distant travel, a dedicated hippogryph roost ties the stronghold directly to major Alliance hubs, including Thalanaar on the Thousand Needles border, Nijel's Point in the Desolace highlands, and Auberdine in the north.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do you reach Feathermoon Stronghold from mainland Feralas?",a="Travelers can catch a ferry boat that departs from a dock on the Forgotten Coast directly across the strait, or simply swim the narrow channel to Sardor Isle. Alliance members can also fly in by hippogryph once the flight master is discovered.",al={"how to get to feathermoon","feathermoon boat","getting to sardor isle"}},{q="Who commands Feathermoon Stronghold?",a="The outpost is commanded by General Shandris Feathermoon, the high-ranking leader of the Sentinels and long-serving military subordinate to High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind.",al={"who leads feathermoon","feathermoon leader","shandris feathermoon"}},{q="Why is the stronghold located on an island instead of the mainland?",a="Sardor Isle provides natural isolation and security from the dense threats of the Feralas wilderness, including aggressive wildlife, primal ruins, and hostile forces, allowing the Sentinels to maintain an unassailable redoubt.",al={"why on sardor isle","why island fortress","feathermoon location lore"}},{q="Where do flight paths from Feathermoon connect?",a="Feathermoon's hippogryph master maintains routes connecting across western Kalimdor, including Auberdine in Darkshore, Nijel's Point in Desolace, Thalanaar in Feralas, and Cenarion Hold in Silithus.",al={"feathermoon flight master","where do feathermoon hippogryphs go"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Feathermoon Stronghold represents the primary safe haven, vendor post, and staging center for Alliance operations deep within southern Kalimdor.",["race:NightElf"]="The stronghold serves as the southern military seat of General Shandris Feathermoon and the Sentinels, standing as a vital guardian of the ancient wilderness."},kw={"alliance","feathermoon stronghold","feralas","forgotten coast","sardor isle","sentinels","shandris feathermoon"},rel={"subzone:sardor-isle","zone:feralas","subzone:forgotten-coast","topic:sentinels","topic:alliance","subzone:thalanaar","subzone:nijel-s-point","subzone:auberdine"},src={"Feathermoon Stronghold (Classic)"}}
E["subzone:feral-scar-vale"] = {t="subzone",n="Feral Scar Vale",z="feralas",s="Feral Scar Vale is a rocky gorge tucked within the High Wilderness of western Feralas. Overrun by territorial Feral Scar yetis, its cavernous tunnels are notoriously perilous to travelers who venture off the overgrown forest trails.",h="Feral Scar Vale is a rocky gorge tucked within the High Wilderness of western Feralas.",sec={{t="Lair of the Yetis",b="Situated amid the thick foliage and sheer cliffs of the High Wilderness, Feral Scar Vale serves as the primary den for the savage Feral Scar yetis. While yetis are common in the snowy peaks of Alterac and Dun Morogh, these primal brutes have adapted completely to the wild, humid climate of Feralas. They fiercely defend the vale's cave network, hoarding bone trophies and aggressively driving off any intruders who wander into their hunting grounds.",sp=0},{t="Curiosities in the Caves",b="Beyond the primal danger of the yetis, the deeper recesses of Feral Scar Vale hide unexpected oddities. Gnomish engineering distress signals have occasionally been tracked into these dark caverns, where lost exploratory devices—such as stranded robotic survey chickens—have ended up trapped by the ferocious beasts, awaiting activation and extraction.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What kind of creatures live in Feral Scar Vale?",a="The vale is dominated by Feral Scar yetis, massive and territorial apex predators who nest inside the rocky caves and patrol the surrounding forest.",al={"feral scar vale mobs","what is in feral scar vale","vale creatures"}},{q="Where is Feral Scar Vale located?",a="Feral Scar Vale lies in western Feralas, nestled within the region known as the High Wilderness, south of the main road cutting through the rainforest canopy.",al={"feral scar vale location","where is feral scar vale","how to find feral scar vale"}},{q="Why are there yetis in a lush rainforest?",a="While yetis are typically associated with snowy mountains, the ancient and untamed wilds of Kalimdor host distinct subspecies, such as the Feral Scar yetis, that have thrived in dense forest valleys for generations.",al={"why yetis in feralas","jungle yetis","feralas yeti lore"}},{q="What is the mechanical chicken inside the cave?",a="Deep inside one of the vale's caves lies Homing Robot OOX-22/FE, an autonomous mechanical survey chicken crafted by gnome engineers that crashed and became stranded behind the yeti lines.",al={"oox-22/fe","robot chicken feralas","homing robot feral scar vale"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Tucked away in the yeti tunnels is a stranded gnome homing robot, requiring an engineer's touch and an emergency beacon to safely extract it back to civilization.",["class:Hunter"]="The hulking Feral Scar yetis that stalk these cliffs offer an imposing test of wilderness tracking and big-game hunting amidst the dense canopies of the High Wilderness."},kw={"feral scar vale","feralas","high wilderness","homing robot","oox-22/fe","yeti"},rel={"zone:feralas","subzone:high-wilderness"},src={"Feral Scar Vale"}}
E["subzone:forgotten-coast"] = {t="subzone",n="Forgotten Coast",z="feralas",s="The Forgotten Coast forms the wild western shore of Feralas, where the ancient rainforest meets the Veiled Sea. Lumbering sea giants and water elementals roam this battered strand.",h="The Forgotten Coast forms the wild western shore of Feralas, where the ancient rainforest meets the Veiled...",sec={{t="Edge of the Rainforest",b="Stretching along the western edge of Feralas, the Forgotten Coast is a windswept shoreline confronting the expanse of the Veiled Sea. Unlike the dense canopy inland, this frontier is exposed to the elements and dominated by towering sea giants and roving water elementals pacing the surf. Travelers emerging from the forest canopy must contend with these primeval coastal guardians while navigating access to the sea, where ferry connections link to the night elven bastion of Sardor Isle.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What threats wander the Forgotten Coast?",a="The shoreline is patrolled by immense sea giants and restless water elementals emerging from the Veiled Sea.",al={"monsters on forgotten coast","forgotten coast dangers","what is on the coast"}},{q="How do you reach Feathermoon Stronghold from here?",a="The shore serves as the primary mainland departure point across the channel to Sardor Isle, where the Night Elves maintain Feathermoon Stronghold. A small ferry dock on the coast provides safe passage across the water away from the dangerous sea giants.",al={"how to get to feathermoon","boat to feathermoon","feathermoon ferry"}},{q="Is the Forgotten Coast accessible to the Horde?",a="Yes. While the southern road leads directly toward the night elven crossing to Feathermoon Stronghold, a secondary path cuts down to the coast further to the north, allowing Horde travelers to reach the shore without straying into Alliance sentinels.",al={"horde access forgotten coast","how does horde reach coast","safe horde path forgotten coast"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The coast is a vital conduit between the Kalimdor mainland and Feathermoon Stronghold on Sardor Isle, requiring vigilance against wandering sea giants.",["faction:Horde"]="Approaching the coast requires care, as the southern trail nears night elven ferry points; navigating the northern forest pathways provides safer passage to the water."},kw={"feralas","forgotten coast","sardor isle","sea giants","veiled sea"},rel={"zone:feralas","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","topic:horde"},src={"Forgotten Coast"}}
E["subzone:frayfeather-highlands"] = {t="subzone",n="Frayfeather Highlands",z="feralas",s="The Frayfeather Highlands form an elevated wilderness in the dense forests of Feralas. This remote plateau is the ancestral roost and nesting ground of the wild Frayfeather hippogryphs. Intrepid scavengers and naturalists often brave its territorial flocks in search of intact hippogryph eggs.",h="The Frayfeather Highlands form an elevated wilderness in the dense forests of Feralas.",sec={{t="Aerie of the Hippogryphs",b="Rising above the surrounding forest floor of Feralas, the Frayfeather Highlands are dominated by steep slopes and crags where wild hippogryphs raise their broods. The local flocks are notoriously aggressive toward intruders, fiercely defending the scattered nests tucked among the rock shelves. Because these beasts are so well adapted to the rugged cliffs, their nesting grounds have drawn significant interest from outsiders—most notably goblin entrepreneurs in distant Gadgetzan who seek unhatched eggs for study and profit.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures live in the Frayfeather Highlands?",a="The highlands are primarily home to large flocks of wild Frayfeather hippogryphs, which nest across the high rock faces and aggressively defend their territory from trespassers.",al={"frayfeather wildlife","what is here","frayfeather beasts"}},{q="Why are travelers interested in the hippogryph nests?",a="The nests contain rare hippogryph eggs. Adventurers collect these viable eggs and deliver them across Tanaris to Gadgetzan, where goblins process them in the Super Egg-O-Matic for research and profit.",al={"hippogryph eggs","egg quest","why steal eggs"}},{q="Where are the Frayfeather Highlands located?",a="The highlands are situated in the southern reaches of Feralas, elevated above the primary jungle canopy and characterized by craggy hillsides and open nesting perches.",al={"frayfeather location","where is frayfeather highlands","how to find frayfeather"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Night elves revere hippogryphs as sacred companions of Elune, making the wild nests in Feralas an important natural habitat worthy of preservation from reckless exploitation.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold the wild beasts of Kalimdor in high regard and view the undisturbed aeries of the Frayfeather Highlands as a pure reflection of the forest's primal vitality."},kw={"eggs","feralas","frayfeather","gadgetzan","highlands","hippogryph","nests"},rel={"zone:feralas","subzone:gadgetzan"},src={"Frayfeather Highlands"}}
E["subzone:gordok-commons"] = {t="subzone",n="Gordok Commons",z="feralas",s="The Gordok Commons comprise the fortified northern quarter of the ancient Highborne ruins of Dire Maul. Under the rule of King Gordok, this sprawling stone complex serves as the seat of power for the elite warrior caste of the Gordunni ogres.",h="The Gordok Commons comprise the fortified northern quarter of the ancient Highborne ruins of Dire Maul.",sec={{t="Seat of the Ogre King",b="Occupying what was once an aristocratic wing of Eldre'Thalas, the Gordok Commons have been thoroughly desecrated and refitted for ogre tastes. Grand night elven pillars and arched passageways now house armories, crude barricades, and training grounds for the Gordok—the fiercest, most disciplined fighters among the Gordunni clan. At the deepest end of the wing lies Gordok's Seat, where King Gordok presides over his brutes through sheer force and intimidation.",sp=0},{t="Law of Succession",b="Gordok culture operates entirely on brutal precedent: might makes right. According to clan tradition, whoever slays the sitting monarch claims the title of King Gordok, earning immediate obedience from any surviving captains and guards. Astute intruders exploit this custom by sneaking or scheming past the king's lieutenants rather than slaying them outright. If a challenger executes only the king, the surviving guards will recognize the victor's authority and present lavish tributes rather than fight to avenge their former ruler.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Gordok Commons located?",a="The Commons occupy the northern quarter of Dire Maul in Feralas. To reach them, enter the sprawling ruin through the Broken Commons and proceed through the massive stone corridors to the northern entrance.",al={"gordok commons location","where is dire maul north","how to find gordok commons"}},{q="Who are the Gordok ogres?",a="The Gordok are the elite warrior caste of the Gordunni ogre clan. Unlike their scattered, feral kin prowling the Feralas wilderness, the Gordok within the Commons are organized, heavily armed, and bound to a strict military chain of command under their king.",al={"who are the gordok","gordok clan","gordunni elite"}},{q="How does ogre leadership work in the Commons?",a="Gordok rule is decided by combat. Whoever kills the reigning King Gordok instantly claims the crown. Once the king falls, the remaining ogres surrender and honor the conqueror as their rightful sovereign.",al={"how to become king of gordok","gordok succession","king gordok lore"}},{q="Why do adventurers leave the ogre guards alive?",a="If an intruder reaches King Gordok and defeats him without slaying his lieutenants, those surviving commanders submit to the new king. In return for showing restraint and claiming the throne directly, the new ruler is awarded valuable tribute offerings from the garrison.",al={"why tribute run","sparing the guards","gordok tribute lore"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The goblin prisoner Knot Thimblejack relies on resourceful engineers and tinkerers within the Commons to scavenge supplies, mend broken traps, and devise clever distractions against the ogre guards."},kw={"dire maul north","eldre'thalas","gordok","gordok commons","king gordok","knot thimblejack","mizzle","tribute run"},rel={"subzone:dire-maul","zone:feralas","subzone:eldreth-row","subzone:maul-subzone","topic:goblin"},src={"Gordok Commons"}}
E["subzone:gordunni-outpost"] = {t="subzone",n="Gordunni Outpost",z="feralas",s="Tucked into the rugged cliffs north of Lariss Pavilion, the Gordunni Outpost serves as a fortified camp for the brutish Gordunni ogres of Feralas. The clan's corrupting influence has choked the once-vibrant wilderness here, leaving the surrounding earth dry, withered, and brown.",h="Tucked into the rugged cliffs north of Lariss Pavilion, the Gordunni Outpost serves as a fortified camp for...",sec={{t="A Blighted Foothold",b="Carved into the northern mountains above the Lariss Pavilion, the Gordunni Outpost stands out as a stark scar against the lush canopy of Feralas. Wherever the Gordunni ogres settle, their reckless magical channeling and destructive habits sap the vitality of the wild, leaving the local flora dead and the hillsides barren. The outpost consists of dirt trails, a shallow entrance cave, and a larger ogre mound burrowed deep into the rear cliffs. Patrolled by heavily armed hillguards, cunning channelers, and ogre tamers, the camp also holds dangerous trophies—including a captured sasquatch named Bigfist kept in crude confinement near the deeper den.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the landscape withered around this outpost?",a="The Gordunni clan exerts a harsh, corruptive toll on the surrounding environment. Their reckless sorcery and destructive occupation drain the natural vitality of the soil, causing the normally verdant jungle flora to wilt into dry brown scrubland.",al={"why is it brown","dead grass feralas","ogre corruption"}},{q="What kinds of ogres occupy the Gordunni Outpost?",a="The outpost is defended by Gordunni Hillguards, Gordunni Channelers wielding crude offensive magic, and Gordunni Tamers who watch over their camp and captive beasts.",al={"what mobs are here","gordunni types","who lives here"}},{q="Who is Bigfist?",a="Bigfist is a massive sasquatch held captive by the Gordunni ogres near the entrance of their rear cave. The ogre tamers keep him bound as a trophy or experimental quarry.",al={"caged sasquatch","who is bigfist","ogre prisoner"}},{q="Where is the Gordunni Outpost located?",a="The outpost is nestled high in the mountain ridge directly north of Lariss Pavilion in eastern Feralas.",al={"where is gordunni outpost","outpost location","how to get to gordunni outpost"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The Gordunni's presence is a grievous offense to nature, transforming the fertile jungle canopy into an unnaturally withered, barren wasteland.",["class:Hunter"]="The outpost is occupied by ogre tamers who capture and abuse local mountain beasts, keeping creatures like the great sasquatch Bigfist bound in cages."},kw={"bigfist","channeler","feralas","gordunni","hillguard","lariss pavilion","ogre","outpost","tamer"},rel={"zone:feralas","subzone:lariss-pavilion"},src={"Gordunni Outpost"}}
E["subzone:grimtotem-compound"] = {t="subzone",n="Grimtotem Compound",z="feralas",s="The Grimtotem Compound is a fortified tribal settlement nestled in the central wilds of Feralas, just east of the elven ruins of Dire Maul. Occupied by the aggressive and insular Grimtotem clan, the encampment serves as a base for their mysterious and destructive operations in the region.",h="The Grimtotem Compound is a fortified tribal settlement nestled in the central wilds of Feralas, just east of...",sec={{t="A Bastion of the Black Tribe",b="Spanning two encampments east of Dire Maul, the Grimtotem Compound establishes a firm foothold for the Grimtotem clan in Feralas. Unlike the tauren aligned with Cairne Bloodhoof in Thunder Bluff, the Grimtotem here operate independently and with hostility toward outsiders. In the southern half of the settlement, they keep captive sprite darters locked inside a large wooden cage for reasons of their own, while rogue gnolls stalk the fringes of their northern perimeter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in the Grimtotem Compound?",a="The settlement belongs to the Grimtotem clan, an aggressive and secretive tribe of tauren known for their xenophobia and ruthless methods. They operate separately from the Horde-allied tribes in Mulgore.",al={"who is here","grimtotem compound mobs","who controls grimtotem compound"}},{q="Why are sprite darters caged in the compound?",a="The Grimtotem have captured native sprite darters and locked them in a massive cage in the southern village. Why they hold these creatures is not recorded.",al={"why are faerie dragons caged","caged sprite darters","grimtotem sprite darters"}},{q="Where is the Grimtotem Compound located?",a="The compound is situated in central Feralas, just east of the ancient Highborne ruins of Dire Maul, with wild gnoll packs camped nearby to the northeast.",al={"grimtotem compound location","where is grimtotem compound"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The Grimtotem clan pays nominal homage to Cairne Bloodhoof, but places like this compound reveal their true, untamed ambition far from the watchful eyes of Thunder Bluff.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Grimtotem are relentlessly hostile to the Night Elves and their allies, making this settlement a dangerous obstacle in the heart of Feralas."},kw={"compound","dire maul","feralas","gnolls","grimtotem","sprite darter","tauren"},rel={"zone:feralas","subzone:dire-maul","npc:sprite-darter","topic:tauren","topic:gnoll"},src={"Grimtotem Compound"}}
E["subzone:high-wilderness"] = {t="subzone",n="High Wilderness",z="feralas",s="The High Wilderness is an expansive, untamed stretch of primordial forest covering much of western Feralas. Bordered by the Verdantis River to the east and the Forgotten Coast to the west, it shelters a wide array of wildlife, wandering treants, and dangerous beasts beneath its towering emerald canopy.",h="The High Wilderness is an expansive, untamed stretch of primordial forest covering much of western Feralas.",sec={{t="The Primordial Canopy",b="Stretching across the western half of Feralas, the High Wilderness represents the quintessential untamed wilderness of southern Kalimdor. Thick foliage and colossal trees block out much of the sky, creating a lush expanse teeming with wolves, bears, hippogryphs, and yetis. Ancient treants wander among the roots, while aggressive ogre clans establish footholds in the shaded clearings. Navigating this vast green expanse requires vigilance, as the dense brush hides both natural predators and lingering primeval hazards.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the High Wilderness located?",a="The High Wilderness encompasses the vast forestlands of western Feralas. It lies west of the Verdantis River and extends all the way to the cliffs and shores bordering the Forgotten Coast.",al={"high wilderness location","where is high wilderness","high wilderness feralas"}},{q="What creatures roam the High Wilderness?",a="The forest is home to dense populations of bears, wolves, hippogryphs, and feral yetis. In addition to natural beasts, travelers regularly encounter roaming treants and aggressive ogres lurking under the canopy.",al={"high wilderness wildlife","creatures in high wilderness","beasts feralas"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The ancient treants and vibrant wildlife of the High Wilderness showcase Kalimdor's natural primal strength, untouched by the civilization of the eastern lands.",["class:Hunter"]="Dense populations of fierce bears, wolves, and wild hippogryphs make the High Wilderness an exceptional proving ground for tracking and taming formidable beasts."},kw={"feralas","forgotten coast","high wilderness","hippogryphs","treants","verdantis river","yetis"},rel={"zone:feralas","subzone:forgotten-coast"},src={"High Wilderness"}}
E["subzone:isle-of-dread"] = {t="subzone",n="Isle of Dread",z="feralas",s="The Isle of Dread is a desolate, cliff-bound island situated in the Great Sea off the southwestern coast of Feralas, south of Sardor Isle. It is notorious for sheltering monstrous two-headed chimaeroks and an entrenched coven of hostile naga hidden within its subterranean sea caves.",h="The Isle of Dread is a desolate, cliff-bound island situated in the Great Sea off the southwestern coast of...",sec={{t="A Land of Monsters and Tides",b="Rising out of the crashing surf of the South Seas, the Isle of Dread lives up to its ominous name. Ringed by sheer cliffs, the island's interior valley is only accessible through a narrow pathway on its southeastern coast. Within this enclosed highland roams a lethal population of chimaeroks—ravenous, two-headed beasts empowered by ambient arcane energies. These beasts are led by the monstrous Lord Lakmaeran, making the island a deadly deathtrap for unwary explorers who cross the channel from Sardor Isle.",sp=0},{t="The Northern Caverns",b="While the inland plateau belongs to the chimaeroks, the island's northern shore conceals a cavern system occupied by the Hatecrest naga. Led by Lord Shalzaru, these serpent-folk lurk within deep submerged chambers, plotting against the night elven sentinels stationed at nearby Feathermoon Stronghold. Their subterranean lair includes hidden underwater passages that wind into secluded grottoes, serving as a heavily fortified outpost away from mainland scrutiny.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do you reach the interior of the Isle of Dread?",a="The island is surrounded by high, sheer cliffs that block ascent from almost every shoreline. The only way to access the central plateau on foot is via a natural path located along the southeastern side of the island.",al={"isle of dread entrance","how to get up isle of dread","climb isle of dread"}},{q="What kinds of creatures inhabit the island?",a="The high plateau is populated by fierce chimaeroks, including arcane chimaeroks and massive devourers led by the apex beast Lord Lakmaeran. Along the northern coast, deep sea caverns are infested with hostile Hatecrest naga.",al={"isle of dread mobs","monsters on isle of dread","chimaeroks feralas"}},{q="Who leads the naga in the sea caves?",a="The coven of naga occupying the northern cave complex is led by Lord Shalzaru. Their presence poses an active threat to the nearby night elves at Feathermoon Stronghold.",al={"isle of dread naga boss","lord shalzaru cave","naga leader feralas island"}},{q="What makes chimaerok meat so famous?",a="Chimaeroks yield exceptionally rich tenderloins prized by master gourmands. Culinary masters like Dirge Quikcleave seek out meat from the island—including the prized carcass of Lord Lakmaeran—to craft legendary feasts.",al={"chimaerok tenderloin","dirge kickin chimaerok chops","isle of dread food"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="The chimaeroks of the Isle of Dread are the only known source of Chimaerok Tenderloin, the key ingredient for Dirge Quikcleave's legendary Chimaerok Chops.",["faction:Alliance"]="The night elven sentinels at nearby Feathermoon Stronghold keep a watchful eye on the isle, seeking brave champions to strike at Lord Shalzaru and halt the naga presence off their shores."},kw={"chimaerok","feathermoon","feralas","isle of dread","lakmaeran","naga","sardor isle","shalzaru","szallah"},rel={"zone:feralas","subzone:sardor-isle","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","npc:lord-shalzaru","topic:naga"},src={"Isle of Dread"}}
E["subzone:lariss-pavilion"] = {t="subzone",n="Lariss Pavilion",z="feralas",s="Lariss Pavilion is an ancient elven structure tucked into the wilderness of Feralas just north of Camp Mojache. While once a peaceful retreat of classical night elf architecture, the surrounding forest has grown dangerous due to corrupted dryads, and an exiled Highborne mage now bides his time within its shade.",h="Lariss Pavilion is an ancient elven structure tucked into the wilderness of Feralas just north of Camp...",sec={{t="A Ruin of the Highborne",b="Standing quietly on the bluffs north of Camp Mojache, Lariss Pavilion showcases the graceful stonework and towering archways of the ancient kaldorei empire. In its prime, it served the great city of Eldre'Thalas, now known as Dire Maul. Today, it offers a sheltered overlook above the dense canopy of Feralas, but the peace here is frail: the once-gentle dryads wandering the surrounding glades have fallen to madness and corruption, turning fiercely hostile to anyone who draws near.",sp=0},{t="Azj'Tordin and the Hidden Passage",b="The pavilion's most notable resident is the elusive elf Azj'Tordin. Having broken away from Prince Tortheldrin's decadent rule within Dire Maul, Azj'Tordin escaped the ruins through a secret passage connecting the pavilion directly to the ancient city's underbelly. However, his quiet exile has been disrupted: an erratic imp named Pusillin stole his treasured book of incantations, leaving the exile seeking outside aid to recover it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Lariss Pavilion located?",a="Lariss Pavilion is situated on the elevated forested terrain in eastern Feralas, just north of the Horde outpost of Camp Mojache.",al={"lariss pavilion location","where is lariss pavilion","how to get to lariss pavilion"}},{q="Who is Azj'Tordin?",a="Azj'Tordin is an ancient Highborne sorcerer who fled the tyrant Prince Tortheldrin inside Dire Maul. He now camps at the pavilion, seeking adventurers to help reclaim a stolen book of incantations from a mischievous imp.",al={"azjtordin","who is the elf at lariss pavilion","lariss pavilion quest giver"}},{q="Why are the dryads around the pavilion hostile?",a="The dryads roaming the woods near the pavilion have succumbed to corruption creeping through the wilds of Feralas, transforming normally reclusive guardians of nature into vicious attackers.",al={"angry dryads","why are dryads attacking","corrupted dryads feralas"}},{q="How does the pavilion connect to Dire Maul?",a="A concealed backdoor at the base of Lariss Pavilion leads straight into Dire Maul, serving as the escape route Azj'Tordin used to slip away from his brethren.",al={"dire maul backdoor","dire maul shortcut","secret passage"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="For practitioners of the arcane, the solitary Highborne Azj'Tordin represents a living relic of Eldre'Thalas's ancient, unchecked spellcraft.",["race:NightElf"]="Night elves will find the pavilion a bitter sight—not only is its beauty shadowed by the legacy of Highborne hubris, but the surrounding dryad kin are suffering from dark corruption."},kw={"azj'tordin","camp mojache","dire maul","dryads","feralas","highborne","lariss pavilion","pusillin","xerash fireblade"},rel={"subzone:dire-maul","zone:feralas","subzone:camp-mojache","topic:highborne","topic:night-elf"},src={"Lariss Pavilion"}}
E["subzone:lower-wilds"] = {t="subzone",n="Lower Wilds",z="feralas",s="The Lower Wilds form the eastern threshold of Feralas, where the humid forests meet the arid canyons of Thousand Needles. The main road cutting through these woods connects Thalanaar at the border to the settlements further west, flanked by ancient greenery and unpredictable woodland creatures.",h="The Lower Wilds form the eastern threshold of Feralas, where the humid forests meet the arid canyons of...",sec={{t="The Eastern Frontier",b="Spanning the eastern reaches of Feralas, the Lower Wilds serve as the natural transition between the sun-baked ravines of Thousand Needles and the deep, primordial jungle to the west. Travelers entering the zone must traverse this stretch of forest along the main highway, past the elven outpost of Thalanaar guarding the mountain pass. The dense canopies here house ancient treants, alongside indigenous wildlife that makes straying from the beaten path perilous.",sp=0},{t="A Contested Highway",b="Because it links the southern wilderness to the eastern territories, the Lower Wilds see frequent movement of travelers, scouts, and couriers. While the night elves hold the gateway at Thalanaar, the Horde maintains Camp Mojache further inland. The road winding through the Lower Wilds is therefore a critical lifeline for anyone moving supplies across southern Kalimdor, fraught with both nature's hazards and faction tensions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Lower Wilds located?",a="The Lower Wilds make up the easternmost expanse of Feralas. They immediately border Thousand Needles, stretching westward from the mountain threshold of Thalanaar toward the interior of the jungle.",al={"lower wilds location","where is lower wilds","how to get to lower wilds"}},{q="What creatures live in the Lower Wilds?",a="The woodlands are inhabited by ancient forest guardians, including treants, as well as the native predatory beasts that roam the feral forest floor.",al={"lower wilds mobs","what is in lower wilds","lower wilds enemies"}},{q="Which settlements are close to the Lower Wilds?",a="At the far eastern border sits the night elf outpost of Thalanaar, serving as the Alliance's primary entrance into Feralas. Further west along the road lies the Horde settlement of Camp Mojache.",al={"lower wilds towns","camps near lower wilds","horde alliance towns lower wilds"}},{q="Is the road through the Lower Wilds safe?",a="The road itself is the safest route through the region, but travelers should stay alert. Straying off the path invites attacks from aggressive forest fauna and territorial guardians, and rival faction skirmishes occasionally spill across the highway.",al={"is lower wilds safe","lower wilds road safety"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers leaving Thousand Needles, the Lower Wilds are their first sight of Feralas, anchored by the night elf frontier outpost at Thalanaar.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde messengers and supply lines traveling to Camp Mojache must navigate the length of the Lower Wilds after descending from the border canyons."},kw={"camp mojache","eastern feralas","feralas","lower wilds","thalanaar","thousand needles","treants"},rel={"zone:feralas","subzone:thalanaar","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:camp-mojache"},src={"Lower Wilds"}}
E["subzone:maul-subzone"] = {t="subzone",n="Maul (subzone)",z="feralas",s="The Maul is a sunken fighting arena situated in the Broken Commons outside the ruins of Dire Maul in Feralas. Formerly a grand venue of ancient elven Eldre'Thalas, the pit is now an uncontrolled bloodsport ring where wanderers fight for glory or survival against fierce beasts and rival champions.",h="The Maul is a sunken fighting arena situated in the Broken Commons outside the ruins of Dire Maul in Feralas.",sec={{t="The Sunken Pit",b="Carved deep into the stone of the Broken Commons, the Maul once served the Highborne of Eldre'Thalas as a theater or ceremonial arena. Following the Sundering and the subsequent occupation by the Gordok ogres, the pit devolved into a raw colosseum. Like the notorious Gurubashi Arena in distant Stranglethorn Vale, entering the sands of the Maul suspends all allegiances, casting combatants into a lawless free-for-all where faction lines dissolve and survival depends purely on martial strength.",sp=0},{t="Beasts and Bloodshed",b="Challengers who descend into the arena must mind their approach. While daring fighters often leap directly from the high ledges of the commons, the fall carries brutal impact. A safer western archway leads through tunnels lined with slumbering Gordok hyenas, providing the only foot exit out of the fighting floor. At irregular intervals, dangerous beasts and notorious gladiators emerge into the pit, making every descent an unpredictable trial of steel and instinct.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why can I attack members of my own faction here?",a="The Maul functions as a lawless fighting pit, much like the Gurubashi Arena in Stranglethorn Vale. Upon stepping onto its sands, standard faction treaties and truces no longer apply, flagging combatants for free-for-all combat against anyone not directly in their party.",al={"ffa pvp dire maul","free for all arena","why can i hit horde"}},{q="How do I safely enter and leave the Maul?",a="While you can jump directly down from the Broken Commons, doing so causes significant falling damage. The safest path is through a doorway on the western side of the commons, leading through a tunnel past sleeping Gordok hyenas. This tunnel is also the only way to climb back out on foot.",al={"how to get into the maul","maul entrance","exit maul"}},{q="What kinds of enemies appear in the arena?",a="Aside from rival adventurers, exotic and vicious threats are known to prowl into the arena pit, including the massive fungal giant Mushgog, the chimera known as The Razza, and the fierce gladiator Skarr the Unbreakable.",al={"arena rares","who spawns in the maul","maul bosses"}},{q="What was this arena originally used for?",a="Before the Sundering shattered ancient Kalimdor, this stone colosseum belonged to the great Highborne city of Eldre'Thalas. The invading Gordok ogres repurpose the ancient elven architecture into a blood arena suited to their savage tastes.",al={"lore of the maul","who built the maul","eldre'thalas arena"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="For warriors seeking genuine combat outside organized battlegrounds, the Maul offers raw, unvarnished bloodsport where only personal prowess and thick armor dictate survival.",["race:NightElf"]="Watching the proud architecture of ancient Eldre'Thalas reduced to an ogre-infested execution pit is a stark and painful reminder of how far the Highborne civilization fell."},kw={"broken commons","dire maul arena","eldre'thalas","feralas","ffa pvp","mushgog","skarr the unbreakable","the maul","the razza"},rel={"subzone:dire-maul","subzone:commons","zone:feralas","subzone:gurubashi-arena","zone:stranglethorn"},src={"Maul (subzone)"}}
E["subzone:oneiros"] = {t="subzone",n="Oneiros",z="feralas",s="Oneiros is a sprawling expanse of ancient night elven ruins located south of Jademir Lake in northern Feralas. Tied intimately to the nearby portals leading toward the realm of Ysera, its moss-covered stones are guarded by elite green dragonkin.",h="Oneiros is a sprawling expanse of ancient night elven ruins located south of Jademir Lake in northern Feralas.",sec={{t="Ruins Beneath the Dream",b="Stretching across the dense forest floor of northern Feralas, the crumbling stone arches and column fragments of Oneiros hint at an ancient Kaldorei settlement abandoned millennia ago. In the present day, nature has reclaimed the structures, entwining them with massive roots and verdant overgrowth. Elite guardians of the Green Dragonflight relentlessly patrol the shaded paths and broken plazas, warding mortals away from ancient secrets.",sp=0},{t="Echoes and Corruption",b="The spiritual link between Oneiros and the Emerald Dream makes the region volatile. Dragonkin loyal to the Dreamer maintain a watchful vigil around its boundaries, yet darkness stirs beyond the veil. Mortals wandering into Oneiros must contend with powerful dragonspawn who view any intruder as a potential threat to the delicate wards holding back corruption.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Oneiros located?",a="Oneiros lies in northern Feralas, directly south of Jademir Lake and north of the main thoroughfares through the forest. It is situated near the Great Tree that borders the Emerald Dream portal.",al={"oneiros location","where is oneiros","find oneiros"}},{q="What creatures inhabit Oneiros?",a="The ruins are heavily patrolled by powerful green dragonspawn and dragonkin sworn to the Green Dragonflight. Travelers should approach with caution, as these sentinels are formidable elite guardians.",al={"oneiros mobs","enemies in oneiros","who lives in oneiros"}},{q="Why are there night elf ruins here?",a="Oneiros is an ancient night elven settlement dating back to before the Great Sundering. Like much of Feralas, the civilization here crumbled over ten thousand years ago, leaving stone colonnades and courtyards reclaimed by nature.",al={"why are there ruins","kaldorei ruins feralas","oneiros history"}},{q="What is the connection between Oneiros and the Emerald Dream?",a="Its proximity to the great boughs connecting Kalimdor to the Dream realm causes the boundaries between the physical world and the spirit world to blur.",al={"oneiros emerald dream","dream connection feralas"}},{q="Is there a safe place to rest nearby?",a="Not within the ruins themselves, which belong to the green dragonkin. Alliance travelers can retreat to Feathermoon Stronghold off the western coast, while the Horde shelters at Camp Mojache in eastern Feralas.",al={"safe camp near oneiros","dreamers rest feralas","friendly hub oneiros"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Druids hold Oneiros in deep reverence and concern, recognizing its ethereal connection to Ysera's domain and the lingering danger of Nightmare corruption.",["race:NightElf"]="For Night Elves, wandering through Oneiros is a solemn reminder of their ancient empire's reach and the vigilant guardianship of the green dragonkin."},kw={"dragonspawn","feralas","green dragonflight","jademir lake","oneiros"},rel={"zone:feralas","topic:emerald-dream","topic:night-elf"},src={"Oneiros"}}
E["subzone:rage-scar-hold"] = {t="subzone",n="Rage Scar Hold",z="feralas",s="Rage Scar Hold is a cavern carved into the wilderness of Feralas, situated on the mainland not far from Feathermoon Stronghold. It is notorious for housing some of the most vicious yetis in the region. Strangely, scattered books, symbols, and traces of night elven architecture deeper within suggest the den once served a far more civil purpose before the beasts claimed it.",h="Rage Scar Hold is a cavern carved into the wilderness of Feralas, situated on the mainland not far from...",sec={{t="A Beastly Domain",b="Carved into the rugged wilds of Feralas, Rage Scar Hold is dominated by savage yetis that attack anyone venturing near their lair. The creatures make the surrounding forest trails hazardous for both Alliance sentinels and passing travelers. While yetis are common to the untamed reaches of Kalimdor, the denizens of Rage Scar Hold stand out for their raw aggression and territorial ferocity.",sp=0},{t="Traces of the Past",b="Deeper in the dark corridors of the cave lie subtle clues of an older occupancy. Carved stonework and night elven architecture suggest the cavern was once a barrow den or an arcane sanctuary. Forgotten tomes and mystic markings remain among the dirt and bone, leaving travelers to wonder whether unfortunate scholars were slaughtered by the beasts or if the yetis somehow gravitate toward the lingering magic of the site.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Rage Scar Hold?",a="Rage Scar Hold is a subterranean cave network in Feralas, located on the mainland not far from Feathermoon Stronghold. It is currently overrun by an aggressive population of feral yetis.",al={"rage scar hold","what is this cave","feralas yeti cave"}},{q="Why are there books and symbols inside a yeti den?",a="Tomes, scrolls, and arcane symbols lie abandoned inside the hold. While it is unlikely the feral beasts are literate or studying spellcraft, the relics suggest the cave was once home to unfortunate spellcasters or night elf scholars who fell victim to the yetis.",al={"why books in yeti cave","are yetis studying magic","rage scar hold books"}},{q="Was this cavern built by night elves?",a="The interior features night elven stonework and cave structures reminiscent of a barrow den. No living kaldorei remain inside, implying that the original occupants either abandoned the site long ago or were wiped out when the yetis moved in.",al={"night elf architecture","was rage scar hold an elf barrow","barrow den feralas"}},{q="Are the yetis here different from others in Kalimdor?",a="The yetis of Rage Scar Hold are noted by local travelers as being among the fiercest and most aggressive of their kind in Feralas, defending their stolen subterranean home with feral brutality.",al={"feralas yetis","how dangerous are the yetis","rage scar beasts"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The desecration of what appears to be an ancient barrow den or sanctuary by filthy yetis is a bitter reminder of the wild perils reclaiming the kaldorei's historic lands.",["class:Mage"]="The presence of arcane symbols and abandoned tomes inside a beast's den raises troubling questions about who met their demise within the cavern's depths."},kw={"barrow den","feathermoon","feralas","magic books","rage scar hold","yeti"},rel={"zone:feralas","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","topic:night-elf"},src={"Rage Scar Hold"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-isildien"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Isildien",z="feralas",s="The Ruins of Isildien are the sprawling remains of an ancient night elven city in southwestern Feralas, destroyed ten millennia ago during the Great Sundering. Today, the overgrown stonework and cracked temple courtyards are occupied by brutish Gordunni ogres.",h="The Ruins of Isildien are the sprawling remains of an ancient night elven city in southwestern Feralas...",sec={{t="A Fallen City of the Kaldorei",b="Ten thousand years ago, before the world shattered, Isildien was a grand night elven settlement nestled in the primordial forests of ancient Kalimdor. Its graceful marble arches and grand terraces stood as monuments to kaldorei civilization and devotion. When the Well of Eternity imploded and tore the continents apart, Isildien fell into ruined desolation, smothered under millennia of untamed jungle growth. Dominating the upper terrace is a colossal domed structure remarkably reminiscent of Darnassus's Temple of the Moon, suggesting the city was once a significant sanctuary dedicated to Elune.",sp=0},{t="The Gordunni Stronghold",b="In the modern era, the elegant stonework of Isildien serves a far cruder purpose. The Gordunni ogres of Feralas have claimed the sprawling terraces and outcroppings as one of their primary settlements. The ogres have fortified the crumbling walkways, desecrating ancient plazas with crude bonfires, primitive barricades, and war banners, fiercely defending their stolen home against any outsiders who venture too close to the southern hills.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Isildien originally?",a="Isildien was a major night elven city built before the Great Sundering ten thousand years ago. It featured extensive stone plazas, multi-tiered terraces, and prominent temples before the cataclysm left it in ruins.",al={"what is isildien","isildien history","who built isildien"}},{q="Who controls the Ruins of Isildien now?",a="The ruins have been seized and fortified by the Gordunni ogres, who use the broken marble halls and natural vantage points as a stronghold in southern Feralas.",al={"who lives in isildien","isildien enemies","ogres in isildien"}},{q="What is the large circular pavilion at the top of the stairs?",a="The prominent circular pavilion closely mirrors the architecture of the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, strongly indicating that the upper dais was once a sacred sanctuary dedicated to the worship of Elune.",al={"isildien temple","round building in isildien","temple of elune feralas"}},{q="Is there anything hidden inside the ruins?",a="A cave is nestled into the eastern cliffs bordering the ruins, used by the resident ogres alongside the scattered stone terraces across the northern and southern grounds.",al={"isildien cave","secrets in isildien"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Walking through Isildien offers a bitter reminder of the heights of your pre-Sundering empire, now fallen into ruin and desecrated by barbaric Gordunni ogres.",["class:Priest"]="The great rotunda at the summit shares the architectural layout of Elune's high sanctuaries, echoing prayers offered to the White Lady ten thousand years ago."},kw={"elune","feralas","gordunni","isildien","kaldorei","ogres","sundering","temple of the moon"},rel={"zone:feralas","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","zone:darnassus","topic:elune"},src={"Ruins of Isildien"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-ravenwind"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Ravenwind",z="feralas",s="The Ruins of Ravenwind are the shattered remnants of an ancient Highborne city nestled in northern Feralas. Today, the crumbling marble structures are heavily infested by the vicious Northspring harpies and guarded by brooding dragonkin.",h="The Ruins of Ravenwind are the shattered remnants of an ancient Highborne city nestled in northern Feralas.",sec={{t="Echoes of the Highborne",b="Much like the great city of Dire Maul to the east, the Ruins of Ravenwind stand as a solemn monument to the height and hubris of ancient Highborne civilization before the Great Sundering. Long abandoned by its original kaldorei architects, the site has succumbed to creeping wild foliage, forgotten arcane altars, and the foul roosts of Northspring harpies who prey on anything wandering beneath the shattered arches.",sp=0},{t="A Confluence of Wild Dangers",b="Beyond the screeching harpies, Ravenwind is bordered by diverse and territorial threats. Fierce green dragonkin known as the Jaedemir circle the central groves and waterways, guarding ancient arboreal sites. Meanwhile, stray wanderers—from distracted night elf explorers to peculiar, solitary gnolls lingering nearby—frequently find themselves trapped in the crossfire of the ruins' lingering magics and wild predators.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who built the Ruins of Ravenwind?",a="The settlement was constructed millennia ago by the Highborne, the aristocratic upper class of the ancient kaldorei civilization. Following the Sundering, it fell into ruin much like Dire Maul and other elven monuments across Feralas.",al={"who built ravenwind","ravenwind history","ruins of ravenwind origins"}},{q="What currently infests the ruins?",a="The ruins are overrun by Northspring harpies, savage avian beasts who nest among the broken stonework. In addition, dragonkin of the Jaedemir flight prowl the surrounding waters and central grove, ferociously guarding the local flora.",al={"ravenwind monsters","what lives in ravenwind","ravenwind harpies"}},{q="Why does the Alliance visit this area?",a="Alliance scholars and sentinels stationed at Feathermoon Stronghold dispatch adventurers here to uncover lost arcane relics and interact with ancient altars to recharge powerful artifacts like the Stave of Equinex.",al={"alliance ravenwind quest","feathermoon ravenwind"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, these ruins serve as a bitter reminder of the reckless arcane empire that tore ancient Kalimdor apart, now desecrated by harpies and wild beasts.",["faction:Alliance"]="Outposts like Feathermoon Stronghold keep a careful eye on Ravenwind, sending brave scouts to recover potent magical relics before feral creatures or darker powers consume them."},kw={"feathermoon","feralas","harpies","highborne","jaedemir","northspring","ravenwind"},rel={"zone:feralas","subzone:dire-maul","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","topic:highborne","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance","topic:gnoll"},src={"Ruins of Ravenwind"}}
E["subzone:sardor-isle"] = {t="subzone",n="Sardor Isle",z="feralas",s="Sardor Isle is a lush island situated off the western coast of Feralas, north of the perilous Isle of Dread. It serves as the home to Feathermoon Stronghold, the primary night elven military bastion in southern Kalimdor. Despite the heavy sentinel presence, parts of the island remain prowled by wild beasts and hostile naga creeping up from the shallows.",h="Sardor Isle is a lush island situated off the western coast of Feralas, north of the perilous Isle of Dread.",sec={{t="Sentinel Bastion and Wild Shores",b="Resting across the water from mainland Feralas, Sardor Isle is anchored by Feathermoon Stronghold, an impressive elven garrison commanded by General Shandris Feathermoon. While the fortress itself is heavily fortified and linked to the mainland via regular ferry crossings, the broader island is far from tame. Roaming wolf packs claim the timbered slopes, while encroaching naga lurk along the rocky western and northern beaches, constantly testing the resolve of the night elven sentinels.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Sardor Isle located?",a="Sardor Isle lies off the western coast of Feralas in southern Kalimdor, just north of the Isle of Dread. It can be reached by a boat that runs from the Forgotten Coast on the mainland.",al={"sardor isle location","where is sardor","find sardor isle"}},{q="What is the main settlement on Sardor Isle?",a="The island is dominated by Feathermoon Stronghold, the primary fortress and staging ground of the night elves and the Alliance in Feralas, commanded by General Shandris Feathermoon.",al={"who lives on sardor isle","sardor isle town","night elf base sardor"}},{q="What threats are found on the island outside the stronghold?",a="Outside the protective walls of Feathermoon Stronghold, travelers face packs of wild wolves prowling the woods, as well as hostile naga lurking around the coastal reefs and beaches.",al={"sardor isle enemies","danger on sardor isle","monsters sardor"}},{q="How does Sardor Isle differ from the Isle of Dread?",a="Sardor Isle lies to the north and is heavily occupied by the night elves of Feathermoon Stronghold. The Isle of Dread sits further south and is a much harsher, untamed territory swarming with dangerous chimaeras and naga.",al={"sardor isle vs isle of dread","difference from isle of dread"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Sardor Isle is the Alliance's primary anchor of power in Feralas, offering safe harbor, supplies, and flight masters within Feathermoon Stronghold.",["race:NightElf"]="Under General Shandris Feathermoon, the Sentinels on Sardor Isle keep close watch over the ancient ruins and emergent naga threats throughout Feralas."},kw={"feathermoon stronghold","feralas","isle of dread","naga","sardor isle","sentinels","shandris feathermoon"},rel={"subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","zone:feralas","npc:shandris-feathermoon","subzone:isle-of-dread","topic:naga"},src={"Sardor Isle"}}
E["subzone:shalzaru-s-lair"] = {t="subzone",n="Shalzaru's Lair",z="feralas",s="Shalzaru's Lair is a sprawling, submerged cavern located at the northern tip of the Isle of Dread in Feralas. It serves as a major stronghold for the Hatecrest naga and shelters their formidable master, Shalzaru. From within these damp tunnels, the serpentine invaders coordinate their aggressive presence just south of Feathermoon Stronghold.",h="Shalzaru's Lair is a sprawling, submerged cavern located at the northern tip of the Isle of Dread in Feralas.",sec={{t="A Serpent Den in the Shallows",b="Carved into the rugged bluffs at the northern end of the Isle of Dread, Shalzaru's Lair is divided into a massive main cavern and a smaller auxiliary chamber, linked together by submerged subterranean waterways. The interior teems with Hatecrest serpent guards and spell-weaving sorceresses on high alert. Deep within the recesses dwells Lord Shalzaru, the serpentine overlord directing the Hatecrest brood across the island. Its proximity to Sardor Isle poses a direct, constant threat to the night elf Sentinels garrisoned at Feathermoon Stronghold just across the channel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Shalzaru's Lair located?",a="Shalzaru's Lair is located at the northern end of the Isle of Dread, an island sitting directly south of Sardor Isle and Feathermoon Stronghold off the western coast of Feralas.",al={"where is shalzaru's lair","shalzaru lair location","how to find shalzaru lair"}},{q="Who is Shalzaru?",a="Shalzaru is a powerful naga warlord and the master of the Hatecrest tribe inhabiting the Isle of Dread. He commands his forces from deep within the flooded caverns of the lair.",al={"who is shalzaru","shalzaru lore","boss of shalzaru lair"}},{q="What creatures inhabit this cave?",a="The cavern is swarming with Hatecrest naga, primarily vigilant Hatecrest Serpent Guards watching the dry paths and Hatecrest Sorceresses channeling magic across the subterranean waters.",al={"what enemies are in shalzaru lair","hatecrest naga cave mobs"}},{q="Why is this lair important to the local night elves?",a="Because the Isle of Dread sits directly across the water from Feathermoon Stronghold, the concentrated naga presence inside Shalzaru's Lair represents an immediate military threat to Shandris Feathermoon's forces and the security of Sardor Isle.",al={"why do night elves care about shalzaru","feathermoon naga threat"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Hatecrest buildup in this cavern threatens the supply lines and peace of Feathermoon Stronghold, making clearing Shalzaru and his brood a top priority for Sentinels and their allies.",["race:NightElf"]="The vile presence of naga desecrating the ancient coastal ruins of Feralas serves as an agonizing reminder of the Sundering and the Highborne's descent into monstrous corruption."},kw={"feathermoon stronghold","feralas","hatecrest","isle of dread","naga cave","shalzaru","shalzaru's lair"},rel={"subzone:isle-of-dread","topic:naga","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","zone:feralas"},src={"Shalzaru's Lair"}}
E["subzone:thalanaar"] = {t="subzone",n="Thalanaar",z="feralas",s="Thalanaar is a secluded night elf outpost nestled directly on the border between the verdant wilds of Feralas and the arid canyons of Thousand Needles. Serving as the primary eastern gateway into Feralas for the Alliance, it offers tired travelers a vital hippogryph roost and shelter beneath the canopy. Though modest in size, it acts as a critical link between mainland Kalimdor and the remote stronghold of Feathermoon.",h="Thalanaar is a secluded night elf outpost nestled directly on the border between the verdant wilds of Feralas...",sec={{t="Gateway to the Forgotten Wilderness",b="Perched at the natural choke point where the baked sandstone of Thousand Needles gives way to the dense, misty canopy of Feralas, Thalanaar is the first sign of night elven presence awaiting travelers from the east. It is little more than a fortified grove with a few sturdy pavilions and sentinels on watch, yet its position is vital. The outpost shelters Alliance scouts, couriers, and craftsmen venturing into the untamed forest, providing a secure staging ground against the beasts, ogres, and Horde forces roaming Southern Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="A Vital Aerial Link",b="Because overland travel through southern Kalimdor is fraught with peril, Thalanaar's primary function is logistics. Its hippogryph master links the secluded wilderness of Feralas directly to Theramore Isle in Dustwallow Marsh, Gadgetzan in Tanaris, and the island bastion of Feathermoon Stronghold to the west. Craftsmen also make pilgrimage here to seek out master leatherworkers who teach the ancient art of working wild hides under the woodland boughs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Thalanaar?",a="Thalanaar is a small night elven border camp situated at the eastern entrance to Feralas, right where the zone borders Thousand Needles. It acts as an Alliance outpost providing refuge, basic supplies, and flight transport.",al={"thalanaar overview","what is this place","thalanaar camp"}},{q="Where can the flight master send me?",a="Thalanaar's hippogryph roost connects to Feathermoon Stronghold off the western coast of Feralas, Theramore Isle in Dustwallow Marsh, and the neutral goblin port of Gadgetzan in Tanaris.",al={"thalanaar flight paths","where can i fly","flight master thalanaar"}},{q="Why would crafters seek out Thalanaar?",a="The outpost is the home of Caryssia Moonhunter, a master trainer dedicated to the elusive tradition of Tribal Leatherworking, drawing skilled artisans from across Kalimdor.",al={"thalanaar trainers","leatherworking thalanaar","caryssia moonhunter"}},{q="Is Thalanaar safe for Horde adventurers?",a="No. Thalanaar is firmly an Alliance settlement guarded by night elf sentinels who will attack any members of the Horde on sight.",al={"is thalanaar horde friendly","horde in thalanaar"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Thalanaar provides your first safe haven and reliable flight hub when marching westward from the treacherous mesas of Thousand Needles into the untamed jungles of Feralas.",["race:NightElf"]="The outpost serves as a sentinel station maintaining a vigilant eye over the border, welcoming kin back into the ancestral shadows of Feralas's ancient canopy."},kw={"caryssia moonhunter","feathermoon","feralas","flight master","sentinels","thalanaar","thousand needles","tribal leatherworking"},rel={"zone:feralas","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","subzone:theramore-isle","subzone:gadgetzan","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},src={"Thalanaar"}}
E["subzone:twin-colossals"] = {t="subzone",n="Twin Colossals",z="feralas",s="The Twin Colossals are a pair of towering, sheer-faced mesas that dominate the northwestern skyline of Feralas. Rising high above the canopy, the narrow passage between their sheer cliffs forms the primary overland route connecting Feralas with the arid wastes of Desolace to the north.",h="The Twin Colossals are a pair of towering, sheer-faced mesas that dominate the northwestern skyline of...",sec={{t="Pillars of the Rainforest",b="Towering over the western reaches of Feralas, the Twin Colossals stand as the highest landforms in the region. Their vertical rock faces cut a striking silhouette against the sky, serving as unmistakable landmarks for travelers venturing south out of Desolace. While the lower slopes merge into the dense jungle and the lands stretching toward the Forgotten Coast, the summits are isolated plateaus far above the forest floor.",sp=0},{t="Reaching the Heights",b="Scaling the vertical cliffs on foot is impossible, yet the summits are not entirely deserted. An intrepid night elf named Marli Wishrunner assists travelers seeking passage to the eastern peak. Those who ascend find a tranquil pond perched atop the stone mesa—though it is inhabited by an unusually large makrura named Diamond Head. To aid adventurers in returning to earth, Kalin Windflight offers sturdy parachutes to descend back into the jungle canopy below.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Twin Colossals located?",a="The Twin Colossals stand in northwestern Feralas, framing the main road that heads north into Desolace. The surrounding subzone extends westward toward the Forgotten Coast.",al={"twin colossals location","where are twin colossals","twin colossi map"}},{q="How do you reach the top of the Twin Colossals?",a="The sheer stone cliffs cannot be climbed normally. Travelers rely on the night elf Marli Wishrunner, who provides magical passage up to the eastern peak.",al={"how to climb twin colossals","get to top of twin colossi","to the top quest"}},{q="Who lives on the eastern summit?",a="At the top of the eastern peak, you will find Kalin Windflight, who sells parachutes for a safe descent, along with a deep pond inhabited by a massive makrura known as Diamond Head.",al={"npc at top of twin colossals","who is on the mesa","diamond head feralas"}},{q="How do you get down safely from the top?",a="Kalin Windflight sells specialized Colossal Parachutes atop the eastern summit, allowing travelers to leap from the cliffs and glide harmlessly down into the Feralas jungle.",al={"leaving twin colossals","jump off twin colossals","colossal parachute"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The sheer heights and nearby corrupted moonwells of the subzone serve as a stark reminder of the ancient history of Feralas and the lingering shadows creeping into the wilderness."},kw={"desolace","diamond head","feralas","kalin windflight","makrura","marli wishrunner","twin colossals","twin colossi"},rel={"zone:feralas","zone:desolace","subzone:forgotten-coast","subzone:rage-scar-hold","topic:night-elf","topic:satyr","topic:emerald-dream"},src={"Twin Colossals"}}
E["subzone:warpwood-quarter"] = {t="subzone",n="Warpwood Quarter",z="feralas",s="The Warpwood Quarter encompasses the eastern district of the ruined Highborne city of Eldre'Thalas, now known as Dire Maul. Once a center of elven nature cultivation and lush gardens, it has devolved into a warped, demon-tainted ruin overrun by frenzied flora and corrupted satyrs.",h="The Warpwood Quarter encompasses the eastern district of the ruined Highborne city of Eldre'Thalas, now known...",sec={{t="A Garden Corrupted",b="Formerly known for its grand botanical marvels, the Warpwood Quarter has become a choking forest of twisted ancients and lethal lashers. The district fell under the sway of Alzzin the Wildshaper, a satyr who bent his dark magic toward defiling the ancient Fruit of Fertility. Under his malign influence, the plant life grew grotesque and predatory, saturating the halls with vile Felvine shards and drawing demons, rebellious imps, and demonic thralls into the ruined halls.",sp=0},{t="Pathways through the Overgrowth",b="While explorers typically enter the district through the central Broken Commons of Dire Maul, an overgrown subterranean backdoor lies hidden beneath the Lariss Pavilion to the east. Navigating the district requires contending not only with Alzzin's warped guardians, but also with elusive denizens such as the mischievous imp Pusillin, whose thievery leads pursuers on dangerous chases toward the secluded reaches of the ruins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Warpwood Quarter?",a="The Warpwood Quarter is the eastern wing of Dire Maul, the ancient Highborne city of Eldre'Thalas. Originally built around grand conservatories, it has been overgrown and mutated by demonic energies.",al={"what is warpwood quarter","warpwood district","dire maul east lore"}},{q="Who rules this district?",a="The satyr Alzzin the Wildshaper holds dominion over the quarter. He has harnessed fell energies to corrupt the local vegetation and the legendary Fruit of Fertility, turning the district's plant guardians into vicious warped ancients.",al={"who controls warpwood","alzzin the wildshaper","warpwood boss"}},{q="How do you enter the Warpwood Quarter?",a="The main entrance is located off the Broken Commons inside Dire Maul. A second, secluded rear entrance tunnels out underneath the Lariss Pavilion in eastern Feralas, which requires a Crescent Key to unlock.",al={"warpwood entrance","how to get to dire maul east","lariss pavilion entrance"}},{q="Why is the imp Pusillin running through the ruins?",a="Pusillin is a thieving imp who lurks near the entrance of the quarter. When confronted by trespassers, he taunts them and flees deeper through the ruins, mocking adventurers all the way toward the Hidden Reach.",al={"pusillin","who is pusillin","imp running dire maul"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The twisted fate of the Warpwood ancients and the corruption of the Fruit of Fertility into foul Felvine are a tragic affront to Cenarion teachings, prompting druids from Moonglade to seek the cleansing of the quarter.",["race:NightElf"]="Seeing the majestic conservatories of Eldre'Thalas perverted into a satyr den serves as a grim reminder of the corruption that brought low the ancient Highborne Empire."},kw={"alzzin the wildshaper","dire maul east","eldre'thalas","felvine","fruit of fertility","lariss pavilion","pusillin","warpwood quarter"},rel={"subzone:dire-maul","zone:feralas","subzone:commons","subzone:lariss-pavilion","subzone:capital-gardens","topic:satyr","quest:5921"},src={"Warpwood Quarter"}}
E["subzone:woodpaw-den"] = {t="subzone",n="Woodpaw Den",z="feralas",s="Woodpaw Den is a rugged gnoll stronghold nestled in southern Feralas, just north of the ancient Darkmist Ruins. The settlement serves as a major gathering point for the Woodpaw gnolls and their fiercest pack alphas, making it a dangerous pocket of wilderness within the dense canopy.",h="Woodpaw Den is a rugged gnoll stronghold nestled in southern Feralas, just north of the ancient Darkmist...",sec={{t="Heart of the Pack",b="Situated amidst the towering boughs of Feralas, Woodpaw Den stands as the fortified heartland of the local Woodpaw gnolls. Unlike smaller scout camps scattered along the jungle tracks, this encampment is heavily guarded by the pack's seasoned Alphas. The gnolls here defend their territory fiercely against both intruding adventurers and the encroaching wilderness. Located just north of the elven remnants at Darkmist Ruins, the den represents an ever-present predatory threat to travelers attempting to traverse the central wilderness of the region.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Woodpaw Den?",a="Woodpaw Den is a prominent settlement and encampment of the Woodpaw gnolls in southern Feralas, situated just north of the Darkmist Ruins. It is heavily inhabited by the pack's dangerous Alphas.",al={"woodpaw den feralas","gnoll camp feralas","where is woodpaw den"}},{q="What creatures live here?",a="The den is populated primarily by the Woodpaw clan of gnolls, particularly the formidable Woodpaw Alphas who lead and protect the pack from outsiders.",al={"who lives here","woodpaw den mobs","what enemies are in woodpaw den"}},{q="What landmarks are nearby?",a="Immediately to the south lie the ancient Night Elven ruins known as Darkmist Ruins. The encampment itself is bordered by the dense rainforests characteristic of central Feralas.",al={"landmarks near woodpaw den","what is next to woodpaw den"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei based out of Feathermoon Stronghold, the feral expansion of gnoll packs near ancient ancestral sites like Darkmist Ruins is a constant nuisance requiring watchful containment.",["race:Tauren"]="Camp Mojache huntsmen view the vicious Woodpaw clan as dangerous competitors for game and territory within the primeval woods of Feralas."},kw={"darkmist ruins","feralas","gnoll","woodpaw","woodpaw alpha","woodpaw den"},rel={"topic:gnoll","zone:feralas"},src={"Woodpaw Den"}}
E["subzone:woodpaw-hills"] = {t="subzone",n="Woodpaw Hills",z="feralas",s="The Woodpaw Hills are a rugged, forested stretch of southeastern Feralas claimed by the Woodpaw gnolls. Once a dominant tribal territory, the hills have become an embattled frontline as insectoid terrors tunnel up from below and ancient stone giants stalk the canopy.",h="The Woodpaw Hills are a rugged, forested stretch of southeastern Feralas claimed by the Woodpaw gnolls.",sec={{t="A Beleaguered Stronghold",b="The dense forests of the Woodpaw Hills serve as the historical territory of the Woodpaw gnoll clan. While the hyena-folk once roamed unchallenged across these slopes, their dominance has crumbled under pressure from multiple fronts. To their southeast, nightmarish silithid swarmers have breached the earth at the Writhing Deep, forcing the gnolls back and compelling their chieftains to retreat deeper into the Woodpaw Den. Adding to the peril, ancient mountain giants—relics summoned down during the Third War to repel the Burning Legion—now wander the hillside woods, crushing any travelers or Horde interlopers who stray into their path.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in the Woodpaw Hills?",a="The hills are primarily occupied by the Woodpaw clan of gnolls, who maintain defensive camps throughout the woods. Ancient mountain giants also patrol the slopes, while invasive silithid insects push in from the southeastern borders.",al={"who inhabits woodpaw hills","woodpaw hills enemies","gnolls in feralas"}},{q="Why are mountain giants walking around this forest?",a="The mountain giants originally descended from the peaks to assist the night elves during the Third War when the Burning Legion invaded Kalimdor. Though the demonic invasion was broken, these hulking wardens remain in the woods, fiercely guarding the wild lands against intrusion.",al={"giants in woodpaw hills","why are there giants here","mountain giant lore feralas"}},{q="What is threatening the gnolls here?",a="The Woodpaw clan is being displaced by a sudden eruption of insectoid silithid carving out hives at the Writhing Deep. The encroaching swarms have driven the gnolls out of several camps, forcing their strongest alphas to fortify their position inside the Woodpaw Den.",al={"what are the gnolls fighting","woodpaw troubles","bugs attacking gnolls feralas"}},{q="Where are the Woodpaw clan leaders?",a="Due to the encroaching silithid swarms across the hills, the tribal leadership has abandoned the open camps. The Woodpaw Alphas have retreated into the sheltered underground caves of the Woodpaw Den.",al={"woodpaw alphas location","gnoll bosses feralas","find woodpaw leader"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Unlike the neutral cliff giants dwelling near the western coast, the mountain giants patrolling the Woodpaw Hills harbor intense hostility toward Horde members who venture inland."},kw={"feralas","gnolls","mountain giants","woodpaw","woodpaw den","woodpaw hills","writhing deep"},rel={"zone:feralas","subzone:woodpaw-den","subzone:writhing-deep","topic:gnoll","topic:burning-legion","topic:horde"},src={"Woodpaw Hills"}}
E["subzone:writhing-deep"] = {t="subzone",n="Writhing Deep",z="feralas",s="The Writhing Deep is a massive, insectoid hive complex carved into southeastern Feralas. Inhabited by the Zukk'ash silithid, this subterranean burrow is a growing danger that threatens nearby wildlife and surrounding encampments alike. The relentless expansion of these subterranean predators has upset the regional balance of the lush forest.",h="The Writhing Deep is a massive, insectoid hive complex carved into southeastern Feralas.",sec={{t="The Zukk'ash Swarm",b="Tucked away in the humid lowlands of southeastern Feralas, the Writhing Deep serves as the primary colony for the Zukk'ash silithid. Unlike the typical woodland beasts of the valley, these chittering insects dig labyrinthine tunnels and fiercely guard clutches of resinous eggs. The hive's aggressive encroachment into the nearby territories has destabilized the wild fauna and agitated local gnoll packs, pushing displaced and frenzied predators uncomfortably close to both Horde paths and native sanctuaries.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures inhabit the Writhing Deep?",a="The chasm is infested by the Zukk'ash silithid, an aggressive breed of giant insects comprising workers, tunnelers, stingers, and wasps led by dangerous brood champions such as Stinglasher and Qirot.",al={"writhing deep mobs","what lives in writhing deep","silithid in feralas"}},{q="Why is the Writhing Deep a threat to Camp Mojache?",a="As the Zukk'ash swarm expands outwards, it pushes into surrounding gnoll hunting grounds. The frantic gnolls are driven northward directly toward Camp Mojache, creating an escalating security crisis for the Horde outpost.",al={"camp mojache writhing deep","why attack horde","gnolls feralas"}},{q="Where is the Writhing Deep located?",a="The Writhing Deep is located in the southeastern region of Feralas, south of the main road and east of the towering forested hills.",al={"writhing deep location","where is writhing deep","feralas hive location"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The silithid expansion out of the Writhing Deep directly threatens Camp Mojache by driving crazed gnolls and roaming insect scouts straight into your supply lines."},kw={"camp mojache","feralas","hive","qirot","silithid","stinglasher","writhing deep","zukk'ash"},rel={"zone:feralas","subzone:camp-mojache","topic:gnoll","topic:horde"},src={"Writhing Deep"}}
E["zone:feralas"] = {t="zone",n="Feralas",z="feralas",s="Feralas is a vast, mist-shrouded rainforest nestled between Desolace, Thousand Needles, and the Veiled Sea. Sheltered by soaring mountain walls, it preserves an ancient ecosystem dotted with overgrown Kaldorei ruins and primordial beasts. Today, the wilderness is contested territory, caught between ancient Highborne remnants, invasive Gordunni ogres, and rival outposts established by the Alliance and the Horde.",h="Feralas is a vast, mist-shrouded rainforest nestled between Desolace, Thousand Needles, and the Veiled Sea.",sec={{t="A Forest Untouched by the Wastes",b="While neighboring Desolace and Thousand Needles have dried into barren badlands and desiccated canyons, Feralas remains intensely verdant. Mountain ranges seal off the canopy, sustaining a warm microclimate of deep mists, ancient trees, and towering waterfalls. Before the Great Sundering, much of Kalimdor looked like this. Over millennia, the deep jungle swallowed the monuments of the Kaldorei civilization that once ruled here, hiding forgotten temples and pavilions beneath strangling moss and thick fern brush.",sp=0},{t="The Ruins of Eldre'Thalas",b="Dominating central Feralas is the ruined metropolis of Eldre'Thalas, now called Dire Maul. Built at the peak of the Kaldorei empire, its vast stone courtyards have fallen into ruin, desecrated by the savage Gordunni ogre clan. These ogres spread across the valley, pillaging sacred sites, defiling pristine groves, and driving indigenous wildlife into territorial frenzy. Deep within Dire Maul's sealed chambers, whispers persist of Highborne remnants and trapped powers dating back ten thousand years.",sp=0},{t="The Struggle for Footholds",b="Both the Alliance and the Horde have mounted major expeditions into the jungle, though traversing it remains dangerous. From Feathermoon Stronghold on Sardor Isle, General Shandris Feathermoon directs Sentinels against both ogre expansion and encroaching naga. To the east lies Camp Mojache, a central Horde garrison struggling against aggressive Woodpaw gnolls, hostile Grimtotem tauren, and the relentless ogre clans. Neither faction commands true control over the untamable interior.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Dire Maul?",a="Dire Maul is the present-day name for Eldre'Thalas, a glorious elven city that survived the Sundering. Over the millennia, it fell into decline and was overrun by the brutal Gordunni clan. The complex is now partitioned into contested wings harboring ogres, treacherous spirits, and ancient Highborne secrets.",al={"eldre'thalas","ogre city","ancient ruins center"}},{q="How do Alliance travelers safely reach Feathermoon Stronghold?",a="Alliance explorers coming from Desolace can pass south through the Twin Colossals, though the beasts there are perilous. Alternatively, travelers can slip into the ocean along the Sar'theris Strand in Desolace and swim south along the Forgotten Coast directly to Sardor Isle, entirely bypassing the dangerous overland road and Camp Mojache.",al={"getting to feathermoon","alliance entrance to feralas","how to get to feralas alliance"}},{q="Why is the Horde fighting the Gordunni ogres so aggressively?",a="The Gordunni ogres are violently expanding out of Dire Maul, raiding supply caravans and attacking travelers across the jungle. Their destructive war parties actively threaten Camp Mojache, prompting Horde leaders like Belgrom Rockmaul to call for swift, aggressive strikes against the clan's outposts.",al={"why kill gordunni","horde ogre war","camp mojache ogres"}},{q="What is the Dream Bough?",a="The Dream Bough is one of the four Great Trees of Azeroth, housing a mystical natural portal that connects physical reality to the Emerald Dream. Like its counterparts in Ashenvale, Duskwood, and the Hinterlands, it is watched by the green dragonflight and ancient guardians.",al={"green dragon portal","great tree feralas","emerald dream tree"}},{q="Why are Grimtotem tauren present in Feralas?",a="A renegade sect of Grimtotem tauren maintains a compound in the wilderness, operating outside the authority of Thunder Bluff. Their presence is hostile toward both the Alliance and the Horde; they have trapped local faerie dragons and are actively targeted by Horde scouts.",al={"grimtotem feralas","grimtotem compound","hostile tauren"}},{q="Are there Silithid in Feralas?",a="Yes. South of the main road lies The Writhing Deep, a swarming subterranean hive of silithid insectoids. Their emergence in the lush rainforest is an unsettling sign that the hive mind is expanding far beyond the desert borders of southern Kalimdor.",al={"writhing deep","bugs in feralas","silithid hive"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Feralas holds profound cultural weight as a cradle of ancient Kaldorei civilization, yet the sight of sacred ruins like Eldre'Thalas defiled by ogres stirs deep sorrow and anger.",["faction:Alliance"]="Operations are anchored out of Feathermoon Stronghold under Shandris Feathermoon, tasking operatives with policing coastal naga and defending elven legacy.",["faction:Horde"]="Camp Mojache serves as a vital frontier bastion, requiring reliable warriors to push back aggressive Gordunni incursions, rogue Grimtotem, and Woodpaw gnolls.",["class:Druid"]="The Dream Bough and its connection to the Emerald Dream make Feralas sacred ground, demanding vigilance against encroaching corruption and defilers.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The damp, shaded floor of the canopy yields prized temperate and tropical flora, including Sungrass, Purple Lotus, and Khadgar's Whisker."},kw={"camp mojache","dire maul","dream bough","eldre'thalas","feathermoon","feralas","gordunni","shandris","thalanaar"},rel={"subzone:dire-maul","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","subzone:camp-mojache","subzone:thalanaar","subzone:dream-bough","subzone:forgotten-coast","subzone:twin-colossals","zone:thousandneedles"},src={"Feralas (Classic)","Feralas"}}
